{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks","id":34492,"title":"1001 Vampire Story Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-21T10:07:46-08:00","id":34492,"title":"1001 Vampire Story Hooks","content":"1) A recent assassination attempt on the prince orchestrated by the Belial's Brood has succeeded. What this means is that the city currently doesn't have anything resembling a government for vampires.<br /> <br /> The PCs are free to do anything they want without fear of reprisal - break the Masquerade, kill anyone they want, Embrace anyone they want.<br /> <br /> Of course, the same applies to the few other vampires who're still left.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T10:51:33-08:00","id":34503,"title":"","content":"2) A local member of the Ordo Dracul claims a breakthrough in his research. His claim is that he explain and reverse the Curse scientifically. The Circle and the Sanctum both oppose this &quot;Breakthrough&quot; as it undermines their own beliefs in the vampiric race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T10:55:08-08:00","id":34504,"title":"","content":"3) The Ordo Dracul has found a mortal (Timoteuz Hale male, 26, unemployed) who's entirely immune to Disciplines, the Vinculum and Blood Addiction. There's no explanation - the powers of the Blood simply don't work on him.<br /> <br /> Timmy is currently living an ordinary, unremarkable life - this will change very soon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T10:56:23-08:00","id":34507,"title":"","content":"4) They dug too deep, the Kine of the city speak of seeing owls at night, many more than ever before. Nobody remembers really seeing them flying into town, nobody can recall such a migration... but the Oil Rigs in the distance light up the sky as they burn off the pressurized gas before pumping begins.<br /> <br /> What have they done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 12-21-2013, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T10:58:04-08:00","id":34511,"title":"","content":"5) One of the PC's mortal relatives has been ghouled by a rival. The rival doesn't know about her ghoul's relations to the PC, yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T11:08:54-08:00","id":34515,"title":"","content":"6) The blood of the city's Kindred has begun to thicken uncontrollably. Elders quickly find themselves turning into veritable gods of blood and even neonates and ancillae are soon unable to feed from mortals. What is causing this strange event and how can it be stopped before Kindred society as we know it breaks down. Should it even be stopped?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T11:15:15-08:00","id":34517,"title":"","content":"VII ) Kindred reading the city's evening newspaper less than delighted to see the front page headline &quot;BLOODLESS BODY FOUND IN CITY CENTRE&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T11:19:28-08:00","id":34518,"title":"","content":"8) A Ven socialite using the Blush of Life to hold down food for appearance's sake at a new posh restaurant finds that the wine there replenishes Vitae. When she goes to investigate, she finds that the staff there are strangely immune to vampiric mind influence. Time for another approach to get to the bottom of this, and find out how to capitalize on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T11:23:45-08:00","id":34521,"title":"","content":"9) Vampires have been going missing downtown. An investigator tasked by the city's night council has identified a common factor: each vampire had fed at a club known in underground circles for proliferating a new street drug. Who's distributing it, and do they know what they have? What is it they really have, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T11:31:11-08:00","id":34525,"title":"","content":"10) Autumn brings the early dark, and local Kindred have become aware of an Orphanage where children play a game called &quot;Prince of the Playground&quot; at dusk. They wear piecemeal costumes of castaway adult garments. They form cliques, politicking for control of the slide, the merry-go-round, the swings, the sandbox. They use words like &quot;Venture,&quot; &quot;Gangrel,&quot; and &quot;the Masquerade.&quot; Several children hold one down, tickling him. Howling with laughter, he shrieks, &quot;Better stop that, or the Beast will get you!&quot; Where did they learn to act like this? Who taught them? It's eerie how their movements mimic the Danse Macabre...like a miniature mummers play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#990000\">Joshua Alan Doetsch</span></b><br /> <b>Freelance Writer<br /> <a href=\"http://joshuadoetsch.com/\" target=\"_blank\">joshuadoetsch.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1054-scrivnomancer","name":"scrivnomancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1054_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T11:47:55-08:00","id":34530,"title":"","content":"11) The Prince went missing. All of his known political enemies deny any responsibility or knowledge of what happened. After fruitless investigation the city holds an election to find a successor. The winner turns out to be an unknown Kindred that only recently arrived in the Domain. The newcomer is quickly accused of election fraud or being responsible for the Prince's absence, but these are quickly squashed by use of Auspex, the newcomer being very co-operative in the investigation.<br /> <br /> After officially taking over Praxis the new Prince announces he will do all he can to turn the Kindred society of the city into a well-oiled machine. Its gears grinding for the greatest benefit of all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T12:09:55-08:00","id":34553,"title":"","content":"12) Life as a kindred in the city is great. Crime is high, industry going strong, lots of people move in and out of town, and the police have about as much of a clue as a blind, deaf and mute Sherlock Holmes. And then something changes. Over night the city newspapers begin reporting, with precision, on the people the kindred have made vanish. Every single one, and only them. They're all called &quot;mysterious disappearances&quot;, and it only takes five days before they start calling it a conspiracy, and on the sixth open discussion begins in the city. &quot;How are we to find and punish whoever is responsible?&quot;<br /> The strange thing? Any attempts at stopping them from writing the stories, from dominating editors, charming reporters or even killing folks, fail to produce the intended result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T17:19:51-08:00","id":34674,"title":"","content":"13) A hot new band is making the rounds in the city, selling out shows all over town. You wouldn't think a group with a name like &quot;Amaranth&quot; would be such a hot ticket but tracks with titles like &quot;Beast's Kiss&quot; and &quot;Blood Doll&quot; seem to be real crowd pleasers. The local vampire population isn't too pleased though. Already one or two concerned Kindred have tried to investigate but haven't been heard from since. Who are these people? Why is their music full of Kindred jargon? And why does everyone say their lead singer is &quot;Mesmerising&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1591-freshman","name":"Freshman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T18:53:33-08:00","id":34709,"title":"","content":"14) A Nomad shows up at Court claiming to have inside knowledge from and unimpeachable, but unverifiable, source. She may be prophet of the Sanctified or the Circle delivering revelation from the devine, or maybe a deep cover agent of the Carthian movement who can't risk identifying a valuable source. The outsider claims that members of Belial's Brood have infiltrated the Prince's government and are preparing to instigate mass chaos in the domain. What the local Kindred don't know is that the outsider is a professional agitator who pulls this same scheme in countless domains across the world to allow marginalized Covenants to attack the establishment with near impunity. What the outsider doesn't know is that this time, it's true. And with the domain alerted to their plot, the Brood just escalated their time table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1591-freshman","name":"Freshman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T00:11:10-08:00","id":34834,"title":"","content":"15) The M is coming. The prince and most of the Elders are already Afflicted with Malkavia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T06:53:15-08:00","id":34929,"title":"","content":"16) Hunters have been alerted to an entire society of blood sucking fiends pulling the strings of the region by a trail of bread crumbs starting with the murder of one of their own. Now they are looking for and attacking any trace of vampirism that they can find, and they are very good at finding it.<br /> <br /> Now you have to deal with it. Only problem is, the murderer is the progeny of someone in your coterie..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T12:33:07-08:00","id":35075,"title":"","content":"17) The covenants in the city are at open war with each other. The PCs have been Embraced as expendable shock troops. The objective is to survive, at any costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T16:27:09-08:00","id":35187,"title":"","content":"18) Kindred are ending up missing all over town, even the older, more powerful ones. The Sanctified Mekhet receive horrifying visions of fire and fury and fall into fear frenzy when they attempt to investigate. One survivor of an attack claims &quot;it was an angel of the Lord, his wings of fire and halo of sunlight!&quot;, but the very next night he is missing too. There are rumors of Sanctified attacks, Cruac rituals or even the VII attacking, but the truth is-nobody actually knows what is going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1566-orabilis","name":"Orabilis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T13:22:04-08:00","id":35766,"title":"","content":"19) The Prince of 5 or so years has become a ruthless tyrant who rules by blood hunting anyone who defies her will, and has the covenants reluctantly compliant by sheer power and force. A group is planning to revolt and overthrow this haphazard government. As the characters get involved they learn something the rest of the city doesn't know. The Prince 5 years ago was a very different person... benevolent with virtuous ideals... Has their crazed ruler's humanity spiraled downward for some reason? Has a Strix possessed them? Will the group let the rest of the city dust the Prince and all of her followers because of a bigger threat that has been looming over the city?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","name":"Samare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1310_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T13:59:29-08:00","id":35794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=34507#post34507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) They dug too deep, the Kine of the city speak of seeing owls at night, many more than ever before. Nobody remembers really seeing them flying into town, nobody can recall such a migration... but the Oil Rigs in the distance light up the sky as they burn off the pressurized gas before pumping begins.<br /> <br /> What have they done.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> <i>&quot;In the Bridge of Khazad-d\u00fbm it appears, like a great shadow, in the middle of which was a dark form, of man-shape maybe, yet greater, it drew itself to a great height, and its wings spread from wall to wall, in what was a vast hall. </i></span></span><i>They could see the furnace-fire of its eyes from afar.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> 20) While feeding on its latest victim a young kindred finds a strange card with some clan symbols, numbers and its own face upon it. Later it finds out similar accidents happened with all its coterie-mates. One week later, in Elysium, the Prince can be seen playing with a deck of cards in his hands while adressing the court. As night goes by an unknown kindred bumps into one of the coterie members &quot;Read you cards right and work on your poker faces&quot; she hears, but the figure is not there when she turns. There's a deck of the strange cards in her pocket. Some speak of events, some of kindred secrets &amp; powers and others with the face of kindred, local and a few others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:59:23-08:00","id":36117,"title":"","content":"21) The Sanctified Bishop has stepped down from his position within the Church. He gives no reason other than he felt his faith waivering. He has moved to a new Haven and has not given up any secrets but he's left a huge hole in the city's power structure. After all, he is attending court and taking his seat at the primogen's table. Not to mention the Sanctified are pretty shaken up by the loss of their leader, all the ex-bishop's enemies are preparing to strike at him and opportunists are taking advantage any way they can.<br /> <br /> It's a frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T23:59:09-08:00","id":36203,"title":"","content":"22) The Sanctified Bishop has stepped down from his position within the Church. He gives no reason other than he felt his faith waivering.<br /> <br /> It is time to rekindle his faith and demonstrate to him why mortals need the Sanctified and why the mission of the Lancea et Sanctum - that of testing the faith of humans, corrupting them and punishing sinners (all mortals are sinners) - is a holy mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T14:07:53-08:00","id":36546,"title":"","content":"23) Three Princes rule the Domain for ages since the old Prince died. In the beginning, many warred for the title until these three established their uneasy truce, not one willing to give up the title of Prince or show weakness in front of the other two that couldlead to their downfall. The decades have passed in an uneasy, cold war between the three until now. In the last week, each Prince has been the victim of an Assassination attempt; a firebomb, a team of unusually well-informed hunters, and vessel whose blood was somehow made poisonous. Each blames the others and the cold war is about to heat up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1591-freshman","name":"Freshman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T20:13:39-08:00","id":36709,"title":"","content":"24) Players are sent an invite to a party, when they arrive it is apparent they are not suppose to be there, quietly they are moved to another room and told to wait there. (Leave them there to build tension) soon they will go to stick their heads out see whats going on, have the party gone, like almost everything is gone. Have them find something random, dead mortals (several), signs of ritual, dead vampires almost anything can by put here. And let the adventure begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T00:33:04-08:00","id":36809,"title":"","content":"25)Vampirekind has come to the stunning conclusion that faffing about killing Hobos for blood and fleeing the Police is goddamn bullshit, It's up to the PCs to produce a less irksome method of getting blood. Failure means a painful, lingering death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T23:26:23-08:00","id":37196,"title":"","content":"26) Because of a series of mistaken identities, a cabal of Vampires now believe you to be their sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T00:08:45-08:00","id":37208,"title":"","content":"27) One of the defiant was working on a new variation of certain scale, but it hasn't worked as intended. In theory, it could extend the duration of a ghouls supernatural state to forever, but it has instead caused the test subjects to act like Draugr instead. This side effect kicks in after about a month, and activates suddenly, like a vampire trying to fight off frenzy.<br /> <br /> Not much is known about them, but they don't appear to be vampires. The sun does not burn them nor does fire. They seem to targeting vampires exclusively now, with evidence suggesting that they tried feeding on animals and humans, but they might not have the means to produce their own vitae. That or vitae is their meal of choice (they were all addicts like any ghoul before the change).<br /> <br /> This Dragon wants this problem solved quickly and quietly, before this problem can be traced back him. He doesn't want the Prince or any of the other covenants coming after him for this mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","user":"DivineWrath","date":". 12-26-2013, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T00:24:23-08:00","id":37212,"title":"","content":"28) Alternatively, the city has become aware of a Draugr lose in the city. The kindred first learned about it from a video recording of it attacking some of the herd. What is frightening is that it doesn't appear to burn in sunlight (humanity 0 vampires suffer 5 aggravated wounds per interval). It was recorded as being out in the open around noon for over an hour. The only signs of discomfort it had was when it appeared to be not satisfied with the blood of its victims. Many of the kindred fear it has thick blood and that only vampire blood will feed this monster. In fact, a few kindred haven't been heard from in the last few days.<br /> <br /> A blood hunt has been put on this monster, and there is a reward for any information one can gather on this creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","user":"DivineWrath","date":". 12-26-2013, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T04:23:45-08:00","id":37786,"title":"","content":"29) A bunch of Strix possess the bodies of the PCs, and go around doing whatever it is they planned to do. It could be to torment the kindred, to have fun (the kind that monsters like), or do something more dark and sinister. This goes on for a few nights or even a few weeks, until the Strix leave.<br /> <br /> However, instead of the storyteller telling the players that they regain consciousness many nights or even weeks later without the darndest idea as to what had happened, the storyteller instead has the players play as the Strix during their little stroll in the bodies of the PCs. The players might even be warned that Strix possessing their characters is part of the plot before the first story begins. The storyteller might provide the goal of the Strix, what they need to know to complete that goal, and how to do it. Alternatively, the storyteller might allow the players to control more details, like the goals, the powers the Strix have, etc. The storyteller might even leave everything open ended and up to the players to decide what it is they do. Regardless, the storyteller encourages the players to use their PCs as though they were a cheap rental car and burn relationships. Be certain to inform the players that part of the plot involves the players trying to prove their innocence of any crimes the Strix commit in their bodies, and the work needed to put things back together. Hopefully the PCs aren't punished with final death, or something distracts the court before passing judgement on them.<br /> <br /> Remember though, there is a limit to how much is too much for the players. The Strix have no humanity and therefore some players might try to take things too far because they think that anything goes. It would be wise for the storyteller to talk with the players, asking how much horror done by inhuman monsters is acceptable, and when it goes too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T20:15:19-08:00","id":38143,"title":"","content":"30) the prince has been in torpor for the past 50 years. During this time, she has continued to rule by proxy through the Herald, her grandchilde who speaks for her by channeling her consciousness with Speaker for the Silent. It's truly uncanny the way the herald almost literally speaks with his grandsire's voice; her speech pattern, her cadences, her mannerisms... If you closed your eyes, you might even mistake him for the real prince, were it not for his voice being deeper and more masculine. But one night while he is addressing the court, who should walk into Elysium but the supposedly torpid prince herself. She says she awoke a few weeks ago, but was delayed in returning. Investigation under Auspex reveals she is not lying, and her kin verify she responds as the prince should to their Blood Sympathy. Her Vitae even tastes the same. She is surprised to learn that she has been speaking through her grandchilde, as she has no memory of projecting her consciousness onto him while she lay torpid. So then... Who has he been channeling all this time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T05:33:09-08:00","id":38255,"title":"","content":"31) The Prince's greatest rival starts gaining massive amounts of support, with the Prince's long-time allies and supporters starting to turn to the other side. At the same time, there are rumors of Solace being sold to Kindred, by persons unknown. Is it a coincidence? The Prince wants the characters to investigate and bring him the drug dealers' heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1566-orabilis","name":"Orabilis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T11:43:11-08:00","id":38356,"title":"","content":"32) A hunter breaks into the hotel where Elysium is being held with a bomb that could kill every Kindred there, and every mortal for that matter. She's just barely caught in time, but this leads to some very uncomfortable questions. How did she get in? Security is the tightest its ever been, and no less than the Sheriff himself, a Mekhet, was on duty with his considerable Auspex. The hunter will say nothing, and all mind control attempts only show that she planned this on her own.<br /> <br /> And what does this all have to do with the rotting remains of the Seneschal, dead in a bathroom upstairs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T02:04:01-08:00","id":40410,"title":"","content":"33) This city harbors too high a vampire population. The Kindred are too many.<br /> <br /> The prince, an Acolyte and a believer in violent solutions, declares the next three nights to be a free for all vampire killing fest. There is no Elysium, and there will be no legal repercussions for thinning the flock and destroying other vampires, as long as doing so doesn't endanger the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T02:05:42-08:00","id":40411,"title":"","content":"34) Someone (something?) is hunting vampires. The population of the Kindred reduces to a bare fraction almost overnight; with the PCs among the very few survivors.<br /> <br /> Whatever it is that's hunting them, it's still out there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T02:11:20-08:00","id":40413,"title":"","content":"35) An Elder vampire, unable to gain sustenance from the blood of mortals, wants the PCs to embrace mortal chattel for him to feed on. Refusal to comply might well result in the Elder feeding upon the PCs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T05:50:23-08:00","id":40473,"title":"","content":"36) There is a new drug hitting the muggle in your hunting grounds, thining their blood. Not enough to kill them or even make them that sick. But you need to consume twice as much to get half the Vitae you need. While there is still viable subject's for the your hunger, their number's are shrinking nightly. What's worse, the dealer's are...more prepared for you kind than normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T06:30:30-08:00","id":40485,"title":"","content":"37) No one seems to know for sure when it started but over the past few months younger kindred have been hearing faint whispers right after feeding. To begin with it seemed almost like it was the spirits of the victims, blaming them, but the more times it repeated the whispers moved steadily towards revealing secrets, offering advice, cajoling.<br /> And now it has come to a head. A carthian neonate managed to put the Whore of the city, an important member of the Circle, on fire using some to then unknown form of blood magic, only to be struck down by another neonate who grew cthulu-esque tentacles upon a moments notice.<br /> What the pebbles is going on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T11:50:55-08:00","id":40618,"title":"","content":"38) With much pomp and circumstance, several highly-placed Invictus reveal that they've built a proof-of-concept blood farm under the slaughterhouse district.<br /> ...without the approval of the Prince.<br /> <br /> Chaos erupts as the city's kindred choose sides between the Prince and his enemies, and between those who value expediency over Humanity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T01:58:56-08:00","id":42183,"title":"","content":"39) The Prince has made a few decisions that directly threaten his praxis and his regency - embracing childer that turn out to favor covenants other than his, giving political power to enemies, trusting the wrong people, destroying the wrong people, etc. Very soon, there will be a revolt.<br /> <br /> He'd never admit it, but he did so intentionally and fully aware of the consequences. His centuries long existence wearies him; and making things interesting again is the only option other than torpor or meeting the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T10:26:09-08:00","id":42347,"title":"","content":"40) Contact is lost with a ghoul family in a tiny, isolated southeastern mountain community. Upon investigation, the characters discover that the town's inhabitants are all gone, including the original Gangrel contact, and that a decade's worth of kudzu growth blankets the community. Several shaggy, elusive figures appear to be the only mamillian life remaining, and the only ones who might be able to give the characters a clue as to how a <i>square mile of vegetation</i> could become a single gigantic mandrake colony.<br /> <br /> So. Do you try to find the civilians lost in the scary woods, or do you shrug, cut your losses, and open a winery?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T22:48:46-08:00","id":42712,"title":"","content":"41) For whatever reason, a particular lick with a very high humanity has roused the ire of a hateful elder. Without said licks knowledge, this elder has made a game out of finding subtle, second-hand ways to gradually break them down by staging an elaborately-ruled, round-robin game of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BreakTheCutie\" target=\"_blank\">Break</a>/<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CorruptTheCutie\" target=\"_blank\">Corrupt the Cutie</a> and secretly offering other, equally jaded monsters prizes for participating.<br /> <br /> Do you warn them, making yourself a target by spoiling the fun? Do you leave yourself out of it so you don't have to watch the carnage? Or do you take the opportunity to make a little social currency by showing that self-righteous jerkstore what unlife is <i>really </i>all about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 01-05-2014, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T23:37:14-08:00","id":42733,"title":"","content":"42) A trained, ghouled animal follows you home. You suspect it's jonesing for a fix, and tracked you down by the scent of your vitae, but what could possibly have happened that would accidentally put a valuable resource like that out on the street? <br /> <br /> Do you keep it out of sympathy, or utility? Hope for a reward from some frantic owner? Or leave it shivering out in the cold, fearing that its master has planned all this in advance and is now coolly watching you from behind those sad puppy-dog eyes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T19:09:11-08:00","id":43280,"title":"","content":"When it was just the occasional street person disappearing in the sewers abutting the reservoir, nobody paid any attention. When <i>those </i>disappearances were entirely replaced with missing Nosferatu neonates, the kindred community started sitting up and taking notice. A lucky survivor reported glimpses of an enormous albino alligator dismembering and devouring an unfortunate perimeter guard, then awkwardly trying to lick up spilled viscera off the cement.<br /> <br /> Looks like <i>somebody </i>has a dependency problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 01-06-2014, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T23:48:06-08:00","id":43375,"title":"","content":"44) The Prince's party's over, and the PCs get to dispose of the corpses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T12:53:44-08:00","id":43672,"title":"","content":"45) The PCs find dirt on one of the Elders in town (evidence of diablerie, membership in a prohibited bloodline, heresy, a plot against the prince etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:00:33-08:00","id":43716,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">46) You wake up one night, and find the Prince and her Sheriff have been replaced completely, without any warning or acknowledgment.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">When you mention this to the Kindred outside your Coterie, they look at you as if you're mad. The current Prince, who is in no way like the one you remember, has reigned over this city for years, according to them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Who was brainwashed, you, or the others? Did any brainwashing even occur?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">47) A Ghoul or Neonate stumble upon a very strange sort of vampire. They're an undead human, they drink blood, and can't digest other food, like the Kindred... but they walk in the sun, and the darkness of night gives them horrible frostbites. They need to rest in a room bathed in artificial light. The light of a full moon alone can allow them to be somewhat active during the night. They don't mind fire, but the sight of ice can send them in a panic.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Interesting. Very interesting.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Every Covenant has a different idea of what to do with him, with, obviously, the Ordo Dracul offering a reward to anyone who brings the Daywalker well and alive, so they can... study this odd vampire. (Is it even a vampire?)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">And you, what do </span></span><i>you</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> do?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T15:25:08-08:00","id":43747,"title":"","content":"48) A young Daeva just got noticed by a big-deal music producer and is about to sign for a rap album recording and promotion. However, that would put him under a lot of Masquerade-endangering scrutiny. The Sheriff wants you to persuade him to give up on his dream of being the Undead Slim Shady...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1566-orabilis","user":"Orabilis","date":".  added a number, to keep track easier :) 01-07-2014, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1566-orabilis","name":"Orabilis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T00:41:17-08:00","id":44011,"title":"","content":"Ah geez guys. Things were working so well. 1 reply 1 story hook. Each story hook clearly label with a number.<br /> <br /> I suppose its not a big deal. Its not like we all agreed to it or were told to do it that way, it just happened that way. However, if I &quot;waste&quot; this post by talking about it, then we are back on track. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T00:42:15-08:00","id":44012,"title":"","content":"49) A kid was talking a picture of herself using her cell phone. However, an obfuscated vampire got caught in it. The girl has no idea who this creepy person is or how he got in the photo. She claims she was alone at the time the picture was taken. It has become something of a minor internet meme of sorts, so it can be found on various places on the internet. However, the local vampire court knows who the guy is and wants him found.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T03:47:27-08:00","id":44061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=44011#post44011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah geez guys. Things were working so well. 1 reply 1 story hook. Each story hook clearly label with a number.<br /> <br /> I suppose its not a big deal. Its not like we all agreed to it or were told to do it that way, it just happened that way. However, if I &quot;waste&quot; this post by talking about it, then we are back on track. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, where I'm from, we don't look kindly on intentional double posts, and I therefore avoid them, that's why, sorry for upsetting the order of things. :P<br /> <br /> 50) Remember that fairly high-ranking member of your Covenant, that disappeared a couple months ago, with everyone assuming they were either in Torpor or killed for real? And everybody took advantage of the power vacuum left behind?<br /> Well, you stumble upon them. And they're human, for all intents and purposes, and don't want anything to do with Kindred society anymore. They're planning to move far, far away from the city.They won't tell what happened. Not so easily. Your old friend still has the same strength of mind they had in unlife; you won't be able to read their mind or force them to talk just like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T05:30:22-08:00","id":44095,"title":"","content":"51) The Regent of the North Quarter is holding a competition:<br /> <br /> Competitors are to kill a mortal and then bring the mortal's obituary from the papers along with the proof of the murder. The best-written, most poetic or ironic obituary wins the competition. Prize-a piece of the Regent's territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1566-orabilis","user":"Orabilis","date":". 01-07-2014, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1566-orabilis","name":"Orabilis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T06:57:26-08:00","id":44138,"title":"","content":"52) As a response to recent killings and gang violence, concerned citizens are forming a militia for the purpose of defending the people.<br /> <br /> The Kindred can't accept a group of armed people with altruistic goals that operate right in their city. The PCs are to infiltrate and destroy, or, alternately, turn the militia into a tool of the Kindred. Seducing key members, addicting them to vitae, etc. The usual deal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T05:51:21-08:00","id":45528,"title":"","content":"53) The Prince is stone dead. He was planning a party, the guests of which are on their way right now, if they discover he's dead you will be suspected as the killer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T03:27:46-08:00","id":46158,"title":"","content":"54. She really looks beautiful, a pretty, fit young thing, all alone walking around the streets at night. And you do feel a bit peckish, so you could probably go for a bite...<br /> And you do.<br /> After your first or second sip of blood, she drops dead. Turns out, she was someone's ghoul, recently drained of blood and held together mostly through the power of vitae inside her. Now she's dead, and it's your fault. It'd be really awkward if her master was someone old and powerful...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T04:00:55-08:00","id":46826,"title":"","content":"55) You wake up. There's a bloodless corpse next to you. It's a highly priced retainer of your Pricus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T00:43:26-08:00","id":47286,"title":"","content":"56) A serial diablerist turns himself in. The Archbishop assign her to the PC's coterie; they are to rehabilitate her and turn her into a good law-abiding Damned who doesn't eat her peers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:42:32-08:00","id":47858,"title":"","content":"57) There's a new kindred in town, according to the Cacophony, but they're a little peculiar. Even after being in town for a while, no one has seen or directly heard from them, and their vocabulary continues to be stilted, awkward, and incomplete. The assumption is that it's a rather stupid, out of touch neonate (maybe one who fled from another city before being fully educated by their sire), or a shy, overenthusiastic cryptomemetic (kindred) hobbyist whose first language isn't English.<br /> <br /> The truth is that by sheer chance, an obsessive-compulsive mortal had stumbled over several of the simplest Cacophany memes, and with several years of intense investigation, has partially decoded the Cacophony <i>without discovering the existence of kindred</i>. The poor bastard realizes that what they're investigating might be something dangerous and occult, but has <i>no </i>idea how badly they've underestimated the risk. What a tragedy.<br /> <br /> If their efforts come to the attention of the elders, chances are that use of the Cacophony will be suspended, or possibly undergo major overhaul to make it less recognizable to anyone who might have had contact with the poor sap (or just the unsuspecting public in general). What a goddamn waste of time. Maybe it'd be better if someone just dug up the academic's notes, made sure they hadn't spread the word around to their social contacts, and then silenced them, rather than getting everybody flustered and dredging up the whole damn Cacophony.<br /> <br /> ...then again, killing a human like this would be <i>suuuuuch </i>a waste of a potentially amazing Mekhet ghoul...<br /> <br /> -credit to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1571-kamikazegerbil\">Kamikazegerbil</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1571-kamikazegerbil\">-</a></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 01-12-2014, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:30:43-08:00","id":48348,"title":"","content":"58) So. The last time your coterie mate left for the weekend, using dubious excuses, you followed him around Obfuscated. He hanged out with some friend. Who happen to be Belial's Brood. What are you going to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T03:35:06-08:00","id":48846,"title":"","content":"59) Finally, you've been able to witness a VII doing their horrible, despicable deed, without being seen.<br /> That VII is the Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T09:19:15-08:00","id":49030,"title":"","content":"60) One of the vampires lose the last dips of their humanity and becomes a draugr. However the prince (or another powerful party) needs him for something. It might be information. it might be a favor or life owed. It might be anything. <br /> The PCs are tasked with uplifting him from Draugrdom if it is at all possible. <br /> Perhaps the draugr's still living anchors can be used. Perhaps there's some other mystical way. And perhaps it's impossible at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T13:01:11-08:00","id":49231,"title":"","content":"61) Your ex-wife, who's also your Touchstone, is a junkie. Not a vitae-junkie, thankfully, but it's still heroin. She's killing herself. The Anvari bloodline - a very old family with a strong affinity for drugs - may be involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T13:02:56-08:00","id":49233,"title":"","content":"62) By simple chance, the PCs get lots and lots of very illegal drugs on their hands.<br /> <br /> The PCs need money. The Invictus doesn't want potential vampire pushers to break the Masquerade. And the owners want their drugs back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T13:04:42-08:00","id":49235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=49231#post49231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">61) Your ex-wife, who's also your Touchstone, is a junkie. Not a vitae-junkie, thankfully, but it's still heroin. She's killing herself. The Anvari bloodline - a very old family with a strong affinity for drugs - may be involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>When using this type of idea in the game, it's important to highlight the parallels between the life of a junkie and the unlife of a vampire. All vampires are junkies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T00:21:24-08:00","id":57957,"title":"","content":"63) A veritable army of policemen is on the way to where the PCs are right now. They need to get out of the way - without endangering the Masquerade, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T03:52:35-08:00","id":58615,"title":"","content":"STOP SCREWING UP THE NUMBERING, FOR THE LOVE OF BLOOD!<br /> <br /> 64) Things are going great. You're a Invictus vampire in good standing, unliving in a relatively small city ruled over by Invictus and populated by mostly Invictus. There's a few Dragons here as well, but they mostly keep to themselves. The small Carthian population is both weak and docile. It has been decades since any of the other covenants were here.<br /> One night, you're minding your business, feeding on some rich skank you chatted up at the opera house, and you suddenly feel something strange in your gut. Your beast stirs, growls, and you feel threatened. You look around, but there is noone else present. It becomes clear to you that you are a target of a blood sorcery ritual...<br /> <br /> 65) You wake up in the square. At noon. The sun is high above, shining brightly, but it does not burn. What the hell is going on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T22:31:28-08:00","id":61325,"title":"","content":"66) Once a year, every vampire in the city must provide the Regent with a living, breathing mortal. It's called the Blood Tax, and for the PCs, it's due next night.<br /> <br /> 67) There's a blood hunt for an Elder going on, and wouldn't you like to join? The Sheriff insists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T22:52:35-08:00","id":61332,"title":"","content":"And the numbering is gone again. Anyways, please guys, 1 post - 1 plot hook so that the number of plot hooks is equal to posts. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T03:08:50-08:00","id":61428,"title":"","content":"Hi. I started this thread. I believe I get to set the rules about numbering.<br /> <br /> There are no rules.<br /> <br /> Done!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T06:57:43-08:00","id":61515,"title":"","content":"z) The Testament of Longinus falls into mortal hands and ... gains some measure of popularity and media attention, primarily among counterculture circles. Most people treat it as a hoax or as a clever mockery of the New Testament. Some see it in a different light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T04:35:48-08:00","id":62079,"title":"","content":"z? As in a plot hook numbered z) instead of 68)?<br /> <br /> Please don't be like that. Each of these story hooks deserve a number. You don't have to get all defiant just because a number of people visiting and posting on this thread liked some sense of order. We can all tone things down so nothing gets out hand (at least I hope).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T05:40:11-08:00","id":62097,"title":"","content":"(No offense, but I'm not really interested in any sort of meta discussion in this thread. The reason I started this thread is because I like writing story hooks and I like reading story hooks posted by other people. That's all. Other people are free to assign numbers to story hooks they post. The numbers are not the point, what comes after them is.)<br /> <br /> .) Your worst enemy knocks on your door. He needs a safe haven and protection from the sun.<br /> <br /> This is a Carthian domain, and there are rules in place that mandate helping each other in times of need. You are bound by law to allow him entry in your haven.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T07:16:20-08:00","id":62146,"title":"","content":"Yes, however if they are numbered it's a lot easier to discuss them with fellow storytellers. In private for example:<br /> &quot;Hey, have you seen that awesome story hook posted by Christian A?&quot;<br /> &quot;Which one?&quot;<br /> &quot;Number 69&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead of<br /> &quot;number.. ah, that one has no number&quot;<br /> <br /> P.S. If you, as a creator, would just now number them, instead of going against numbering &quot;on principle&quot; we wouldn't have to discuss this... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T04:42:31-08:00","id":62841,"title":"","content":".) Random complications affecting vampire PCs/NPCs:<br /> <br /> .) Humanity way too low, and it shows<br /> .) Mortal hunters chasing you<br /> .) Diablerist<br /> .) crippling addiction to Vitae<br /> .) Congratulations! There's a blood hunt on your head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T04:44:25-08:00","id":62842,"title":"","content":"Random complications affecting vampire PCs/NPCs:<br /> <br /> .) Secret member of a dangerous, reviled bloodline (Morbus, Nocktuku, that kind of thing)<br /> .) Lies about covenant affiliation<br /> .) secretly a member of the Brood<br /> .) secretly a member of VII<br /> .) hears the Call of the Brood, will likely join up soon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T04:46:25-08:00","id":62844,"title":"","content":"Random complications affecting vampire PCs/NPCs:<br /> <br /> .) Afflicted with the M<br /> .) frequent Masquerade breaker<br /> .) blood bound to someone really dangerous who has not the character's best interest in mind<br /> .) Strix really like you<br /> .) character is actually a millenium or two older than he appears","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 02-01-2014, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T04:49:34-08:00","id":62847,"title":"","content":"Random complications affecting vampire PCs/NPCs:<br /> <br /> .) Feeds on dangerous prey that's difficult to hunt<br /> .) Has high risk thralls that cause more damage than good<br /> .) bad day, only seconds away from anger frenzy<br /> .) feeding gone wrong happened just now<br /> .) sun's up in half an hour, and your haven is far, far away from here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T04:52:32-08:00","id":62850,"title":"","content":".) Covenant x really hates you and would appreciate it if you stopped existing, like, right now.<br /> .) VII assassins are out there, hunting for you.<br /> .) last person you fed on had some really weird drugs in his system, and now you're starting to feel the effects<br /> .) There's a bloodless corpse in front you, which you have to dispose of, and you have only a couple minutes to do so.<br /> .) Your blood has been cursed, possibly by a rival in one of the mystic covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T07:26:56-08:00","id":62899,"title":"","content":"Not only you ignored my post, which I believe holds a logical reason to number them properly, but you also started spamming the thread with almost useless posts, since these include only the very basic plot hooks, which are known to everybody. <br /> <br /> Please don't mess the nice thing you started yourself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cheers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T13:33:46-08:00","id":63085,"title":"","content":".) When you wake up, the angel Amoniel greets you. He says it's time for him to give away the true secrets of Theban Sorcery - but only to those who are worthy. It's time for a demonstration - Amoniel needs to know you've internalized the teachings of the Sanctified - only true monsters deserve to know the greatest of rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T15:17:39-08:00","id":63147,"title":"","content":"If he is going to be difficult, perhaps we should ignore this thread and let it die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T15:21:44-08:00","id":63149,"title":"","content":"That's not a bad idea. I'm sure one of us could come up with an entirely new, ordered thread for this sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T15:43:34-08:00","id":63157,"title":"","content":".) Your younger sibling has learned of vampires, and that you have become one. Sibling tracks you down and demands to be made a vampire also. The Prince forbids any within his territory to Embrace members of their own family. Sibling threatens to approach some other vampire if you will not do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T15:50:52-08:00","id":63162,"title":"","content":".) The dominate discipline stops working. The Ven are undergoing a crisis of epic proportions as their most important power ceases to have any effect at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T00:14:55-08:00","id":63327,"title":"","content":"Yeah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm sorry, such a wonderful thread had to be ruined by someone's principle. sad really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T00:30:54-08:00","id":63333,"title":"","content":"(If you have only white noise to contribute and no story hooks, I suggest you follow DivineWrath's advice and stay out and &quot;let this thread die&quot;. Not that this'll actually happen, because I'm not planning to stop posting anytime soon, but I'd appreciate it if the story hooks to white noise ratio would change for the better. This thread is not for bickering about numbers. It's for posting story hooks. This will be my last comment on the issue. I have more interesting things to post, and I think so do you people; and I'll ask the moderators to delete unnecessary posts in this thread if things get out of hand.)<br /> <br /> <br /> .) The Strix show up with an ultimatum. They'll not cause a natural catastrophe that will end up destroying the entire city if its vampiric population finally decides to embrace its monstrosity and work on decreasing everyone's humanity rating quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 02-02-2014, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T03:17:45-08:00","id":63361,"title":"","content":"Due to some... heated talk... in another thread, I felt it was prudent to create a new thread to provide an outlet so that &quot;creative differences&quot; do not lead to the mods getting involved and possibly making every one's day bad. I would like it everyone involved let the issue go. If anyone wants a fight, they may remain in the old thread. If people want to move ahead and go about creating a new thread for story hooks, you're welcome to come here and join the discussion. I recommend we take a few days to let heads cool off before we open a new thread to list story hooks. Until then, we can discuss ground rules, since many of us wanted things like the story hooks to be numbered and that each story hook number should match the reply number.<br /> <br /> Once the ground rules are set and heads are cooled off, we can move ahead. I'm thinking that when that happens we could re-purpose this thread for open discussion of the story hooks or something (or maybe it would be best to create a new thread for that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T03:29:11-08:00","id":63365,"title":"","content":"*WHISTLES LOUDLY*<br /> <br /> @ everyone except Christian A<br /> <br /> Lets move to a new thread where we can work on story hooks and stuff without the attitude. I've already made a new thread where we can cool off and get started once we lay down some ground rules.<br /> <br /> Move here please:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/63361-the-new-1001-vampire-story-hooks-thread-open-discussion\">The new 1001 Vampire story hooks thread</a><br /> <br /> @ Christian A<br /> <br /> You are welcome to stay here and *not* join us. If you do decide to follow, please leave any attitude and inclinations towards being &quot;difficult&quot; at the door. If it is not obvious, I being quite stern on this matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T03:50:12-08:00","id":63372,"title":"","content":"1. One hook per post. One post per hook. <br /> 2. Abstain from listing the things that need not be listed, such as &quot;you are hungry&quot; or &quot;someone died&quot;.<br /> 3. Rename it to the Story Hook Compendium or something similar?<br /> 4. Don't be a dick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T04:16:29-08:00","id":63377,"title":"","content":".) A ghoul with sensitive information decides it's time to escape the city to a place where there aren't any vampires and assorted madness (ha!). The Primogen council needs him to be tracked down. The PCs are under order not to talk to the ghoul under any circumstance - he knows things they can't be allowed to know. The Primogen council isn't stupid, and it's likely that they'll have ways to find out if the PCs have communicated with the ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T04:28:13-08:00","id":63379,"title":"","content":".) A charismatic vampire appears and founds a new covenant in the city based on winning freedom from the curse of vampirism and becoming human again. Is it real, wishful thinking or something more sinister?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T04:32:41-08:00","id":63381,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to seeing the story hooks you come up with. Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":".  grammer an spellig 02-02-2014, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T04:38:04-08:00","id":63382,"title":"","content":".) Members of the Belial's Brood are performing a gigantic ritual of some kind, until the PCs crash the party and heroically whip them out of town.<br /> <br /> Noone really knows anything substantial about the Brood ritual, except for one piece of information the Acolyte blood mages can uncover - whatever it was, it *worked*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T05:22:22-08:00","id":63388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=63372#post63372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. One hook per post. One post per hook.<br /> 2. Abstain from listing the things that need not be listed, such as &quot;you are hungry&quot; or &quot;someone died&quot;.<br /> 3. Rename it to the Story Hook Compendium or something similar?<br /> 4. Don't be a dick.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I don't really like 1st. Creates limitations, and unnecessary thread bloat. I see no reason not to be able to list X hooks within one post. As Long as they are properly numbered. <br /> 2. Should be obvious, but sometimes obviosu things must be mentioned<br /> 3. Totally agree<br /> 4. Agree even more","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T10:00:33-08:00","id":63476,"title":"","content":"- The city's hobos start to miss, but obviously no one cares, or notices. Except for the hobo's population. Mayor is being praised, but he also doesn't have a clue for what is happening. Meanwhile, someone approaches the Prince and Primogen with a solution for their &quot;drinking problem&quot;, some kind of bottled blood. Who is he? And is this related to the disappearances? (Or rather, the Blood Farm branches out).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T10:02:56-08:00","id":63478,"title":"","content":"1. An exsanguinated body is found in your hunting territory by mortal authorities. Needless to say, the Prince is very unhappy. Thing is, no one else operates in your turf (that you know of), and the body didn't have any obvious puncture marks. It's up to you (and your friends) to figure out what's going on, unless you want the Prince to leave you out for the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T10:27:20-08:00","id":63491,"title":"","content":"- She started as your ghoul. She was intense, passionate. A bit too much beyond the regular ghoul, maybe. One night, you met her again, and sense the beast. She managed to be embraced, just for you, to be like you. But the bond is still strong and she is everything you like in a woman, so you guys still fuck like bunnies. But now, she is trying to get you bonded as well. She wants you to love her as she loves you. At first, she tries small things, but as you resist, she will do ANYTHING to get you bonded to her, so you can be together, forever. You might not want this, but she is doing out of love. And the bond is very strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T19:32:20-08:00","id":63693,"title":"","content":"Isn't it a tad absurb to get ornery about the numbering? Does it really matter that the precise, exact number of plot hooks that the thread's name contains is reached or adhered to? I'm honestly confused as to why it matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T20:24:44-08:00","id":63717,"title":"","content":"Someone's out there, they say. It started as some rumors from neonates staking out their hunting grounds. Those were recently verified by an ancillae, for all that that matters. A person, one of the Kine, who makes the hackles of the Beast rise. Who can lash out with the strength of an elder. They're not Kindred, they don't seem to have any disciplines, or banes. But descriptions of the stranger match up with reports from witnesses regarding a prime suspect in a string of particularly brutal murders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T21:34:25-08:00","id":63755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=63693#post63693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it a tad absurb to get ornery about the numbering? Does it really matter that the precise, exact number of plot hooks that the thread's name contains is reached or adhered to? I'm honestly confused as to why it matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was nice to see that little loading progress bar. But more importantly, the dude was acting extremely childish, so this seems like a better solution than just continuing to argue. Honestly though, does it really matter who was in the wrong? The arguing was getting really obnoxious and distracting, so is it not better to just allow the plot hooks to keep coming in two peaceful threads than to wade through one thread full of pointless bickering?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T22:13:06-08:00","id":63771,"title":"","content":".) For the past three months, on the day after the new moon, three different Kindred were each destroyed in the same mysterious and disturbing manner. Their servants all describe a similar scene: the master failed to rise at sundown, and upon investigation, only ashes were found in the spot where the master normally takes his or her daily rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T22:56:47-08:00","id":63786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=63372#post63372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. One hook per post. One post per hook.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=63388#post63388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I don't really like 1st. Creates limitations, and unnecessary thread bloat. I see no reason not to be able to list X hooks within one post. As Long as they are properly numbered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the merit for that one is it allows one to quickly find a specific story hook if you know the number. If every post must have 1 story hook and only 1 story hook, then you can find a story hook by looking for the same numbered post. If I recall correctly, the default settings for posts per page is 15, so if you were looking for story hook #34, then you start looking on page 3 and scroll down until you get post #34.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure how that will work out in practice because this is an internet forum on the internet. There is not a whole lot that will stop people from doing stuff you don't want. In fact in the old story hooks thread, we had someone act in defiance of such a rule (technically it was a pattern that many people liked, but still), trying to stomp out any possibility that it may still work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T00:25:16-08:00","id":63810,"title":"","content":".) The Prince relaxes his rules a bit, the Sanctified stop being obnoxious about converting the heathens, the Carthians form peace treaties with the Invictus and the Requiems of most vampires in the city turn a little more comfortable and less dangerous. Things get better.<br /> <br /> Something can't be right.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T01:51:23-08:00","id":63831,"title":"","content":".) The Prince would like to make some sort of announcement, to all vampires in the city. The date and location is set, and participation is mandatory.<br /> <br /> The PCs are made responsible for general security and for making sure that this whole event won't be one huge Masquerade break.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T22:41:17-08:00","id":64615,"title":"","content":".) Your best mortal friend - your only Touchstone - has just confided a secret to you. He has recently discovered the existence of vampires. This is why he's stocking up on ammo and crosses and garlic, and wouldn't you like to help him get rid of the undead plaguing the city?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T02:48:51-08:00","id":64698,"title":"","content":"No more talk? Are we ready to begin soon?<br /> <br /> Based upon feed back, I'm thinking the new thread title should be &quot;Vampire Story Hook Compendium&quot;.<br /> <br /> Rules being considered:<br /> A) Please leave quality story hooks. Please don't point out easy stuff like &quot;You are hungry&quot; or &quot;Someone died&quot;. We would like it if things were more interesting than that. We would like something that would be worth writing a paragraph over.<br /> B) Please no fighting in the thread. If you have a problem, or don't like a rule, then take it over to the open discussion thread. (A separate thread will be provided)<br /> C) Please try to keep it 1 hook per thread, and 1 thread per hook. We would like to try to make it easy to find specific thread hooks. (Yes, no? Does this create too much friction?)<br /> <br /> If people like this, then I'll move ahead in the next day or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T02:52:56-08:00","id":64700,"title":"","content":"Seems reasonable to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T02:57:30-08:00","id":64703,"title":"","content":".) They've done it. A coterie of Ordo Dracul Ventrue has successfully established a ghoul family whose members is extremely susceptible to vampiric mind control, to the point that anyone with even the most basic proficience in the Lord's Words or the grandeur of the Daeva or scary face of the Haunts can get these people to do anything at all.<br /> <br /> Members of the family are currently doing their best to infiltrate the city government; and it's working.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T03:06:40-08:00","id":64711,"title":"","content":"The &quot;1 post per hook, 1 hook per post&quot; rule is here for ease of navigation, gauging progress at a glance, and general sanity. You'd be amazed how much faster you can get around by typing in the number of the hook in the address bar, especially since these forums count from 1, not 0. (note: this means there must also be a hook in the OP)<br /> Also, I think this is a pretty good thread for conversations about specific hooks, rules discussions, etc. Why clutter the forums with yet another?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T03:21:18-08:00","id":64721,"title":"","content":".) The most powerful, crazy, dangerous elder in town shows up at your door (rumors of serial diablerie, demonic sorcery, affinity with the Strix etc. abound).<br /> <br /> She doesn't want to eat you. She just wants you to take her out shopping. Her clothes are, well, nonexistent, and she isn't really used to how things work in the mortal world in 2014. She intends to spend a little more time in the company of mortals these days, so she needs young vampires to advise her on the ways of the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T21:48:36-08:00","id":65392,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>The admin and the mods would like everyone to calm down and let this issue go. As we found fault with parties on both sides of the issue, the threads have been merged. Everyone needs to find a way to get along, or don't participate in the topic.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T22:24:43-08:00","id":65416,"title":"","content":".) Twenty vampires. All of them staked. In an abandoned cellar in the catacombs of the old town. All of them bearing strange symbols that not even the most educated Acolytes can identify.<br /> <br /> And a written warning in Sanskrit - &quot;Do not wake them. Do not talk to them. Do not drink their blood.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T00:30:53-08:00","id":65472,"title":"","content":"Well in that case, I'll have to ask Christian, to at least get back to numbering, since it seems that we are not allowed to have a second thread for hook/story seed posting. And then we won't ask to keep 1 post/1hook or any other kind of rules in here. <br /> So please Christian, don't keep going on this &quot;not numbering&quot; principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T02:16:55-08:00","id":65513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=65392#post65392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>The admin and the mods would like everyone to calm down and let this issue go. As we found fault with parties on both sides of the issue, the threads have been merged. Everyone needs to find a way to get along, or don't participate in the topic.</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh well, so much for trying to solve things without bothering the moderators.<br /> <br /> However, I'm confused. I was under the impression that I was doing good by moving things to a new thread so we could act in peace without being bothered by someone who was being difficult. Was there something I did wrong? What do you recommend I should do in the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T03:05:09-08:00","id":65520,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I should reply... I'm genuinely worried, and that is never a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T04:14:25-08:00","id":65547,"title":"","content":"(Is numbering story hooks from now on with &quot;x+y&quot; whereas x is just x, and y a sequential number, ok with you guys?<br /> Also, I really think posts that don't contain any story hook are out of place in this thread. If you'll reply to this thread, I'd appreciate it if you to contribute to the fun.)<br /> <br /> x+1) Courier ghouls. Everywhere. Everytime the PCs feed, they get visions of some place they've never been, experiencing things that don't seem to make sense or have any sort of pattern.<br /> <br /> The ghouls don't seem to know what's going on and who ghouled them, even unter heavy Auspex scrutiny.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T04:17:48-08:00","id":65550,"title":"","content":"x+2) So you now have a cult.<br /> <br /> Some minor Masquerade break happened, and someone figured out what you are, and she decided that vampires are the coolest thing since sliced bread. So now she and some friends follow you around.<br /> <br /> They don't do much, other than fawn over you. And create even more Masquerade troubles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T04:35:54-08:00","id":65557,"title":"","content":"turns out X = 102 (counted all the threads. might have made a mistake, but it's as good of a number as any since at most it might differ by +-1.). <br /> <br /> So <br /> <br /> 103) A mortal starts to become a little bit more famous around the city, claiming that he can see the future. Some of his prophesies start coming true, except for the bloody ones. But those also come true, only among the vampires. Characters are the first to make the connection between his prophesies which didn't come true and the vampiric events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T12:45:21-08:00","id":65875,"title":"","content":"104) The Vinculum stops working; at least for the people who've drunk your blood. Their affection for you is getting weaker and weaker every night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T17:44:24-08:00","id":66116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=65513#post65513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh well, so much for trying to solve things without bothering the moderators.<br /> <br /> However, I'm confused. I was under the impression that I was doing good by moving things to a new thread so we could act in peace without being bothered by someone who was being difficult. Was there something I did wrong? What do you recommend I should do in the future?</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If you want to discuss this, send me a PM. This thread is about story hooks.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T09:02:15-08:00","id":66525,"title":"","content":"105) Some magical badness happened, and the PCs are in dire need of occult assistance, preferably by someone as skilled in Theban Sorcery as the Bishop. The PCs are either devout Sanctified or good enough at faking it, so it's likely that the Bishop is going to help them.<br /> <br /> Problem is, the Bishop is currently at Humanity 0 and a draugr. Someone needs to help him regain his sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T09:38:42-08:00","id":66536,"title":"","content":"106) You wake up. There's an owl in your haven. It's calling you &quot;master&quot; and asks for your instructions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T04:53:30-08:00","id":67112,"title":"","content":"107) You can't feed. Like, at all. When drinking human blood, it's as if the usual process of transformation from blood to vitae didn't happen. There is no explanation.<br /> 108) You can't feed. Like, at all. Something always goes wrong at the last moment; the victim doesn't cooperate, other people show up, the cat is on fire, etc. It's like a spell or a curse or something.<br /> <br /> 109) You can't feed. Like, at all. Everytime you try, you see unnatural visions of the first victim you've killed, and that kinda keeps you from going for the throat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:41:58-08:00","id":71014,"title":"","content":"110) A mortal, or perhaps a ghoul, is found spying on a member of the Council. Normally this wouldn't have been much of an issue, whoever sent the spy would be punished (if kindred) or killed (if anyone else really) and people would forget. Except this time, when the Sheriff tried to read the mind of the spy, she threw herself backwards screaming, flailing, falling to r\u00f6tschrek and storming away.<br /> Six hours later, when she is found, she's incoherent and just keeps muttering about how &quot;it must be impossible, it couldn't add up, please say it doesn't add up&quot;.<br /> The spy is now kept in a cell, also known as a bomb shelter, and the prince wants Someone to figure out what the hell the thing is, and if it might be possible to fix his sheriff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1734,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","user":"Asaram","date":". 02-13-2014, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:02:03-08:00","id":71437,"title":"","content":"111) The city was growing, the mortals were quite staunchly against mass-surveillance, the werewolves had finally been wiped out. Life was looking up, big time, for the kindred of the city. The CEO was even such a charmer and diplomat the Carthians gave her their support. Then, one day, the characters wake up not only with one secret each from another kindred in the city, where the bodies are buried so to speak, but also a piece of occult secrets, formulae, methods, signs.<br /> A lot of people worried, wondered what it might be. A Carthian tried his and managed to step right through a wall. Suddenly everyone tried theirs and they all did something incredible. Then the madness came.<br /> Everyone knows things, everyone has some impossible new power and, over night, three elders declared themselves the rulers of the domain... run for cover or try to figure out what is going on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T00:48:10-08:00","id":72503,"title":"","content":"112) The Lesu are a recently discovered group of hunter-gather peoples living in the rainforest of Northern Congo. They have spent the last couple thousand years with no interference from the outside world.<br /> <br /> And they're openly ruled by a coterie of vampires.<br /> <br /> If the Kindred don't act soon, there will be a Masquerade break of gigantic proportions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T08:36:51-08:00","id":73206,"title":"","content":"113) At first it seemed like a normal breach of the Masquerade, some sadistic fuck getting caught on camera feeding on three men, literally tearing them apart while doing so. It became wildly popular on youtube, spread for a while, the Chairman made some decisions and efforts, had some special effects experts claim responsibility. All done. Except the worrying thing is; the creature in the video can't be kindred. It was firmly on the video, it could split it's hands and they had sharp bits, it grew wings and flew away into the sunlight.<br /> Now a blood hunt is usually a pretty straightforward solution to things, but how do you hunt something you've never even heard of before? Something that seems to be immune to the weaknesses of kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T02:19:20-08:00","id":76937,"title":"","content":"114) Pope Francis is to install a couple new cardinals. This is a great opportunity for the Sanctified to get their claws into one of them and expand their influence quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T00:33:35-07:00","id":92166,"title":"","content":"115<br /> You're a bit of an occultist, so you understand the danger of Strix possession, what can happen. Your coterie embarks with you on a quest for more knowledge and defense, having seen first-hand what Strix possession can do (perhaps to a friendly NPC, perhaps to an official in the city).<br /> While searching, the expected happens: you get possessed. All of you. In one terrible hurricane of feathers and unlight.<br /> <br /> You awake two weeks later, by your watch, and expect to see dead loved ones, an eviscerated touchstone, maybe the sheriff banging down the door demanding to know why you (and your coterie, who are coming-to nearby) ashed everyone.<br /> Instead, you see the back of a piece of paper, which you proceed to tear off your face (it was stapled).<br /> It's written in a sloppy hand, vaguely reminiscent of your own. It just reads: &quot;WE ARE HAVING A SCAVENGER HUNT.&quot;<br /> <br /> The group of you leave the apartment, only to find the list of ten items on the outside door, along with another note (nailed, of course, which is classy):<br /> &quot;PS: WELCOME TO DETROIT.&quot;<br /> Shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T00:35:46-07:00","id":92167,"title":"","content":"116<br /> It's just you and the other guy.<br /> You and the other guy, sitting in a windowless train car.<br /> You and the other guy, in a train car, for six hours.<br /> You, that guy, no windows, quarter of a day, half a night trip.<br /> You smell like copper, probably, and dirt.<br /> He smells like wet dog and rage (which, apparently, smells a lot like whiskey and bad childhood memories).<br /> What do you do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T00:42:42-07:00","id":92170,"title":"","content":"117<br /> Dating sites are a great way to hunt. You started joking to other Kindred about how it's like &quot;GrubHub for Vampires.&quot;<br /> There's an ancilla in the city who's a little out of touch, but you taught him how to use computers yourself, so he starts bragging too. The old guy, who wants all the youngin's and yoots to think he's cool. Hip. Hep?<br /> The Bees Knees.<br /> <br /> Anyway, he bangs down your coterie's shared haven (or mutual hang-out, or crashes half-hazard into your favorite bar table, or whatever) and starts screaming and freaking out.<br /> <br /> You drag him out back (or punch him into torpor and wake him with blood, since he's a little bit on the soft side), and then ask him what's up.<br /> <br /> He made two big mistakes:<br /> 1. He gave a date <i>his actual Haven address</i> online.<br /> 2. He sorta kinda maybe met that date in-person.<br /> <br /> So two big, un-life changing events happened:<br /> A. He fell in love.<br /> B. The person he fell in love with showed up to the date with a stake.<br /> <br /> He has maybe been followed. He doesn't know. His haven is made out of ash and cinders, now.<br /> Sure, you delete the account for him, since it takes five seconds and it's a Masquerade breech so ridiculous that maybe you'd get punished for <i>not</i> covering it up.<br /> Do you do anything else for him, though? He promises he'll make it worth your while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T12:06:43-07:00","id":92385,"title":"","content":"Over the last thee months, thee vampires who do not share any ties of blood or Covenant have been found dead in their havens, their bodies withered as if all the moisture had been drained from them. they were posed standing in the middle of the room beatifically, held up by strings like a puppet, wreaths of flowers laid on their heads and around their feet. The flowers seem to not wilt until they leave the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T12:38:01-07:00","id":92403,"title":"","content":"119<br /> Someone replaced the local church's communion wine with vitae.<br /> The Lanacea Et Sanctum is somewhat pissed over this, because at some point during the days the congregation tore down the giant cross and replaced it with a statue of this old grizzled warrior dude with one eye and two ravens.<br /> There are some pros and cons to this situation:<br /> <br /> Pros:<br /> - It's hillarious<br /> - The local wolves have actually been acting <i>friendlier</i> to the Kindred<br /> - A group of quote-unquote wizards a city over have sent letters of accord to local leaders, offering mutual protection.<br /> - He seems like less of a pussy than the last deity they worshipped? I mean he has a spear, you think the Sanctum could get behind that.<br /> <br /> Cons<br /> - The Sanctum is going apeshit and threatening covenant war<br /> - The Circle of the Crone is totally down with this, but they claim it wasn't them<br /> - It's getting really, really cold out. Like, absurdly cold for late September; the lakes are freezing and the sky is cloudy and there are owls everywhere.<br /> - Draugr sightings have increased, and they have ghouled animals with them.<br /> <br /> The Sanctum wants your Coterie to investigate, the Circle wants you guys to help prove their innocence, and the Prince basically orders your little group to figure out who the hell is doing this.<br /> Who do you help? How do you help them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T12:42:45-07:00","id":92405,"title":"","content":"120<br /> Your sire, distant and detached, sends you - out of the blue - a hat box.<br /> Opening it reveals a mummified head of distinctly Egyptian descent with a note detailing some obnoxiously (characteristically) vague instructions:<br /> <br /> 1. Do not expose to daylight, Malkavians, wolves or the Sanctum<br /> 2. Be polite<br /> 3. To use, just add blood","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T12:47:06-07:00","id":92408,"title":"","content":"121<br /> Someone keeps leaving you little love notes.<br /> They are attached to drugged or/and dead prostitutes, so like, it's super sweet?<br /> You think they're trying to feed you? Maybe this is a box of chocolates kind of thing.<br /> <br /> It's also the kind of thing that has the potential to be a terrible breach of the Masquerade, since it's been happening every night for a week now, and they <i>know</i> where your Haven is. You'd best find your sick paramour and shut them down quick, least it gets worse than murder (and your Beast, ever the canny thing, assures you it's going to get so much more darling than murder).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T12:52:11-07:00","id":92412,"title":"","content":"122<br /> The Prince calls a meeting. Everyone rolls in. It's the kind of meeting where no one gets to bicker, and when they start, stern glares from a hundred and one beasts silence them immediately.<br /> <br /> The wolves in the woods and the Kindred of the city, they don't get along so great here. It was territory war, for a long time, and now it's a city divided in half, incursions to the other side constant and covert - the Kindred need blood, and the wolves need to do whatever the fuck they do.<br /> <br /> The Prince got a very clear and verifiable message, though, form their royalty: &quot;Go crazy,&quot; it said, &quot;the city is yours.&quot;<br /> What made them finally end the feud? Are they moving? Why would they abandon territory?<br /> <br /> Most of your Kindred exalt in being able to hunt without fear of reprisal, curfews, or feeding from something that only looks human; a few voices dissent, though, and say this must be a trap. It's a set-up; they want us to do something for them, or whatever scared them off? Maybe they think it and us, we'll wipe the board with each other.<br /> <br /> Which side do you take?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 04-04-2014, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T19:05:31-07:00","id":93128,"title":"","content":"123. Vampire Slayers have been watching too much Lupin III. Or Jing King of Bandits. Or Mouse. Or maybe one of the Carmen Sandiego variants. Either way, it seems some troublemaker has stolen your prince's house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 03-20-2014, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T09:41:52-07:00","id":140619,"title":"","content":"124) The Sanctified aren't convinced you've fully accepted your undead nature, so, on the anniversary of your death, they plan to surprise you a little. Like, by giving you pictures of one of your family members. Wrapped up in a neat little box. With a red ribbon around it and everything.<br /> <br /> The message is obvious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T02:39:51-07:00","id":141417,"title":"","content":"125) Well it finally happened, just like the elders feared it would. Some young fledgling learned how to Diablerize other vampires and has been systematically targeting the more powerful kindred in the city. They've already claimed 3 victims, one of which was a member of the city's Primogen! Their identity is still unknown, leading to more distrust and oppression of the neonates than ever before. If something is not done, the paranoid elders may incite a revolt from the angry neonates! The PC's are considerably powerful vampires (Ancilla through Elder status) and believe they can use themselves as bait to lure out the Diablerist. But will their plan succeed, or has this killing spree left the kindred too powerful to stop?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 126) The players are all newly sired and still learning the ropes of being a kindred. As it turns out, each of their sires belonged to the same coterie, and they're hoping their childer will form a similar allegiance with each other. That's not so bad, until some rival kindred suspect their sires of trying to form their own sub-faction under the Prince's nose! Can they work to disperse these accusations, or will the considerable old (and paranoid) Ventrue decide they're too much of a threat?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 127) Something incredible has happened! Word has it that an unaligned Nosferatu has become prince of the neighboring city and has revolutionized kindred society. The Nosferatu are granted equal rights and privileges, the Ventrue are now respectful and compliant, the city's kindred have freedom of religion, and the covenants share equal territory with each other.<br /> <br /> Yeah, we're not having that shit! The princes of various other cities have assigned the PC's with a mission: Find and assassinate this new Prince and bring down his vision of equality and acceptance! Succeed, and you'll earn a barony in your respective home domains. Fail (or defect), and your names will be added to the blood hunt as well!<br /> <br /> So first things first: A - How do we kill a Nosferatu who's so powerful he brought peace to a society of predators single handed? And B - Is the title of Baron worth it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-18-2014, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T16:13:03-07:00","id":141894,"title":"","content":"128) Nobody believed them when the cabal of mages said the vampires would pay for killing them all. But the very next day, the kindred of the city discovered something seriously wrong. They woke up at sunrise and found they could walk in the daylight. That's awesome right? Well not exactly... You see, while they can now withstand sunlight, it's darkness that incinerates them on contact. The vampires can't just carry flashlights around forever and the Nosferatu are having some considerable difficulty not being roasted, so they have to figure out a way to reverse the spell and once more confine them to darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T20:56:00-07:00","id":142050,"title":"","content":"129) For the past several years now, there has been a rather infamous Hunter who was pretty good at his job. His last hunt ended in a disaster that got the rest of his squad killed. Now this would be a time for celebration, if the vampire he sent out to destroy hadn't decided to Embrace him as a form of poetic justice. As if the Hunter wasn't already a big enough threat, he now has access to Nosferatu powers and has nothing else to lose. His sire is nowhere to be found, and the enraged childer is on the war path. He may only be a fledgling, but he knows the strengths and weaknesses of the city's kindred, and he's been killing them for years as a human. Can the PC's stop this new super-assassin before he exterminates them all?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 130) Out of curiosity, the PC's decided to investigate a string of missing children's reports in the city, fearing something supernatural may be at work. What they find is worse than they could possibly imagine, when a young haggard looking girl appears to them in an alley. It's clear she's been Embraced and the broken shackles around her neck and wrist suggest she was being held against her will, but when she reveals the culprit is none other than the city's own Prince, the PC's must make a choice. Do they ignore this and risk the Masquerade, or do they confront the Prince and risk earning Blood Hunts on their heads?<br /> <br /> Wait a minute... how does this girl know anything about vampire society, and how did she know where to find the PC's in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-19-2014, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T14:55:12-07:00","id":146062,"title":"","content":"131) The sire of one of the PC's had another childe before they came along. She was talented, obedient, hard working, and showered their sire with affection. Basically the vampire equivalent of a daddy's girl who went onto make her &quot;father&quot; proud by establishing a base of power in the city. Well it turns out she's suffering from an acute version of sibling rivalry, and thinks the PC is here to replace her as daddy's favorite. She's determined to win back daddy's affection, even if that means killing her &quot;baby&quot; brother / sister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-22-2014, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T22:40:11-07:00","id":156270,"title":"","content":"132) The city's kindred are ruled by two factions, the Circle of the Crone, and the Lancea Sanctum. Even though it's been a few decades, none of the other factions were able to gain a foothold, and now the Circle knows why. The leaders of the local Sanctified are zealots who have been crushing any attempt for the other powers to stake their claim, and now they've finally turned their attention on the Circle. They've announced a full blown crusade, which basically translates to open warfare on all who will not convert to their doctrine.<br /> <br /> Will the PC's side with the fanatics, or the heathens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T07:37:14-07:00","id":176986,"title":"","content":"133) The prince has issued a blood hunt on a vampire for defying him. Having no intention of meeting final death alone, she decides to blow the masquerade and bring the prince's entire kingdom down with her! The PC's are in charge of hunting her down, as well as clean up duty with any witnesses who see her in action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T07:47:23-07:00","id":176990,"title":"","content":"134) A Hollow Mekhet of the Ordo Dracul murders the father of a teenage girl and, as directed by his Elders, begins to analyse the changes that this death causes. Twelve years later, the girl has become a woman. The Shadow has spent the intervening time studying the girl and recording every aspect of her life. He has become obsessed. Every minute detail of the woman's mundane existence is strutinised, analysed and painstakingly recorded. His Haven bursts at the seams with volumes of handwritten notebooks. He has made a deal with his reflection to tail the woman during the day and has explicit instructions to ensure the precise accumulation of the very specific data he requires to complete his notes. It is far from certain that the reflection is providing accurate information and this uncertainty is a constant torment.<br /> <br /> His Mentor despairs. She feels that he has overlooked other lines of enquiry by focussing on this one mortal. He has lost the Dragon's Tail. This Lesser Work no longer merits further study, and even worse, he neglects his study of the Coils altogether. His coterie is finding it difficult to get him involved in their schemes, he rarely attends Elysium. If it wasn't for the necessity of feeding, he would spend his entire Requiem following this woman and documenting what he sees. He is very careful not to interact with her in any way, so as not to contaminate what he sees as useful and essential data.<br /> <br /> He has become stagnant.<br /> <br /> What would divert his attention from this pointless study? Perhaps one could begin a new Dragon's Tail. Perhaps select a better subject, a subject whose life is already well-documented. All those relationships, casual and meaningful, already transcribed in the minutest of detail. A wealth of material that could form the basis of some meaningful research. All he has to do is murder the object of his obsession.<br /> <br /> Tonight.<br /> <br /> <i>(This is actually the character concept for the main protagonist I ran in a game a few years ago - good times)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3349-kaleb-d-aark","name":"Kaleb D'aark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T01:05:33-07:00","id":199774,"title":"","content":"135) Some worthless Caitiff Nosferatu got their feelings hurt and decide they want equal rights. They decide to form picket lines and protest for a more compassionate Domain. So, will the local kindred give in and treat them with respect, or will they risk a confrontation with a bunch of Haunts who don't know their own strength?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 136) A sarcophagus from some forgotten wasteland half a world away has been brought to the city and rumors abound that it may contain some ancient vampire. Most of the sound minded kindred think nothing of it, until the night when the museum plans to examine it. The moment the sarcophagus opened, the entire museum exploded with enough force to leave behind a pile of rubble and debris. What's even more shocking is unconfirmed reports of a single, unidentified survivor fleeing the center of the blast after it happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T18:10:00-07:00","id":202525,"title":"","content":"127) The Carthian Baron decided to make a statement. Walking straight into the Invictus Prince's throne room, he proceeded to shoot him in the groin with a double barrel shot gun. Well, looks like the two covenants are at war!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T23:44:03-07:00","id":207961,"title":"","content":"128) The characters are charged with retrieving the prince's childe, who has fled onto a new luxury cruise liner (funded in large part by the prince, the primogen, and their mortal pawns) and concealed himself somewhere onboard just before its midnight maiden voyage departure gala. Your choices are going back empty handed, sabotaging a multi-million dollar ship belonging to elders... or joining the cruise and ferreting out the fugitive before it reaches its first port in six days.<br /> <br /> Enjoy the all-night buffet, but it might be best if you<i> didn't go back for seconds</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T16:39:09-07:00","id":250216,"title":"","content":"129) The local Carthians have come up with a unique way to decide who gets to rule as Prince of their domain. Every 10 years, they hold a mixed martial arts tournament, and the champion gets to reign for the next decade. The next tournament is coming up soon, and you've decided to try your hand at being king of the mountain. Will you take home the belt, or be disgraced in a contest of strength and skill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-13-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T07:00:08-07:00","id":250728,"title":"","content":"130. One day every year all vampires leave the city. Every vampire who remains in the city that day is never found again. What is behind this? Is it a monster are maybe an ancient vampire?<br /> 131. A new drug appears in the city. It's very addictive, very lethal and people seem to get hallucinations from this drug. They can even predict the future while hallucinating. However the drugs are red crystals and they seem to resemble dried vampire blood. What is this stuff? And where does it come from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T20:00:40-07:00","id":251198,"title":"","content":"132) Word has it that the Carthians have discovered a way to synthesize human blood, which can successfully feed a vampire without endangering human lives in the process. That's awesome, right? Well not exactly, because they've decided that with this new food source, they don't need the Masquerade anymore, and once they've made enough of it, they plan to expose themselves to the public. They didn't ask the other covenants about their opinions on this decision, and expect everyone to just fall in line with their new dietary supplement. Taking care of this problem won't be easy, you'll need to find and destroy the formula, eliminate the scientists who produce it, and destroy the production factories to ensure all trace of this plan is completely wiped out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T03:49:37-07:00","id":251371,"title":"","content":"133.<br /> <br /> 1:7 And the LORD said unto Satan, Whence comest thou? Then Satan answered the LORD, and said, From going to and fro in the earth, and from walking up and down in it.<br /> 1:8 And the LORD said unto Satan, Hast thou considered my servant Job, that there is none like him in the earth, a perfect and an upright man, one that feareth God, and escheweth evil?<br /> 1:9 Then Satan answered the LORD, and said, Doth Job fear God for nought?<br /> 1:10 Hast not thou made an hedge about him, and about his house, and about all that he hath on every side? thou hast blessed the work of his hands, and his substance is increased in the land.<br /> 1:11 But put forth thine hand now, and touch all that he hath, and he will curse thee to thy face.<br /> 1:12 And the LORD said unto Satan, Behold, all that he hath is in thy power; only upon himself put not forth thine hand. So Satan went forth from the presence of the LORD.<br /> <br /> A domain ruled by the Sanctified is plagued by series of brutal murders. Someone, clearly not done Kindred as some of these murders are committed in the daytime, plagues the community, plagues the truly righteous mortals trying to ruin their lives and make them denounce the God through taking away those who are close to them [But not taking their lifes, at least not before they curse the God]. And when kills, he clearly does it in Biblical fashion. The Slasher did not resist temptation of announcing himself, leaving clues and messages in which he styles himself the agent of the Lord, testing the righteous. What is worse, hunters followed the trail of bodies, trying to put stop to the tide of murders.<br /> <br /> How will local Sanctified react to someone usurping the mantle of God's chosen? Is this madman delusional or really is there something to his claims, as he displays clearly supernatural abilities [A scourge]? What to do with hunters who might uncover local Kindred by accident?<br /> <br /> PS. Personally I envision the Slasher as a Legend or quasi-Legend with appropiate Frailty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T22:54:05-07:00","id":257902,"title":"","content":"134) Ah the 50's. A time when organized crime was just starting to become a major threat in America. When Al Capone is crowned the Invictus Prince of the city, he's looking to expand his operations. Will the players earn their way into the legendary crime lord's inner circle, or will they meet final death at the hands of gang warfare?<br /> <br /> Vampire Mobster story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 135) When the head priestess for the Circle of the Crone is found crucified in her own Haven, it ignites a full blown war with the Lancea Sanctum. The Pagans are so pissed off, they're attacking the Sanctified on the streets, not even trying to be political or stealthy about it. Was this actually the work of the Sanctified, or is one of the other factions trying to ignite a war between the two and swoop in when they're too weak to fight back?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 136) The Carthian movement has finally done it, they've convinced vampire society to become democratic in its government. All decisions from now on will be decided by popularity of vote. But when the new government uses too much deliberation, their problems begin to pile up. And various sub-factions are now squabbling over who's ideas are right and wrong. The Cathian Movement is beginning to crumble to pieces, and those who counted themselves among the ranks of the Invictus can do little to hide their smiles as they watch it all come tumbling down around them. Have they truly given into the Carthian way of thinking, or have they decided to let their arch rival wipe itself out? Either way, somebody needs to bring stability to the situation, before full blown anarchy comes to the city's kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-13-2016, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T08:05:09-07:00","id":264617,"title":"","content":"137) It started with them breaking the mold from clan stereotypes, then it moved onto other things. Eating mortal food, walking in the sunlight, and now there are rumors that one kindred may have actually gotten pregnant after her Embrace! Something is causing a fraction of the newest vampires of the city to develop... wrong. Their clan markings are weaker, they seem more human than they should be, biologically as well as mentally. The Prince finally decides to call down the hammer when the newest Fledgling spontaneously manifests Dominate, Nightmare, and Majesty without any formal training and no apparent clan lineage. These &quot;thin bloods&quot; as they are being called, need to be driven out, and the cause behind their creation discovered!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 138) A recent census taken shows that 5% of the city's population are vampires. That is far, far too many vampires! In order to regulate the population control, the Prince decides to hold a competition. The winners will be allowed to hold onto their domains and maybe even granted new ones. The losers (who aren't destroyed in the process) will be exiled to the suburbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-24-2014, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T17:20:25-07:00","id":269616,"title":"","content":"139) The masquerade has been blown, the world knows about the supernatural and is mobilizing its armies to stamp it out. With the vampires of the world vastly outnumbered and facing extinction, they must perform the unthinkable, they must set aside their political differences and unify under a single banner where loyalty and kinship are more important than status and territory. This is the birth of the Sabbat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T05:31:27-07:00","id":298023,"title":"","content":"140) About 20 years ago, you descimated a Hunter who attempted to slay you. Leaving him broken and humiliated, you decided letting him live would be a fitting punishment. Now he's returned for you, and he's carrying the blood of the Noctuku in his veins!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T18:37:38-08:00","id":309702,"title":"","content":"141) The Children's Crusade has arrived in the city, demanding, among others, a member of the Prince's mortal family; a ten-year old boy unaware of vampirekind. Furious, the Prince has rallied his vassals including you to protect the child. Will you risk the wrath of the Crusade by denying them a recruit, or will you offer up the boy to fend off the fearsome army?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T19:02:00-08:00","id":381501,"title":"","content":"142) Our vampire player has themselves a secret admirer. Well more like a crazy stalker. It turns out she's mortal and fell madly in love with him after witnessing his true nature. The World of Darkness is more terrifying than she imagined, but she's just crazy enough to stick around for her &quot;true love&quot; and see it through. Question is, how will her lover deal with the situation, and more importantly, how will the city's kindred react to her presence?<br /> <br /> Designed to be a two player game, though can include more for additional drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T22:22:02-08:00","id":416161,"title":"","content":"143) The PCs are approached by the most experienced, powerful ghoul of an Elder. She says she wants out - she's sick of being a blood doll and a junkie. She's willing to trade away all the elder's secrets in exchange for a safe existence somewhere far away from him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:44:28-08:00","id":416516,"title":"","content":"144) The PCs need to question a vampire hunter who staked [someone important to them] on where he stashed the body. Problem is the hunter got a bit careless and ended up in prison. This wouldn't ordinarily be a problem but Tombs, an ancient Nosferatu, is Lord over that prison. He'll allow the PCs access if they are able to get the head of a local drug gang convicted and sentenced for only reasons he knows. The PCs will have to use all the influence at their fingertips to see the well connected and well armed gangster arrested and sent to prison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:35:22-08:00","id":416702,"title":"","content":"145) For as long as anyone can remember members of 4 vampire lineages would take turns bringing a 15 year old red-headed child to the edge of the Lake at the edge of the domain every 13 years. They said it would keep the Old Thing away. The last two times one of the lineages went, they came back changed: speaking an Indian language that hadn't been spoken in 300 years and practicing a bizarre new form of blood magic with what seems more like fear than devotion. The PCs have pissed off the Prince, and he sends them to deliver the next 13th year sacrifice to the edge of the Lake. What will happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T22:27:07-08:00","id":417253,"title":"","content":"146) A ghost, man. It's one of your former victims, so you're yourself to blame for it (she) haunting you. You get to see her everytime you're about to eat. <br /> <br /> &quot;Why would you hurt him like that?&quot;<br /> &quot;Why would you violate her mind?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's sickening. And it's also seriously interfering with your ability to feed, which is a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T02:47:04-07:00","id":660547,"title":"","content":"a neonate stumbles on a group of hunters plotting the demise of the city`s prince who happens to be the the clans mate of the neonate .what do you do report it,and explain why you were out in a forbidden area . or do you not report it and hope it does not happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7751-dark-skye","name":"Dark Skye","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T15:57:16-07:00","id":662317,"title":"","content":"148) There's a turf war between the local Ventrue and Daeva clans, each wanting to prove that they are the true echelons of society by establishing their clan as the majority rulers of the city. In order to establish a spy network, the Ventrue have taken to hiring the Nosferatu, while the Daeva have employed the Mekhet. The Gangrel, not being one to take sides in a political conflict, have remained a neutral party, hiring their services to whichever clan is willing to supply them with resources and other privileges.<br /> <br /> So who do you want to see leading the city? The clan who rules with the iron fist, or the clan who rules with the silver tongue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:44:54-07:00","id":674596,"title":"","content":"149.) It's Vegas Baby. Anything goes... including the toppling of Princes.<br /> <br /> Las Vegas is a city of illusions and sin. Everything is different there: Wolves wander the Desert, the Vampires rule the Casinos, and there is rumor of a Mage enslaved to the local Prince that can strike fear into the local creatures with her powers. The saying 'What happens in Vegas, stays in Vegas' is notoriously true with the creatures of night.<br /> <br /> The previous prince was murdered two years ago, but the internal investigation to what happened to him has gone cold with no results only that the killer went by the alias &quot;The Voice&quot;. The clans have specifically selected the players to investigate what is happening. Delve into the twisted politics of keeping power over not only blood, but money in Sin City. Solve the mystery behind the last prince's death, choose to friend some of the local power brokers, or the abused, and find the Voice before they strike again.<br /> <br /> Your first night in Vegas? The Voice has struck: exploding a wing of Ceasar's Palace... Good luck.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> In this story, after investigation and choices of the players, they find that the Voice, all this time, had been the enslaved Mage at the Prince's and party's side. Add as many twists and turns as you like, it took my players 2 months to figure out the Voice was the Mage. Our conclusion came with the Prince becoming paranoid of being next and destroyed a club with a bomb that was a hot bed of Mage activity. In return, the Mage murdered him, without knowing just how close to home the threat was.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8027-calconstantine","user":"CalConstantine","date":".  Did not know I could add spoilers! 10-27-2015, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8027-calconstantine","name":"CalConstantine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:24:49-07:00","id":714826,"title":"","content":"150) Self-Made... Man?<br /> <br /> The city is in an uproar after a secret message to the Prince somehow became common knowledge- that a <i>kine somehow forced the Embrace from a neonate</i>.<br /> <br /> The power structure is paralyzed as the Elders, the Primogen, and the Prince all hurl responses and motives and consequences and half-formed plans back and forth among one another in a near-literal Frenzy. Worse, the metaphysical and political consequences of any given opinion could be catastrophic, so everybody's deployed their own under-table agents to get the job done.<br /> <br /> Is the story immediately proven or disproven as a hoax? Is this only a momentary hiccup as a plan rattles together after a couple of days, a consent is formed, and the mystery is dealt with? Does the mystery disappear entirely, with no further evidence or update, after that first baffling revelation? Is it a protracted cold war, with the unthinkable, an unknown vampire traitor among them? Is it the start of a dreadfully successful hunting campaign against local vampires? Is it ultimately of little meaning, but responsible for tipping the power in one direction or another, enough for a coup, enough that it comes forward that the story was misinformation? Dear God, <i>did the human know this would happen</i>, set the stage for him to attack or seize power or run? That <i>DICK</i>!!<br /> <br /> ...is the new vampire... <i>accepted?? </i>As someone's pawn, or protege, or genuine attempt at altruism?<br /> <br /> How long do they survive the All Night Society?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 10-22-2015, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:43:12-07:00","id":714891,"title":"","content":"151) The Damp<br /> <br /> Over the course of several days, water is revealed to have been getting in through a window beside a kindred's daytime resting spot. Sunproofing is uncompromised, but the water gets in no matter how tightly sealed the window is, possibly through the wall or lintel. Without physically tearing apart the window, which would defeat the purpose, there's no way to tell without professional evaluation where it's coming from. Over the several days this takes to schedule and investigate, the damp spot in the carpet slowly spreads wider, to touch the owners' bed.<br /> <br /> That day, while the vampire is sleeping, they wake in darkness to the feel of someone embracing their back, spooning them. The intruders' body temperature is somewhere between hypothermia and room temperature, and they are drenched with wetness. If provoked, the entity vanishes, leaving only a matress and floor damper still. If unprovoked, it continues to lie motionlessly until your concentration wanes and you return to sleep, waking to find nothing but more dampness.<br /> <br /> As a standalone story: The expert finds nothing wrong and the existing wetness evaporates as per usual physical water, although damage might have been done. The entity never returns- what do you make of a creature that spent days of effort to spend a few hours embracing you quietly, then leaving forever? Did it do something to you? Take something? <i>Was it just that lonely??</i><br /> <br /> As a seed: How long do these events continue? Who escalates them? Do you find it's feeding, trying to possess or kill you, and have to stop it? Was it a messenger, and what was the message? Is this only a prelude to communication? A new ally? God, <i>is this an OLD ally??</i> <i>What did you DO?!?</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 10-22-2015, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T12:53:33-07:00","id":715154,"title":"","content":"152) Earthquake!<br /> <br /> The worst one on record for the entire country. Where no one expected it, right in the players city.<br /> <br /> Vampires across the domain are awakened in the middle of the day to the psychic death cries of their clanmates, some closer than they ever expected, crushed by buildings and swallowed by the earth. For long hours they can only wait in their havens, corralled in by the sun and chaos. It doesn't take long for communications to fire up, some of the harpies arranging contacts and shooting out group texts, noting deaths and warnings. <br /> <br /> No one's heard from the Prince.<br /> <br /> In the hours before sundown, centuries-old plots are scrapped, new plans made in haste, coteries organize, waiting patiently to strike at bitter enemies, some vampires mourn over their lost touchstones and ghouls, while others see the chaos on the news, hear that help will take days to organize, and see only feasts and opportunity.<br /> <br /> When nightfall comes, fires are ravaging the city, along with the moon the only source of light with the power lines severed, emergency services are paralyzed, humanity is flailing. The scent of blood rides the smoke in the air. Danger. Cries of pain in the distance, punctuated by joyfully sadistic laughs. Vampires aren't the only things crawling through the dark ruins tonight. It's time to act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T21:21:10-07:00","id":731166,"title":"","content":"<b>#153: Cobwebs in the Attic</b><br /> <br /> A favored ghoul has been complaining about a spider infestation in his home. He also complains about headaches which you might have mistaken for Vitae-born hunger pangs. Then one day he didn't answer your calls or messages. You went to investigate and you found him, acting strangely. He's colder now, more distant, and his eyes are those of a dead thing. Your Vitae seems to bring him around a little, but he has still grown disjointed and distant. Even Disciplines can only reveal so much. Auspex says that this is a supernatural creature, a human body sustained by Kindred Vitae\u2014a ghoul, surely? But it tells you that this creature is also being controlled by someone else, and yet you cannot find any hint of the vampiric mind magic that haunts her steps. Perhaps one of your enemies has made a move against you, seeking to use a favored servant as a weapon or spy.<br /> <br /> Things get stranger still when Lupine activity occurs in your territory. Stories, rumors among the Kindred, &quot;dog attacks&quot; in the news. Someone's pit bulls, they say, perhaps dogs bred for fighting. You know better. Something has agitated the Lupines and now the court is growing tense. You notice that the cobwebs seem to be getting worse in the places you frequent. What could be causing it?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The ghoul is in fact host to an <i>Azlu</i> Crawler. The Crawler found its perfect host body: perfectly preserved as long as it consumes blood from its vampiric master, protected as part of that same vampire's brood. It's using the shadowy world of the Kindred to spin its webs, relishing in their stagnant unlives, supping upon the blood of those they victimize. The <i>Azlu </i>has become addicted to the power of Vitae just as surely as any mortal would. What's more, it realizes the sheer supernatural power of the Blood and grows ever hungrier for it. Perhaps, the <i>Azlu </i>thinks, ensnaring and devouring a vampire will provide it with greater power, even spark its horrid metamorphosis. This process is not unlike diablerie, but it may in fact be creating something neither vampire nor <i>Azarath</i>. It may be on the verge of birthing a new race of horrors into the world, a bloody genesis of vampiric spider shapeshifters whose fangs pierce the very flesh of the spirit world and suck it dry.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T19:17:48-07:00","id":733704,"title":"","content":"<b>#154 How It All Fell Apart</b> (This is a add-on to #149 to tie into a larger arc of my <i>Obscured Lines</i> story to explain some further lore of that story, but would work great on its own and start your own lore reasoning to the fall of Julii)<br /> <i>Requirements: Requiem for Rome mixed with elements from Changeling and a touch of Mage</i><br /> <br /> Julius Ceasar has just returned from Gaul, but with lesser mentions of a secret attempt to reach Britannia, a mysterious Isle of Fog ruled by a coalition of three siblings. What was unknown was Senex (Aulus Ceasar) himself had gone along with his blood descendant, and was thought missing all those years while he was on campaign. Things for the Julii has been fragmenting, strained relations with the other clans are starting to come ahead... but Senex has been put on a special task from the nefarious Striges to try and redeem and gather favor once again as Remus had done. <br /> <br /> However, upon his return, the Striges are furious with Senex and have awoken forces Romans have not faced, and they are calling for blood. He had failed them, and the consequences will be dire. His mission was to bring back a being from Britannia simply called The Witch Queen for the Striges. A mage of power who can call upon Fire itself, and has a gift of Prophecy. However, in spite of the Striges, Senex has murdered her in cold blood, disposing her body in ways not to grant honor and damn her soul to wander the Earth. <br /> <br /> Aid Senex in fighting off the rage of the Striges along with enraged Changlings after the murder of a powerful ally, the Witch Queen, and fend off the fall of the Julii for a little longer, or help the Striges with taking down Senex for his betrayal while paying retribution to the Changlings and Fae, and aid in the fall of the House of Julii. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> In our story Arch we have modified some placements of real people in that time period and their fates obviously. If you wish to do something simliar as we have, the spoiler in this story is that depending on the choices of the party, they can aid or try and stop a horrendous fate for two innocent beings. The Striges, seeing that Senex has no regard for what happened, have targeted Julius Ceasar's daughter, Julia. In our story she is pregnant with twins, as she is the wife of Pompeii who flees the city after Julius's return. <br /> <br /> While on route to capture Pompeii, word returns to Rome that Pompeii has been killed, triggering a sudden labor for Julia. She has twins, a boy and girl, but dies in child birth. The children are taken by the Striges, one given to the Fae and Changlings for the repayment of the Queen's blood, and one kept hidden by the Striges for their own devices, which can be up to the digression of the DM. This story is easily to deal with customization depending on how badly you wish the Striges to lash back and vice versa if you chose to go against Senex.<br /> <br /> The key point of the Witch Queen in our story line is that the Striges wished to test the mixing of blood with mages of certain elements to see if something may stick as a sort of half breed, but Senex knowing this, decides on himself, even if it will help vampires against the weakness of fire, this is not something that should be done. Thus, he murders the Queen, knowing it will set them back years, if not centuries to find a powerful enough mage again. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8027-calconstantine","name":"CalConstantine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T10:48:52-07:00","id":735207,"title":"","content":"155) High and Dry<br /> <br /> After an instance of the fire department suffering an outrageously unlikely setback during a routine fire-fighting excursion, property in the city burns to the ground. Investigating, the Senechal is alarmed to discover that this is only the tip of the iceberg- several stations have been having serious financial, personnel, or equipment problems. The characters are deployed to determine whether this is innocent infrastructure failure, an attack on the city, or an attack on the parts of the city that conspicuously fear fire.<br /> <br /> If they don't get results in time, or if this is just the seed to a larger encounter, an extremely high-ranking kindred has their Haven utterly destroyed via a combination of competent arson and yet another fire department blunder (was the elder killed, or is somebody playing houseguest with the PCs?) Now it's urgent, <i>and </i>it's a fight to keep the locals from panicking. Worse, it's still not clear whether this is an unknown kindred attacking their foe(s), or whether it's an outside player like a Hunter, or whether it's <i>both</i>, like a collaboration or Strix possession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 10-28-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T12:48:00-07:00","id":735557,"title":"","content":"156) You're in Good Hands<br /> <br /> A character with a ground-floor haven is awakened in early afternoon by a horrible crunching sound as a sedan plows full speed halfway through a wall. Moments later, a disoriented driver begins to try and find someone to apologize to.<br /> <br /> How long can you yell a conversation from the shadows before he gets suspicious? Will it only take a few awkward minutes furiously warding them off with an insurance card so you can call your minions to help you deal? Do they insist you come with them to inspect the damage? God help you, are those <i>bullet holes and bricks of coke </i>in that car??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:55:59-08:00","id":812815,"title":"","content":"157) Magic within the Blood.<br /> All hell has broken loss the Lancea et Sanctum have allied themselves with the Circle of Crone. Together they have discovered the means to make the Tremere Mages slaves once more. They only need one last piece to complete their spell, an artifact within the partys possession. Now the troupe must survive the assault from the two covenants, evade the Tremere as they stop at nothing to escape enslavement once more. <br /> What can the troup do to save the balance of power in not just the city but the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T13:54:03-08:00","id":844714,"title":"","content":"158.) (A little late calendar wise, but I only just learned about the subject) Somebody has been sending old fashioned <a href=\"http://www.collectorsweekly.com/articles/happy-valentines-day-i-hate-you/\" target=\"_blank\">vinegar valentines</a> to various notable kindred in the domain. In addition to the usual things that vinegar valentines insulted people for (as seen in the link) the cards also include rhyming barbs at more vampire specific violations of societal mores, including a few cards that indicate knowledge of embarrassing secrets of elders and even more cards meant to provoke fights between kindred, which is why the prince has put the PC coterie in charge of finding this anonymous harasser. Figuring out who's sending the hate mail will be tough, since the cards have come in and out of style since the Victorian era and have recently become trendy again among the modern kine (both as a rejection of valentines day and as a harassment tool), making it harder to narrow down a suspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:18:03-08:00","id":845057,"title":"","content":"159) Another Court Altogether<br /> <br /> At a minor kindred social function, the characters are approached by an awkward, milquetoast Elysium outsider, who is clearly trying not to look like he's hemming and hawing over an awkward subject to broach.<br /> <br /> Once relaxed or intimidated, he admits to an ulterior motive and pitches a job- his Touchstone is a basketball trophy on display in a local high school, and he wants the characters to safeguard it for him for a sizable cash reward. If the characters tell him to do it himself, or scoff at the ease of the task, he slumps (or bristles) and admits that <i>safeguarding </i>isn't quite the right word. His old high school got a new coach a few years ago, and since then their sports programs have improved enough to get state-level attention.<br /> <br /> Which wouldn't be a problem, but His <i>actual</i> Touchstone is, in fact, the trophy, <i>while it's still inside the display case. T</i>he client's old high school achievement is about to be bettered, and the trophy replaced.<br /> <br /> That's right. If they take the job, the characters are basically committing to using their sinful vampire powers to quietly <i>fix a children's sporting event. </i>At which there will be at least one college scout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T09:55:41-08:00","id":845690,"title":"","content":"160) The Piper of Pubtown<br /> <br /> A regent is having trouble with their feeding grounds. A string of disappearances at the local bars is stressing the herd and making it harder to feed or contract out the grounds. So far they have it under wraps with the mortal authorities, but the ramifications for the Masquerade are worrisome as well. Four disappearances over the course of two weeks.<br /> <br /> The culprit is a Gangrel nomad from a despised medieval bloodline known as the Coppenbr\u00fcgge. The line is known for creating pseudo-revenants called Waisenkind from children killed in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> Using a mortal honeypot in the form of a shot boy/girl (or any mortal that can blend in to multiple bars on a weekly basis), the victims are given an alcoholic shot/concoction which causes them to hear faint music in their heads, and to follow that sound wherever it leads. Of course, it leads to their devouring.<br /> <br /> The Red Herring<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If the players scope out the bars or manage to get a hold of security tapes from the nights of the disappearances, early on their radar is a local singer-songwriter who's had contact with two of the victims. A serial tail-hound, the musician is known for one-night stands and maybe-kinda taking advantage of drunken paramours. They ply their shtick somewhat aggressively in front of (or on!) the PCs. A roughing up, in addition to discipline use, reveals they didn't seal the deal with those two, and never met the other two victims. They can prove they were playing other bars on those two nights.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Master<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Parent Clan: Gangrel<br /> Bloodline: Coppenbr\u00fcgge<br /> Nickname: Whisps, Pfeifers<br /> Heritage: Medieval German (Saxon)<br /> Disciplines: Animalism, Dominate, Protean, Resilience<br /> <br /> Bloodline Bane: The Coppenbr\u00fcgge must sleep for the day in ground or water in the presence of special herbs important to the creature. If the Coppenbr\u00fcgge\u2019s slumbering area is located, and its herbs are collected, they can be crafted into an oil or poultice (Medicine, Science or Survival roll, 'doses' = successes) and applied to bladed weapons to change the damage to aggravated - each hit uses one 'dose'. Further, Coppenbr\u00fcgge are tied to old medieval contracts in which mayors (regents/princes) would pay them 100 guilder (gold pennies) to leave their hunting territories alone. The gold coins would be buried near the hunting sites of the bloodline. If a Regent buries one-hundred golden coins in their feeding grounds, the Coppenbr\u00fcgge cannot gain any sustenance from mortals who have visited the territory in the last 24 hours.<br /> <br /> Signature Devotions:<br /> <br /> The Piper's Drink<br /> Pre-Req: Dominate 2. Resilience 2<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> <br /> The Coppenbr\u00fcgge mixes their blood with an essence of their 'bane' herb along with some sort of flora from a specific location. If the mixture is imbibed or ingested, roll contested Wits + Crafts + Dominate vs. the victim's Resolve + BP. If the Coppenbr\u00fcgge wins, the victim hears a faint ethereal music in the back of their head. They gain the Mesmerized condition, with an active command of going to the location where the extra flora was harvested for the concoction. On an exceptional success, the victim even risks direct danger to follow the music to its source. Despite the name, the concoction can be food or drink.<br /> <br /> (Depending on your setting, there are usually foraging guides on the internet that people use to go herb/plant hunting IRL. Wild mint and Elderberries are decently common across the states, and often used for drinks / sweets.)<br /> <br /> Create Waisenkind<br /> Pre-Req: Animalism 2, Protean 2 (or 4), Resilience 1<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae, 1 WP<br /> <br /> The Coppenbr\u00fcgge feeds its blood to the corpse of a child who was killed by the 'elements of nature.' Roll Strength + Survival + Resilience. On a success, the child rises as a Humanity 1 Revenant (see p94:VtR2E) with an additional benefit: one Predatory Aspect from Protean. If the vampire has Protean 4, the bonus is upgraded to an Unnatural Aspect. What aspect is granted depends on how the child died. Creating Waisenkind is a Level 3 Sin. See Minions Entry for build details.<br /> <br /> General Methods:<br /> <br /> At start, the antagonist is in the cycle of feeding themselves and their pack of Waisenkind. Using The Piper's Drink to create alcoholic beverages and using a mortal minion through Dominate or the blood bond to disperse them to loner-type clients of the bars. These victims then return to a secluded spot where they are preyed upon. If you want to prolong the encounter at this stage, only the Waisenkind are present and waiting for the victim. Otherwise, the whole group can be there. If the Waisenkind are destroyed or captured, the Coppenbr\u00fcgge changes tact to begin rebuilding their pack. This takes the form of now targeting children in the feeding territory, luring them into the the closest wilderness/natural area, and letting nature take its deadly course.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> The Minions<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Waisenkind: Feral Children created by a posthumous embrace. Rising as revenants with Humanity 1, these creatures are very close to animals themselves, wrangled only by the Coppenbr\u00fcgge's blood and disciplines. <br /> <br /> Disciplines: None<br /> <br /> Bane: In addition to the rules for Revenants, Waisenkind can be affected by certain Animalism powers (Feral Whispers and Summon the Hunt) of anyone they hold Vinculum towards. <br /> <br /> Ability: Waisenkind do receive one aspect of Protean that is always on display, determined by how the child died.<br /> <br /> Fashion of Death: Predatory Aspect p139-140 (Unnatural Aspect p140)<br /> Cold/Exposure: Patagia (Wings)<br /> Wildlife/Poisoned: Claws (Horrid Talons)<br /> Drowning/Suffocation: Aquatic (Rubbery Flesh)<br /> Falling/Crushed: Wall Crawling (Hooked Hands)<br /> Thirst/Starvation: Pack Vocals* (Pack Threat **)<br /> <br /> * Pack Vocals: The Waisenkind develops the capability to howl, screech or sing across long distances. These can only encompass very basic primal communications (Danger, Help, Food, Pain, Trapped). <br /> <br /> ** Pack Threat: These vocals can now also be used to threaten or intimidate other vampires. The Waisenkind may lash out using the bestial aspect, rolling Strength plus the combined BP of all Waisenkind in the immediate location.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:20:51-07:00","id":846673,"title":"","content":"161) One night, the players awaken to find that each of them has about five to ten mortals waiting patiently in their Havens. These mortals calmly obey any commands given to them by their Kindred (and are immune to mental powers used by others), genuinely have no idea where they came from, and seem to regard their Kindred as a god worthy of total submission and veneration.<br /> <br /> Also, their irises are gold, and their veins pump smoke instead of blood. Might want to start looking into why.<br /> <br /> 162) The players are newly Embraced Kindred. Their Sires have introduced them to the laws and rules of Kindred life, they've been accepted as a member of their Covenants, and they are now attending their first Elysium as full citizens of the Domain.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, every vampire in the city who's been dead for more than 50 years screams and bursts into dust.<br /> <br /> Now the city is thrown into chaos, as everyone and their dog struggles to fill the nascent power vacuum left by the death of all Elders and all but the youngest of Ancilla. And just what the sam hill killed all of them, and how do you stop it from happening again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:00:39-07:00","id":846687,"title":"","content":"163) It started out subtle. Just some stray thoughts or blurry hallucinations in your peripheral vision. Nothing to be concerned about, you were probably just over worked. But then it got worse as the thoughts began to take on a will of their own. When you tried to push them away, they <i>fought back</i>. The hallucinations likewise began to step into clearer view, their images becoming sharper and more defined. Then you find out it's not just you, but the rest of your coterie are having similar problems. But it wasn't until the last city meeting that you found out the source of these distractions.<br /> <br /> Your entire coterie has been infected, you've all become Malkavians and your sense of reality is collapsing with every passing night. You don't know how to stop its progress, and you can't think of anybody who's managed to find a cure. So what do you do when nobody in your group is able to tell reality from imagination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T01:25:05-07:00","id":848046,"title":"","content":"164) Heart in Your Mouth<br /> <br /> When one of your characters gets a Covenant-granted holding, some kind of long-established but minor property asset to utilize or guard, the place is an unexceptional example of its kind... with the exception of repeated minor items of architectural wear and tear. If repaired, the damage reasserts itself- there's something wrong in the building's orientation. If investigated, this eventually reveals a long-escalating sublimation in the surface the building rests on. If left alone, during a major rainstorm part of the basement folds up and drops into a hole in the ground. Regardless of how it's reached, eventually a long-secreted series of non-blueprinted chambers below the ground are revealed.<br /> <br /> The chambers were added after the building's construction, secretly, but the damage has been so severe it's all but impossible now to tell how anyone got in or out. Virtually nothing salvageable remains; decades of gradual exposure to the city's flood-drains have washed away or rotted beyond recognition almost everything. Most of what's left are piles of storm-dross, warped fragments of furnishings, and waterlogged bricks of pulp that used to be boxes of files.<br /> <br /> <i>Oh</i>, and the heads.<br /> <br /> A recessed steel shelf contains a half-dozen withered heads, with what turn out to be a strip of their own spine and viscera wrapped around their hearts, then stuffed into their mouths. An attached credenza has protected enough of the notes to make broadly clear what happened, and how- the heads are stripped-down kindred, <i>possibly still in Torpor</i>. Why anyone would want to be able to fit a city's worth of slumbering vampires into a single broom closet is anyone's guess, though. There is no discernible hint as to who would do this, except probably &quot;anyone who had access to this Covenant asset long enough to build a secret room.&quot;<br /> <br /> Leaving alone how the characters choose to respond to this , there's one last twist; if they reveal the discovery, the Covenant <i>rapidly </i>tries to bury the whole thing. The site represents fairly solid circumstantial evidence that one of their own was, at one point, not just involved in grisly, illegal research, but research in the <i>wrong kind </i>of blood magic; a little brick chapel reveals reams of broken alchemical glassware, or that little Mystery Play theater has tattered parchment ribbons inked with pre-Druidic runes, or a private corporate parking garage contains what are, unmistakably, Night Doctor implements. Whatever insight the Covenant could gain from investigating this madman's experiments come with a potential side of serious and unpredictable political consequences, from without and within.<br /> <br /> If the characters are willing to risk losing their shiny new asset <i>and </i>brave that powder keg for the sake of valuable or levergable information, though (or, hell, for the sake of the poor bastards on the shelf), hey, more power to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 03-16-2016, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:03:52-07:00","id":858467,"title":"","content":"165) Getting Tanked<br /> <br /> A socialite is holding a Mandrake tasting, and taking the opportunity to present a new product.<br /> <br /> It's... different. Not <i>bad</i>, certainly, but peculiar, with tones of what more experienced tasters describe as acid, swampy, gamy, or salty. It's crazy cheap, though, and no weird side-effects.<br /> <br /> It's from coral*. A huge, rusty-colored, fast-growing, aquacultured, obscure Indian Ocean coral, in a series of tanks filling a whole basement. It's ridiculously delicate and expensive to maintain, but it also produces an order of magnitude more Mandrake than equivalent expense for another variety. The vintner obviously doesn't want the secret getting out, both to protect their investment and their innovation, and to keep the competition in the dark, and because your product getting nicknamed Chum-Juice is bad for business.<br /> <br /> The fact that the whole business venture could <i>also</i> be described as &quot;basically ghouling a large colony of invertebrate predators with stinging tentacles and bodies covered with rough, horny blades, then leaving them unsupervised all day&quot; probably won't occur to anybody for a while, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> *specifically the unusually aggressive symbiotic algae making up part <i>of</i> the coral","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 04-04-2016, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:58:41-07:00","id":860390,"title":"","content":"166) <br /> <br /> The gang wars in the city are getting on abnormal proportions even the cops are starting to use high grade military equipment. Said gang war is becoming a problem for... everyone. It's harder to feed, it's harder to conduct business, people that would be embraced are being killed. It's a problem for every one.<br /> <br /> A older member of the carthians wants the PCs to solve the matter. Said older member is also a fan of gruesome killings but you can solve the problem in anyway you want. <br /> <br /> The culprit or culprits for this can be one of many. Maybe a gangrel killed the wrong person and this lead to a gang war? A mistake that we all could make. Maybe some mekhet made the war scalate to such levels to have a easier time feeding? Hunger can take us to such lengths. Maybe some Ventrue decided that this small scale war would move the economy to his favor? Greed and Ventrue walk side by side. Or some thing that is not a kindred? Fate? Hunters? Who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11165-tangledvirus","name":"TangledVirus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T00:11:22-07:00","id":900744,"title":"","content":"167) ...That Ought To Crawl<br /> <br /> An Ordo researcher has failed to come out of a regularly scheduled torpor on time. Upon investigation, his resting site bears... inconclusive suggestions of some kind of broad-area destructive force that left behind only traces of old blood and tiny bits of cloth.<br /> <br /> The first twist is that they were murdered. The researcher was working on developing some kind of Vitae-friendly necrophage worm, God knows why, which their assistant liberally sprinkled on the torpid corpse.<br /> <br /> The second twist is the reason there's no body is because it <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheWormThatWalks\" target=\"_blank\">got up and left</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 05-27-2016, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T14:53:16-07:00","id":903029,"title":"","content":"168) Your covenant is in an uproar. Your primogen has gone missing. For whatever reason you are sent to the sheriff to report this and aid in the investigation. Upon arriving at Elysium to find the sheriff you discover that you are not alone in your worries; The entire primogen has been destroyed, and many suspect the prince himself of masterminding the ordeal. The sheriff puts you on a team with members of the other covenants and order you to investigate the matter. You report only to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T17:46:06-07:00","id":906080,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Plot hook 169) A Mekhet elder with an interest in technology has been attempting to use Twilight l Projection as a means of listening in on phone calls and internet messaging. Unfortunately, his experiments have left him Hollow and his reflection is now somehow residing in the internet. The reflection has been sending emails to the elder\u2019s enemies with humiliating details of the elder\u2019s plans and past sins. It also was able to completely wipe out the elder\u2019s bank accounts leaving him near penniless. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The elder approaches the coterie with two tasks. Find out how to get rid of this reflection by any means possible before it does anything else to hurt him. Second, find a way to get his money back. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Quest Hint: The elder has heard rumors from his sire\u2019s second childe\u2019s primogen\u2019s ghoul that there is reclusive member of an obscure Mekhet bloodline called the Lynx in the players\u2019 city. The Lynx may be able to help the coterie...for a price, of course.)</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T17:48:08-07:00","id":906083,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Plot hook 170)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The crazy homeless man on the corner is preaching about the end of the world again. He\u2019s been there, every night, saying the same garbage for the last ten years. He must have gotten some of his bible verses confused because tonight he\u2019s talking about blood turning into water. Lo and behold, every Kindred in the city, no matter if drinking a blood pack or straight from the vein, only gets a half of the vitae they consume. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The next night the man talks about vermin getting the scent of tainted blood. Rats, frogs, bats, and assorted vermin hound the Kindred throughout the city. Somehow they only seem to be attracted to the undead, leaving the kine unharmed. The third night the vampires wake up at night to ticks, lice, and mosquitoes swarming on them. Though small there are a lot of them and they drain what little vitae they managed to procure the last couple nights. As an added bonus the vitae makes the insects resistant to regular bug sprays. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">According to the bible there are 7 plagues left. The Prince wants this homeless prophet brought in for interrogation. The problem is that the Prince has already sent two coteries on this same task. The one survivor of these missions tells that the prophet called upon the name of God and burnt the coterie members to ash with the light of the sun in the middle of the night. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T18:22:11-07:00","id":906100,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">171) Prince Werner of Baltimore has sent nearly every Kindred in Washington DC a text, email, letter, or astrally projected message. It simply states \u201cPrince Damien Cruze of Washington DC is hereby considered a traitor to all Kindred. Any who present his person or verified remains to Alexandria Werner, Prince of Baltimore, will receive citizenship, prime hunting territory, and ten million dollars in cash or wire transfer.\u201d Prince Damien has disappeared. Some say he\u2019s gathering allies to declare war on Baltimore. Other\u2019s say he\u2019s hiding from his own subjects. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Normally, blood hunts don\u2019t apply to elders, and especially not to princes. They\u2019re the ones who know where all the bodies are buried and have spent their unlives cultivating allies and slaves. Even then, the prince himself has got to be an apex predator to survive as long as he has. There\u2019s no way that anyone is going to go against Prince Damien and win...right? And w</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">hat did Prince Damien do to piss his neighboring ruler off?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T20:15:09-07:00","id":906150,"title":"","content":"<b>172)</b> It doesn't happen often; so when it does, it tends to turn heads. The Prince of the city is unaligned, swearing allegiance to no authority but himself, and somehow he's managed to keep his throne for over five decades! Recently, your coterie has stumbled upon evidence as to how he's able to maintain his authority. The Prince is a war monger, using his influence to manipulate the other covenants into feuding with each other, instead of rallying against him. The Prince knows you've learned his little secret, and has come to you with a proposal. He's finally grown paranoid of the other factions and wants them removed from his city. If the coterie works for him as double agents to tear their covenants (if applicable) down from the inside, he'll reward them handsomely for their efforts. Of course, there's also the possibility of acting as a triple agent and letting the other covenants know about the Prince's ambitious cull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:28:17-07:00","id":906832,"title":"","content":"173)<br /> Some of the Kindred of the city report an encounter with a darkly cloaked figure. Some of them remember teeth piercing their flesh, becoming paralyzed with euphoria so intense it prevented them from escaping, and dulling their senses to the environment. Afterwards they stumbled to their havens in a daze, awoke the next evening to grogginess, hunger, and tattered memories. One of the victims, a former blood doll who impressed her domitor enough to be granted the embrace, states that the feeling was exactly like the Kiss.<br /> So what creature is preying on vampires like the Kindred prey on humans? What does the Prince, the Primogen, the factions want done with this creature if it can even be found? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T07:55:23-07:00","id":907099,"title":"","content":"174) The Kindred of the city are being plagued by a cell of hunters that are actually managing to take down elders. Piece by piece, block by block, they are taking the city. How do they do so? This cell is composed of IRS Criminal Investigation Agents*, and they\u2019re going after the Kindred where it hurts the most; their wallets.<br /> <br /> Shell corporations are exposed for dirty business practices and suddenly the elder who spent five decades building up her fortune is left nearly penniless. Some foreclosure paperwork is mixed up and a primogen\u2019s bedroom wall is demolished by a wrecking ball at noon. Vampires needing a one way ticket out of town find that their credit cards are frozen. If they try to fly they\u2019re told they are listed on the do not fly list and won\u2019t you please come into this room with a window facing the eastern sky until a special agent and his buddies can arrive to sort this whole thing out.<br /> <br /> These agents are well connected, and are able to use their fellow officers as pawns in their schemes (parallels between parasitic elders and using neonates as pawns springs to mind). Worse, they\u2019re usually holed up in their offices in a heavily guarded government building that also houses the FBI, a component of the national guard, and the sheriff\u2019s office. At home they live in a cop neighborhood with a line of squad cars lining the street. Can the players do anything to stop these hunters? Or do the Kindred of the city give up and admit that they\u2019ve been beaten at their own game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T08:29:06-07:00","id":907113,"title":"","content":"175) The Village was a horrible movie, but vampires have never been known for having good taste. A group of Kindred have established a village/blood farm in the middle of nowhere. The hundred or so human inhabitants think the year is 1798 and have the technology level to match. The Kindred have accomplished this through taking orphans and drifters and using lots and lots of Dominate to rewrite everyone\u2019s memories and to condition the Two Rules; never bar a Kindly One from entering your home and taking what is theirs through the Kiss, and never enter the Kindly One\u2019s forest.<br /> <br /> The coterie stumbles upon this village. The kine seem happy enough. The Kindred seem to get their fill of precious blood very easily. Do they see the village as a sick form of slavery, the best thing since sliced bread, or a necessary evil? If they approach the local werewolves they find that the pack has been on good relations with the Kindred who established the village. They\u2019ve been very interested in finding out if keeping humans at a pre-industrial tech and cultural level affects the spirit world. So what do the players do?<br /> Twist: A changling motley has come to the area and are ready to free the inhabitants of the village from the True Fae\u2019s clutches.<br /> Double Twist: This entire charade has attracted the attentions of a True Fae. Things are about to get Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T08:47:07-07:00","id":907121,"title":"","content":"176) The coterie travels to a nearby city. They find Invictus elders and Carthian neonates engaged in lively but friendly debates. They see members of the Circle and the Lancea praying together. They hear lectures from Ordo Dragons detailing how the Coils can make Kindred not only more humane, but more fulfilled and better members of society. Elders share power and hunting ground with neonates, primogen work for the betterment of their constituents, the Prince is loved by all, and their hasn\u2019t been a death by over-feeding or from a vampire losing control to their Beast in thirty years.<br /> WHAT THE HELL IS GOING ON?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T17:36:13-07:00","id":907341,"title":"","content":"177) The Devil's Music<br /> You're checking out some sweet tunes on the internet one day when you come across a song by an obscure, local metal band called UnHoly NecroKings. Something about the lyrics catches your attention and soon enough you check out their album called Masquerade. It happens to be a concept album about a society of vampires and their nightly struggle against each other and themselves. You listen to the album and find out a great deal of it is about your coterie and the sins you thought you've hidden from the rest of the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T21:06:06-07:00","id":913211,"title":"","content":"178) <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">New Orleans Revolution no xp</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">starts off with a covenant of choice but at least one in Lancea Sanctum</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">You wake up feeling horrible. A wave of hunger rushes over you over you. You smell something in the air and it is familiar and mouth watering. It was the smell of blood. When you turned to the source of the smell there was a dog. You are famished and something compelled to attack the dog and you did. Maybe after a long personal fight with yourself before doing so but you did any way. The hunger was just too much to suffer through. When you attacked the dog fangs appeared in your mouth and you instinctively bite the dog, draining it of all of its blood. You are confused and started going through a surge of emotions. What happened? What am I? What did I just do? These questions and probably more have been going through your head as you drained the blood from the dog. When you finished drinking the blood a door opened. You were hesitant about going through the door at first but in the end it was the only way out and to find out what happened. As you leave your room you see others appear through doors all leading into the same room. You get a quick glimpse at each other before a screen turns on.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cWelcome my newborn children. You have a lot of questions so I will cut to the chase. I am in need of soldiers and that is you my children. Soldiers of darkness. denizens of the shadows. I hope yo learn to enjoy the unlife. You are now a kindred or more commonly known as vampires. My colleagues created you and they will destroy you if you disobey me. You will help me take control of New Orleans one step at a time. In due time we will meet in person and until then do not ask any unnecessary questions. Before you are five files, each containing information about one of the five covenants. My colleagues will help you get accepted into the covenant of your choice, though I suggest atlas one of you choose Lancea Sanctum. Those who do so will have the opportunity to be the most influential piece to the entire plan. Choose your covenant wisely. You have 48 hours to meet one of my colleagues or you will be terminated. You are free to use this place as a haven. Always find shelter to go to sleep when the sun comes up.\u201d after the message was done the screen turns off and the lights turn on revealing that the room was a dungeon and there was a door that opened above to your new home.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11945-shadow-walker","name":"Shadow Walker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T21:08:47-07:00","id":913214,"title":"","content":"179) Dogs. <br /> Well it's happened. Somehow the Curse has been spread beyond the human form. Maybe it was an elder's ghouled pets that died with vitae in their system. Maybe it was some Ordo science project. Either way a pack of feral dogs are undead. They haven't been hurting humans too much, preferring the vitae of other canines, similar to how the Kindred disdain the blood of animals. However stray dogs and even pets have started to go missing or have been found throughout the city torn apart. The dog population is down and the vampire dogs are starting to turn their sights on better tasting Vitae, from the Kindred themselves. <br /> These creatures are pack hunters and a lone Kindred would make easy prey. Some of the creatures have displayed physical disciplines and even Obsfucation. Worst of all are rumors that the canines numbers are growing. Perhaps they've found a way to Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T12:45:16-07:00","id":914993,"title":"","content":"180) Right, so my sire's sire's sire's great-granchilder's Avus knew this Gangrel who apparently had an in with a local werewolf pack (Apparently he was supposed to be one. Wolves are weird.) and they mopped up the blood-dog problem. Problem is, they were being egged on by an Owl, and apparently one of the wolves died and had their body possessed by the damn bird. Long and short, every vamp on the East Side is running crying or in that fucker's belly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T17:58:34-07:00","id":922951,"title":"","content":"181) Can the Strix fall in love? The idea itself is sheer lunacy, but recent circumstances has made it a pressing question. One of your friends/allies (mortal or Kindred) has recently acquired a stalker. Their email, phone, and social media are regularly bombarded with bloody, disturbed love poems, both written and voiced. Though the mannerisms and word choice remain the same, each few days it's a different voice. Sometimes pictures are sent, claiming to be from the stalker. Sometimes they're of the friend in a variety of vulnerable or private situations; other times, they claim to be of the stalker themselves. In the latter cases, those faces show up the next morning on the news as particularly gruesome suicides. More importantly to you is the fact that in all cases, the stalker's eyes appear a cruel, avian yellow. <br /> <br /> Has one of the Birds of Dis actually developed affection for another being, expressing it in its own twisted, monstrous way? Is this just some exercise in torture? Or is there something far more subtle and sinister afoot? Better figure out fast, because things are escalating; already the ally has walked into their home to find some poor soul beaten, bound, and drugged, tied up with a little ribbon and a note telling them to &quot;Have fun!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:21:27-07:00","id":923031,"title":"","content":"182) The city is a powder keg. The Carthians came to power decades ago after wiping out the Invictus, but the only things they have accomplished is instituting an only-somewhat functioning democratic system, and splintering into three separate factions who all hate each other's guts. Too bad they have this nasty habit of dragging the mortals into their squabbles. Crowds of rabid communists clash with mobs of out-and-proud fascists, and moderates vindictively play the system to make sure they stay comfy. Homelessness and unemployment is rising. Minority neighborhoods are one more bad day away from rioting. The Sanctified Bishop didn't leave his haven in the Puerto Rican neighborhood for six months, and only emerged to start meeting with the local Crone, who loudly proclaims dire portents for the city and all of its citizens. The Dragons just hope their bolt holes are deep enough, that their vaults are sturdy enough, to weather whatever storm is coming.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T13:05:35-07:00","id":923435,"title":"","content":"183)<br /> <br /> The prince's pet crafter of whimsical lethalities has made a wonderful new thing. It's a thing of elegance and beauty. A poem of engineering and ergonomics and occultism really- a rosewood, rowan, and figwood stake, driven by cunning little brass and tungsten innards. Once planted in a victim, it smoothly unfolds itself deeper into the wound, inexorably towards and through the heart, unless removed. More amazing still, the runes exposed on the interior metallic surfaces compel the victim's Vitae against its own sympathies, and spill to the ground in rebellion.<br /> <br /> Everybody but its creator is more worried about the fact that the prince's prototype fire-and-forget stake has been stolen, and the fact that it can put you in Torpor and slurp you dry at the same time.<br /> <br /> Followup Twist- things become much worse when an Amaranth'd vampire's leavings indicate that the extraction point was directly through the ribs, from the heart. Apparently the thing was also secretly designed to be... basically a powered straw, for Diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T14:49:06-07:00","id":925052,"title":"","content":"184) It was supposed to be an iron-clad alliance. The Invictus drove out the Carthians when they tried to launch their little coup in the 50s, and they declared the triumph of order and hierarchy over anarchy and democracy. Less than a decade later, the Ordo Dracul threw down with the Circle over some theological dispute that turned ugly, and the Kogaion himself personally slew the Crone; when the dust settled, the Defiant said it proved the superiority of reason and secularism over the lunatic gibbering of a mad goddess. The Lancea et Sanctum saw its numbers shrink to less than a dozen in the aftermath; it was a new order, one ruled by secular logic, with no room for any gods or prophets muddying the waters. <br /> <br /> The First Estate cozied up to the Defiant quickly, congratulating each other on vanquishing their respective philosophical rivals. High-ranking members of the Invictus started encouraging childer without the necessary aptitude for cutthroat politics to pledge themselves to the Dragons, as a safer alternative to being a flailing sardine in a pool of barracudas. The Dragons, for their part, began performing Scales of the Dragon for Invictus members in exchange for boons. The Lancea et Sanctum muddled along, taking in any neonates who were cast aside, or ancillae who suffered a fall from grace that would otherwise be fatal. <br /> <br /> All that changed a couple months ago, when important texts disappeared from Ordo safe houses. The Invictus publicly scolded the Defiant for such carelessness, and it seemed like the Ordo had suffered a permanent diminishment in standing. Then, six nights ago, the Sanctified Bishop marched into Elysium, with the culprits at hand: two members of the city's police department, ghouls by the Sheriff, and ordered to steal the texts by their regnant. Elysium exploded into finger-pointing and dire accusations. The Dragons swore dire repercussions against the Sheriff and any who had knowledge of the plot; the Invictus, for their part, have remained tight-lipped, and mixed coteries are suddenly bereft of their Invictus members, replaced instead by Sanctified who shake their heads at the consequences of godless ambition, and hint that the theft was but the first act of a string of betrayals decades in the planning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:58:58-07:00","id":928780,"title":"","content":"185) One and a half centuries ago Patrick Brighton rode to war for the Union against the forces of secession. He was issued a warhorse named Chestnut by his regimental quartermaster. At the killing fields of Shiloh he was Embraced by a vagabond Kindred who saw something of worth in the wounded and dying young officer. His first act after learning about the power of the vitae was to ghoul his loyal warhorse. From that night onward Brighton and Chestnut remained together through wars, Kindred politics, the Depression, and societal upheaval. All throughout that century and a half Brighton has remained dedicated to Chestnut, making sure the horse gets plenty of exercise, feeding her a living meal whenever she's feeling the urge for blood, and making sure she is treated with a level of decadence most Daeva would balk at.<br /> And now Chestnut is dead. Murdered.<br /> Brighton is livid as only an elder can be. He's made a city-wide announcement to the Kindred as well as the lupines in the countryside; 20 million dollars, a mansion in the suburbs, and a favor for the capture of whomever did this deed to his beloved ghoul.<br /> <br /> 186) Patrick Brighton has gone off the deep end since his ghoul was killed. He's been taking out his aggression on the kine, giving his mind and soul to the Beast with each atrocity he commits. The Prince approaches the coterie, and tells them to find a way to curb the worst of Brighton's excesses before his friend becomes a draugr with the all the strength and cunning of an elder.<br /> <br /> 187) Involving the lupines in Kindred politics was one thing but now Brighton is sending messages to the merlins, changelings, and stranger beings. The Prince is livid, seeing this as an open invitation for other factions to try to take over his city and disrupt the carefully constructed society of Kindred politics. The coterie is deputized by the sheriff to patrol the city and make sure the any other supernaturals get packing or end up in a grave.<br /> <br /> 188) Brighton's reckless actions have caused enough disruption. Kill him. Brighton has connections outside of the city and they may try to retaliate if they find the Prince has had a hand in Brighton's death, so make it quiet. The Prince even offers to conduct a ritual to remove any black lines on any coterie member's aura after the deed is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11901,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","user":"Icon787","date":". 07-09-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T16:00:28-07:00","id":928929,"title":"","content":"I like 185-188.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T16:24:42-07:00","id":928944,"title":"","content":"189) Monster Garage, a dingy local auto repair shop, has a secret and extremely profitable business chopping up stolen cars and modifying vehicles for criminal purposes- including those of the Kindred. Sunproof retractable window shutters, RVs with lead-lined hidden compartments, choppers fit for a Bruja, it's all there. But when a group of rebellious vamps start using their tricked out cars for street racing, it's only a matter of time before the chaos and crashes attract attention from the police- and others.<br /> <br /> (RE #2, turning vampires back into humans would go against what most of the Ordo want, as well. So an Ordo scientist who developed something like that would have his own covenant after him as well.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 07-09-2016, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:09:16-07:00","id":928989,"title":"","content":"(Are multiple posts okay? I know they usually aren't, but I don't want to break the one hook per post rule.)<br /> <br /> 190) There's a draugr on the loose, mercilessly attacking his victims and either draining them dry or leaving them at death's door. But he uses an ingenious defense that makes him hard to track down- he's always been sighted in full Elvis impersonator costume, meaning that neither the human authorities or the Prince will take sightings of &quot;The King&quot; seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:09:48-07:00","id":928990,"title":"","content":"191) The corporate headquarters of a powerful and far-reaching company are located in your city. This particular corporation is also completely vamped up- its board and executives are made up entirely of vampires, ghouls, and blood dolls. So when a federal investigation uncovers massive corruption and criminal activity, the Kindred of the city must rush to cover up as much of their involvement as possible, lest their secret world be exposed by the IRS. But how did the Feds get all this information anyway? And how did they get their case pushed through so fast, when it's usually notoriously hard to nail corporations for shady business practices?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:10:19-07:00","id":928991,"title":"","content":"192) A VII assassin is on a rampage with a truly dangerous weapon. They carry a compact crossbow loaded with aerodynamic bolts containing some sort of chemical that causes the target to come alight almost instantly, with flames that burn like napalm. And things get even worse when someone starts leaving these devices around the city like party favors, so everyone from Neonates to hobos could be packing a &quot;hotshot&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:10:51-07:00","id":928992,"title":"","content":"193) redroom.com is a schoolyard legend, one of the &quot;death sites&quot; that pops up in modern web-savvy folklore. Supposedly, you can type in the name of someone in this website that appears only at midnight, and the next night they'll be attacked and drained of all blood. Not only are these hits being carried out, but the younger kindred find the website to be even more disturbing. It really does only appear at midnight and it's impossible to hack or trace, meaning that whoever is running it isn't just a merciless Beast-ridden serial killer, they're also one hell of a programmer. And why would a vampire set a site like that up anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:11:22-07:00","id":928993,"title":"","content":"194) There's a young crusading politician running for office, and he's getting the Prince worried. His rhetoric about cleaning up the town and fighting corruption is familiar, but something about the way he phrases it makes the kindred fairly uncomfortable- he talks about &quot;burning out the infection&quot;, &quot;taking on the leeches and parasites sucking this city's blood&quot;, and &quot;driving a stake through the heart of the forces who think they can control us&quot;. Not only that, but his staff has proven impossible to penetrate or corrupt, and a Mekhet elder using Auspex Five swears he went to spy on him but ran into some sort of invisible wall around his hotel room. What's more, the Kindred could swear there's something...off about him. The people at his rallies don't look right, the way they stare at him all glassy-eyed, never looking away, always falling silent as soon as he talks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:11:56-07:00","id":928994,"title":"","content":"195) There's a new cryptid in town, one that's being sighted across the U.S. People are calling it the Midnight Mothman, since it resembles a nocturnal, black version or the infamous monster of Point Pleasant. This creature seems to share the mothman's oracular tendencies, but the Kindred are realizing that the places it's been sighted all have some connection to their world- business they control, havens of elders, and so on. And they aren't the only ones- groups of hunters have started to follow the creature across the country, since it seems to lead them right to sights of vampire activity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:16:29-07:00","id":928997,"title":"","content":"196) No one in the city remembers. In times long ago, before even the american revolution, the city's Kindred launched all out war against the Rotgrafen, driving them from its ports and haranguing them across the east coast of the americas. Since then, the Kindred government of the city has undergone several complete turnovers, and no one left remembers what drove the original Kindred rulers to wage all out war against the corsairs. The Rotgrafen remember, though, and they've been building their forces for centuries to finally avenge their defeat. The city is about to face a full naval assault, and its inhabitants have no idea it's coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-13-2016, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T18:23:32-07:00","id":929001,"title":"","content":"197) The Elder has started telling a story. It's meandering, makes no sense, it's long as hell, and you're pretty sure it's literally driving you insane to listen to. The problem? You're locked in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T21:25:54-07:00","id":929046,"title":"","content":"&quot;So I tied an onion to my belt, which was the style at the time...&quot;<br /> <br /> 198) Surveillance is bad news for vampires (and, really, any other non-ephemeral supernatural creature). It hasn't quite progressed to the point it has in our world, and that's partially because vampires use their sway in politics to push through plenty of anti-surveillance and anti-drone legislature. But the governments of the world are only going to take this for so long. One group of vampires believes they've found a devil's deal solution, and have been in covert meetings with powerful politicians: various national governments and even the UN itself pass powerful anti-surveillance laws, but in exchange groups of vampires have to agree to act as secret police for the various governments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T21:29:35-07:00","id":929048,"title":"","content":"199) There's a contest afoot, but it isn't a normal one. All around the city, and even farther away, a few select vampires have received covert messages about an ancient artifact being held under high security within the city. The messages say where the treasure is, followed by the statement: &quot;Gather anything and anyone you need and then stake your claim. Those that succeed shall win my interest.&quot; It isn't long before rumors start to swirl that the Phantom Queen, a legendary Mekhet known as the world's greatest thief, set off the odd contest to recruit a protege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T21:32:34-07:00","id":929050,"title":"","content":"200) A group of Iron Masters show up at Elysium one night, making it abundantly clear that they're there for diplomatic purposes. They want to establish a clear, written treaty and territory agreement with the Prince, and possibly even encourage vampire-werewolf cooperation. Things grow even more tense as negotiations proceed from night to night. Elements on both sides might not want the deal to go through. And what about the rumors that the werewolves are doing this because they believe the city is facing some menace so deadly that they require the help of the vampire community to repel it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T20:48:43-07:00","id":932364,"title":"","content":"201) Your husband is being embezzled by one of his people; the plot appears to be originated by a rival noble to gain political capital from the Prince. In order to discover proof of this embezzlement and to whom it is going to, the player(s) must follow the trail of money and couriers throughout the city. Success means your husband gains power in the city and possibly wealth, whereas failure means your husband's business is ruined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12112-dspayr","name":"dspayr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T11:06:26-07:00","id":944950,"title":"","content":"202). The nos were raiding an abandoned office building downtown for supplies when they found something interesting on the computers. seems the defunct company had a number of underground research facilities around the tri-county area, with populations of researchers who lived their with their families. The company was working on some high end stuff in those bunkers that could really be useful to the kindred. Problem is, the company lost contact with the underground labs right before they went under and the haunts have decided they might need some back up if they go dungeon crawling, backup like your coterie.<br /> <br /> (that's right, VtR dungeon crawls in the style of the vaults from fallout, you're welcome.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T12:11:45-07:00","id":944992,"title":"","content":"The Queen is dead. She met Final Death last night, supposedly from wounds inflicted on her by an animal (but what kind of animal can do that to a centuries-old Gangrel?). Tonight, her ancilla childe took Praxis with the backing of the Ventrue Priscus, a man whose Requiem began before the United States was even envisioned. Everybody but the new Prince knows who really rules the city now. The Prince's first order of business: the execution of his sire's Seneschal, the Priscus of Clan Gangrel and Hierarch of the Circle of the Crone. The Circle is in an uproar, and the Hierophant's childe has rebelled against the new Prince. The Queen's brothers have both declared their intention of seizing Praxis. Civil war is upon the city, and nobody heads the warnings of the Watchmen, who speak of owls, and shrill cries on the air. If the Strix are coming, they may find that the Kindred have already destroyed themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T15:29:48-07:00","id":948116,"title":"","content":"204) Something interesting has been found, an underground temple of sorts where Kindred fall in to torpor and awaken with one higher Blood Potency and the Tainted Condition as thou they had consumed a BP 10 kindred. The Dragons want access and the Sanctified want it closed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:20:00-07:00","id":949845,"title":"","content":"205) Owls, owls, owls. Last month, the city voted to change the state bird to an owl. The new minor league team that moved in has an owl mascot. The big up and coming street gang calls themselves &quot;The Owls&quot;. The damn things are everywhere...but there's no Strix activity that anyone can find. Is someone in the know trying to freak out the Kindred? Why, and what kind of strings are they pulling to orchestrate so many seeming coincidences?<br /> <br /> 206) The All Night Society has always maintained a carefully crafted web of agreements and proxies with the local sewer and utility workers, making sure that the various subterranean haunts of the city's Kindred remain undisturbed. But the city's just signed over their maintenance contracts to a new private firm, so the entire protective network needs to be reestablished, and quickly- before the workers find something they shouldn't, or another power gets them in its pocket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-13-2016, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T16:46:33-07:00","id":957924,"title":"","content":"207) a group of government workers and contractors in the local homeland security sector, all of them puppets of one powerful local elder, managed to kill each other in a Mexican standoff turned massive shootout at a famous local landmark that has made national headlines due to the shocking public violence and the alleged corruption that lead to the shootout. Bizarrely enough, Their master was not involved in this mess at all, the whole thing seems to have been the result of competing unrelated private agendas of the agents, who don't seem to have known that the others were working for the same kindred but that doesn't change the fact that the attention from the shootout is drawing suspicion toward the elder from the media and authorities investigating the mess. The elder is offering a great boon to whoever can lead the investigation away from them, and preferably find out exactly what their puppets were doing behind their back in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T15:52:44-07:00","id":960064,"title":"","content":"208) The Carthians aren't the biggest proponents of ghouling mortals. Some of them view it as too similar to the caste system that the Invictus try to impose. But now Premier Kristina has issued a command to all Carthians in her domain; find a mortal in the next two weeks, ghoul her, and present her at next weeks Elysium for the beginning of their training. She explains that this is to bolster their forces as she expects an attack from the Invictus of a nearby domain within the next few months. If the Carthians want to hold their territory their going to need every weapon they can get. <br /> She says that this is better than a mass forced embrace as it won't put any strain on hunting grounds or territories, and if the hapless ghouls end up dead in the coming conflict, well, there's always more of the Kine around. Of course this is recruitment for a potential invasion. Don't just pick up any soft-eyed blood doll to give your precious vitae to. <br /> So how does your coterie decide who to enslave with the blood bonds? Is there any moral concern about mass enslaving members of the Kine? What about using them as cannon fodder? And how the hell does the Premier know what the Invictus the next city over are planning?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:18:11-07:00","id":965001,"title":"","content":"209) It's war. It started over a simple misstep by the agents of an Inviticus elder who were running a people trafficking ring and picked up a ghoul or herd member only for her owner to reclaim her (who knew Dragons could Blood Simplify their thralls?) and may have expressed his displeasure with fire (the order of events is disputed but he claims the kidnappers knew she was owned). Few kindred dispute that letting the words Invitus and 1st Estate along with the elders name reach the police investigation was going a bit far.<br /> Just when it looked like the matter was going to be settled (by ignoring the younger party and telling him to shut up) the matriarch of his dynasty announced that of course the Circle would assist the Ordo in getting proper compensation and the Carthians set things rolling the next night.<br /> No one knows the sides, no one knows if it's hot or cold, no one knows where the church stands and no one really knows the facts but someone needs to win so we can end this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 09-12-2016, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:21:46-07:00","id":968779,"title":"","content":"210) The Prince sends you out to investigate a bizarre anomaly in the city, one where physics aren't working as they should. When your group finally makes it to the epicenter, a bizarre wave of energy engulfs you, and you find yourselves stranded in a parallel city. Not only that, but the process seems to have disrupted you on a quantum level, and now each of you no longer craves blood, but has become a different sort of vampire: psychic energy, spinal fluid, electricity...can you find a way back home while coping with these strange new hungers?<br /> <br /> (Would be a good excuse to let the players learn some rare/homebrew Disciplines or Devotions based on the experience)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:29:49-07:00","id":968785,"title":"","content":"211) &quot;Little Annie&quot; is the media's current obsession. People all over America are glued to their TV sets following the story of this orphan runaway from a cruel foster family, and all the news channels are circling like mutant shark-vulture hybrids for some bit of information. Unfortunately, this all went down in your city, and you've got information that she ran into the labyrinth of sewer tunnels and catacombs under the city, which most residents don't even know exist. Even the Nosferatu aren't sure how deep they go. So the Prince organizes a search for the lost child, because if the media finds out where she ran, an army of searchers and reporters are going to descend on the dark haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T05:17:41-07:00","id":969154,"title":"","content":"212) The Circle of the Crone has never been known for cohesive organization, nor popularity among the other covenants. But this new cult has been gaining power at an uncomfortably fast rate. Investigations have concluded that the cult is derived from Aztec faiths, using Cruac to perform the horrifying sacrifices performed by the lost civilization. But the real bad news is that the Aztecs were a warrior civilization, and those who have been sent to deal with them have found that the Circle has far more than just blood magic to defend themselves. The more recent attacks against them have stirred things up. The Circle has been making not so subtle advances on the other covenants, abducting their allies and contacts, and using them to power their rituals, slowly working their way up to the top brass until they become the dominate Covenant in the domain.<br /> <br /> As a young (no older than ancilla) vampire, you are faced with conflict in the upcoming war. Friend, Foe or Sacrifice, anyone of these could be your fate, and you probably won't get a second chance to pick once the war gets into full swing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:03:29-07:00","id":969478,"title":"","content":"213) Night 83. We still don't know what exactly happened. I finally managed to make contact with Father Simpson. He seems to be the only survivor of Mother Veneficia's Night Mass. He says that in the middle of Mother Veneficia's sermon, a figure with metallic wings and swords for hands appeared hovering above the congregation. It proclaimed that the Lord had tired of our predation on humanity, and would now cleanse the city of us. The entire church burst into flame, even the stonework, and then many beings like the first appeared, and began killing every vampire in sight. Father Simpson was consumed with frenzy and fled. <br /> <br /> We have had similar reports from the other covenants. The heathens of the Circle of the Crone... the heretics of the Ordo Dracul... the rabble of the Carthian Movement... the gentry of the Invictus... all had a gathering on the same night, and those few who attended and survived reported similar figures, and similar words spoken, and similar aftermaths. Lester the Seneschal says that similar events happened at the Prince's Haven that night. <br /> <br /> There has been no Elysium. No Midnight Mass. It was nights before my childe and I could bring ourselves to venture out of our Haven, and only then to feed lightly from a handful of mortals. But when we returned, our Haven was in flames. We have been moving from shelter to shelter from night to night. Clair Novak of the Carthians claims that the &quot;angels&quot; do not attack if she slumbers in places where humans come and go during the day. The thought of stability and safety is tempting, but how could we possibly dwell among humans? The risk of discovery is astronomical. How?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:33:58-07:00","id":969494,"title":"","content":"214) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/967098-5-things-for-a-mage-to-encounter?p=969219#post969219\">An obscure flashlight-App for a cellphone that has a single five star review written in a strange indecipherable gibberish. When the App is used the light it produces acts as functionally identical to sunlight against things with vulnerabilities to sunlight.</a> Since the light is directional it has begun to prove problematic due to a teenager Ordo Dracul discovering it and sharing the secret of its existence among the local Ordo in exchange for status among her Covenant. The Apps reviews are already awful, as if there is already a campaign to keep it from becoming popular.<br /> <br /> Any vampire that isn't &quot;in&quot; on the secret simply knows that there is a teenage Ordo Dracul Deva has used her cell phone flashlight to blast the face of a particularly cruel and powerful Circle of the Crone Nosferotu that was quote-unquote &quot;Creeping on her&quot; for severe burns. It is rumored to be a Coil-Majesty Devotion or that the phone is a magical artifact, or maybe a magical artifact that requires a Devotion to use or the girl has a literal guardian angel able to inflict Godly Wrath upon those that threaten her.<br /> <br /> Actually the girl was embraced because she was part of a tech savvy Hunter Cell and was then used to eliminate the cell because it was literally her un-life or their lives. The Cell heard about the App via rumor on something called Network Zero. The App itself is the source of the power, the cell phone being just a way to run the App. The source of the App is a mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-14-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:58:58-07:00","id":969659,"title":"","content":"<b>215)</b> There's a new vampire on the scene who's garnered a mysterious reputation. Word around the domain is that this kindred appears to be honest and forthright in his dealings with others. He doesn't lie, doesn't cheat, and doesn't manipulate. If he sends you on a suicide mission, he makes sure you know the risks before doing so. He also seems to be genuinely happy and charismatic without having to utelize Disciplines to compel the minds of others. Which may explain why so many neonates and fledglings have taken a liking to the guy after only a few days associating with him.<br /> <br /> When these fledglings began to reject their Sires in favor of following this newcomer, many Elders were displeased. But the latest information to leak their way has them seeing red with anger. Mr. Popularity is one of the Brood, and those who flock around him are corrupted into the service of his demonic cult. Many young and inexperienced vampires have already fallen victim to demonic influences, and if the cult isn't stamped out immediately, the domain could see a full scale invasion on its hands!<br /> <br /> <br /> That's where you come in. He won't approach any of the elders, claiming they're too paranoid to have a civil discussion with. But he will approach you, thinking your coterie is still relatively young by vampire standards. Your mission is to infiltrate the Brood as double agents and destroy the cult from the inside out. But once you're behind enemy lines, you begin to hear the The Call, and it only becomes more incessant the longer it takes you to complete your mission. Can you hold onto your soul long enough to purge these demons from your land, or will you sell your soul for tainted power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-15-2016, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:55:21-07:00","id":970694,"title":"","content":"216) Urban planning and expansion being what it it in about 3 years two cities will becom one. Where as this is great news for the local economy and what not with new homes being built and stuff the local kindred haven't got any agreements in place yet, in fact they don't know much for sure about the new city.<br /> Will our heroes volunteer to travel to meet the new neighbours, try and claim that new feeding ground or seek to sell their services to those of more ambition?<br /> Possible complications include.<br /> The new domain although smaller is near exclusively one covenant.<br /> 20 years ago a settlement/recon force was sent out to this city, a message was delivered by crow telling the prince that if this wasn't intended as an act of aggression he had chosen his envoys poorly and any intrusions across the river would be seen as an act of war, the new city has already expanded past the river.<br /> Strix/VII/Brood etc.<br /> One city has been keeping its population down so every kindred has plentiful feeding territory and does not wish to share with it's &quot;frivolous&quot; neighbours, war is coming.<br /> The one kindred in town who came from this city has skipped town telling his friends that they too should dig in or get out.<br /> All envoys sent disappear, the domain seems empty and yet it clearly isn't safe.<br /> The other city is very ready, they know all about their new neighbours and are ready to hit them hard, there will be a prince of their choosing on the throne or blood on the streets.<br /> Feel free to invert any complications if you prefer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 09-16-2016, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:46:36-07:00","id":970805,"title":"","content":"<b>217)</b> Teeth as long as steak knives, eyes solid white and big as a man's fist, an elongated jaw that stretches to the chest, claws like hooks, hair like tentacles and wings like a crow. That is the description a Ghoul managed to give about the monster that attacked and devoured his Nosferatu master in the dark alleyway they often frequented. According to his report, the creature just dropped from the sky, grabbed his master by the shoulders and chomped down on him without a word of explanation! When it had finished it's meal, it turned and screamed at the Ghoul before spreading its wings and soaring back into the sky.<br /> <br /> This is not the first instance of random attacks on kindred society, it's just the first time somebody managed to give a description of the attacker. Whatever this thing is, it targets vampires specifically, attacks them completely unprovoked, and flees immediately afterward. And with the ability to fly, it's almost impossible to predict where it will strike next. Which has the kindred of the city jumping at shadows as paranoia begins to set in. And that's when the court is approached by a strange group of teenagers who wish to offer their assistance in getting their wayward &quot;sister&quot; under control!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-16-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T14:30:52-07:00","id":980432,"title":"","content":"218) Dirty Laundry<br /> Every night for the last four weeks, between 2am and 3am (Eastern Standard Time) there is a live web stream called Dirty Laundry. It can be found just by making a search of the title. Despite many, many attempts to remove the sites and the mirrors hosting this stream, another one and another one always seems to pop up. The Masquerade seems to be secure as any mortal, ghoul, mage, or lupine that is shown the stream only sees a black screen and only hears a faint static. As far as anyone can tell only Kindred can see the show.<br /> <br /> The stream itself shows two well-dressed news anchors, a nosferatu and daeva. They report on Kindred politics at a variety of locations. Most importantly, their information appears to be incredibly accurate. They\u2019ve already exposed schemes that have left the Prince of Orlando deposed, a covenant in Santa Fe completely wiped out, several coteries along the west coast turning nomad, and a Lancea Bishop committing suicide.<br /> Some Kindred think this is the best thing since bottled blood. Others say that this news station needs to be destroyed for the good of all. Others are on the fence seeing the inherent risk, but enjoying the manipulative elders being exposed for all to see.<br /> So what do you want to do?<br /> <br /> <br /> 219) Dirty Laundry 2: Even Dirtier<br /> After a few days of trying of trying to investigate the web cast you get an email. It\u2019s from someone named Cicero says they are looking to expand coverage in your area and offers you a job as a reporter. All it requires is a keen eye, an open ear, and a quiet mouth. Take a few videos of minor meeting between Kindred, maybe write a couple paragraphs about the local covenants, maybe some petty theft or mind reading here and there. They also are willing to pay your heart's desire, whether money, power, blood, or something of your choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:40:58-07:00","id":983697,"title":"","content":"220) From the Depths Below. (Best suited at a coastal city)<br /> The Mariners visited last Elysium. They were an odd bunch of Kindred, though individually they were different. Webbed hands and feet, black eyes, one of them even had long tail coming out of her back. All who have taken to living beneath the waves, and who have been changed through Protean or other means to adapt to unlife in the sea. They\u2019re mostly Gangrel, but there is a Nosferatu and even a Daeva with them, and they speak of other clan members back in their undersea community, almost a city unto itself.<br /> They come with an offer for any Kindred to join them. There are no sects, no politics in the ocean. Blood is plentiful once you learn to enjoy the taste of fish, though they say whale blood is nearly as sustaining as human. Go deep enough and there\u2019s no sunlight. Havens are crude but they can be secure, and there is plenty of room for all. Any who join will be taught how to be a Mariner and guided on how to survive as sea-vampire until they are ready to make it on their own. <br /> Some Kindred, especially the neonates, are looking at it as a way out of a twisted, incestuous system of abuse and power-mongering. Word spreads to a few of the exiles out in the barrens who think it might be a good place to lay low for a while. Things really come to a head when an elder agrees to join them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T15:56:32-07:00","id":984101,"title":"","content":"221)<br /> All kindred know of the weird and the wild between cites. Them rural and suburban areas of america. A group of kindred are sent into the wild to find out what happened to missing group of kindred. Their investigation leads them to strange farm. During the day the farm is a bit creepy with skulls lining the fence post but at night the flesh regrows on each skull. The heads are alive and slowly bleeding out kindred blood into the soil. The Blood pools and flows into the crops and even flows into the scare crows in the land. Is this blood magic is this something more what horror could do such a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:51:28-07:00","id":991155,"title":"","content":"222) The Prince fled the city last night without telling anyone why, and he only took one thing when he left: a tiny locked box that he always kept near him at Elysium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:53:20-07:00","id":991156,"title":"","content":"223) The Gourmand has been sighted in your city. They're a notorious nomadic vampire obsessed with drinking the blood of rare targets, especially other supernatural beings, who keeps on the move to avoid the various groups pursuing them for their crimes. And if the Gourmand has been sighted, it's only a matter of time before supernatural forces converge on the city seeking vengeance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:54:50-07:00","id":991157,"title":"","content":"224) The city's Rack is in its waterfront district, but it's getting less populated and more vigilant after people started going missing and sightings of a &quot;water monster&quot; started being reported. The monster seems to have left the less populated dock district completely alone, and it seems to somehow strike near the best feeding locations. Is something trying to make it harder for the Kindred to feed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:56:31-07:00","id":991158,"title":"","content":"225) Your city has long had a standing Blood Hunt on the Morbus bloodline, and you're sent after a Coterie that's taken over an abandoned laboratory. When you track them down, however, their leader insists that they're trying to create a virus that doesn't harm humans at all, and simply alters their blood enough for the Morbus to feed from them. Will you believe him? Will the Prince?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T15:58:21-07:00","id":991159,"title":"","content":"226) A kindred of some renown visited the city recently, and he gave the Prince a mysterious egg as a gift. The egg was stolen some time ago, and the prince hasn't been able to track it down. Now, tremors are hitting the city and its sewer-dwellers have reported seeing a serpentine creature digging around underground. What's worse, the Prince's greatest enemy, a master of Animalism, appears to be hunting down the creature to take control of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T16:13:53-07:00","id":991163,"title":"","content":"227) Kindred around the city have been exhibiting symptoms of illness after feeding, even though they've all had different victims. Mortals around the city have reported being stalked and attacked by strangers holding syringes. Who's trying to poison the Kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T16:15:31-07:00","id":991164,"title":"","content":"228) The city's Kindred had been having problems with a pack of werewolves and a group of hunters, so one ambitious young courtier attempted to solve the issue (and impress the prince) by turning them against each other. However, the werewolves made a better argument, and now the two groups are united. The courtier begs the players to take care of the situation before the prince finds out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:50:40-07:00","id":991229,"title":"","content":"<b>229)</b> The time approaches, and the Lord of the Harvest requires a blood sacrifice to ensure a bountiful crop for this year's herd. The Circle of the Crone is only too happy to feed this ancient pagan lord, for he infuses the land with his divine essence, making those who consume its bounty grow strong and healthy. Perhaps that wouldn't be so bad, just another missing persons case gone unsolved. But that's not all there is to it. See, the sacrifice is part of a Cruac ritual, which means it requires the blood of a vampire to work its magic properly. And unfortunately for the rest of the city, none of the Circle are willing to volunteer themselves. And unfortunately for you personally, your coterie has been chosen as this year's sacrifice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-21-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:29:59-07:00","id":996116,"title":"","content":"230) Well, the Prince is pregnant. She tried to hide it but a chance meeting with some gossipy harpies has spread the secret as far away as the suburbs. Almost everyone is surprised, as only a few elders and scholars are aware that Kindred pregnancy is even a possibility.<br /> The factions are reacting stereotypically. Invictus and Carthians are planning on using the pregnancy, and the Prince\u2019s subsequent physical weakening, to gain more power. The Lance wants the Prince sent to Final Death before the abomination can be born. The Ordo want to study the entire process and the creature that comes out. The Circle wants to either sacrifice it or make it their god or something (no one really knows with the Crones)<br /> <br /> 231) There\u2019s a Kindred named Dr. Netchurch who has seen this phenomenon before and is rumored to have even assisted in the birth. He just happens to live on the other side of the country and rarely leaves his domain. He\u2019s also rumored to be a Malkovian.<br /> Optional twist: (He\u2019s actually one of Belial\u2019s Brood masquerading as a Malkovian, and thinks that a Dhampir child could be a keystone towards becoming the Anti-Man.)<br /> <br /> 232) Maury Show.<br /> The Prince has a moderate derangement of Nymphomania and indulges in sex regularly. There a few, maybe even several, possibilities of who the father is. Find him, get him out of the city or in the Prince\u2019s mansion before any of the other Kindred can figure out who it is. Or find him and sell him to the highest bidder. Or keep the father and make your own power play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:54:41-07:00","id":996123,"title":"","content":"I like 230 through 232 but there's too many comedic undertones I couldn't ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:14:19-07:00","id":996261,"title":"","content":"233) Apparently, there's a new kind of Vampire out there, supposedly fuelled by blood-borne nanites and with a knack for computers. They want in on the whole Kindred deal, and have managed to get enough notice from your Prince that some poor schmuck has been asked to investigate and figure out if they're worth Siring in as full Kindred, or failing that, whether they are a threat.<br /> <br /> That poor schmuck is you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:04:00-07:00","id":998967,"title":"","content":"234) Mostly cribbed from Inception<br /> A Bishop of the Lance has been having terrible dreams during his daysleep. These are not the normal torpor nightmares. He dreams of a series of twisting, sulfurous caverns, populated by creatures that could only be called demons. He seeks to escape but the path seems to be shaping itself as he travels, taking him to deeper and darker torments. He wakes at sundown, covered in blood sweat, and remembering the horrors in exacting detail. The Bishop knows his lore well and believes his nightmares are actually visions into one of the realms beyond this mortal one.<br /> He has prayed nightly, castigating himself with blades and fire, calling on God and Loginous to free him. It seems his prayers were answered last week. In a fit of inspiration (he would say divine inspiration) the Bishop discovered a magical rite to let a small number of Kindred open the door to the realm he sees.<br /> Of course he can\u2019t turn to other members of the Lance, treasonous snakes that they are. They\u2019re just as likely to find a way to end his unlife there and declare themselves bishops. An coterie outside of the church\u2019s hierarchy is what he needs.<br /> And of course he has no idea what the coterie should do if this planewalking actually works.<br /> (Maybe bring a mortal along, find a tower in the middle of the realm and write their name on it?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:23:51-07:00","id":998973,"title":"","content":"235) You wake up one evening in your Haven, and check you messages. You see a number of them which make no sense and seem to be dated from the future. Then you notice three weeks have actually gone by. &quot;Man, we had fun, didn't we?&quot; you hear from behind you, said by an owl made of smoke before it flies off into the night.<br /> <br /> 236) You meet up with your Coterie. They greet you by a name you don't recognize and say &quot;so, are we still on with the plan for tonight?&quot;. You don't know of any plan for tonight. And their eyes gleam yellow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-05-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:03:00-07:00","id":999051,"title":"","content":"<b>237)</b> Over the last several weeks, you've noticed some disturbing patterns of late. The Gangrel seem to be appearing within the city limits with increasing frequency. Nosferatu have begun to set up shop in more publicly accessible areas. Daeva have reluctantly sworn vows of chastity, while Ventrue seem to be donating large tracts of territory and finances towards more charitable enterprises. Even the Mekhet seem to be actively avoiding the shadows of late. Someone, or something, has the clans of the city frightened away from their typical M.O's and nobody seems exactly clear on what's causing it. Scrounging together a coterie, you decide to do your own investigation into the matter. One can only imagine the level of prestige you'll gain by putting the fears of not one, but all five clans to rest!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:29:41-07:00","id":999057,"title":"","content":"238) Some of the Daeva of the city are starting to look a little\u2026strange. Skin peeling, scars appearing on faces and hands, limbs becoming twisted, all sorts of weird stuff. I hear a few of the harpies have locked themselves in their haven and sending out ghouls to buy make up in bulk.<br /> <br /> One of the Kindred out in the boonies swears that he was talking to a member of his coterie when her eyes turned black. Majesty also doesn\u2019t seem to be working for them half the time.<br /> <br /> By the way, did you see the Nosferatu primogen at Elysium? He seemed different. Less repulsive. Honestly, he was looking pretty hot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T05:19:10-08:00","id":999174,"title":"","content":"239) A new medical firm has moved into town - one boasting all kinds of revolutionary new treatments. But when the local ranking Kindred tried to get their hooks into the firm's administration, the vampires who tried disappeared. And disappearances amongst the Neonates have been on the rise since. Last night, an associate of your Coterie barely made it out of an ambush by hunters (who were also Ghouls). It's pretty obvious now where Kindred have been disappearing, where the medical treatments are coming from, and who sent the hunters.<br /> [Whether you want to make the firm a branch of The Cheiron Group, a breakaway, or a new player is up to the ST. Basic idea is a group harvesting Kindred Vitae for super-drugs.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:45:41-08:00","id":999192,"title":"","content":"240) The Bloodening!<br /> It\u2019s breaking the box office as the hottest indie horror movie of the year. Reviewers say it\u2019s the most terrifying thing they\u2019ve ever seen. It\u2019s a movie whose special effects are in reality some obscure Lance and Crone magical rites.<br /> Someone is going to get a sun tan for this.<br /> <br /> 241) The mystics have found a new conjunction of leylines that would be great for magical rites. The Circle, Ordo, and Lance haven\u2019t pursued it with any interest because it happens to be located about 500 feet above the ground. Are you a bad enough dude to cut through the city\u2019s bureaucracy and build a something high enough to get to it?<br /> By the way, the merlins know of it too and have the same idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:55:25-08:00","id":999200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Icon787</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=999192#post999192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">241) The mystics have found a new conjunction of leylines that would be great for magical rites. The Circle, Ordo, and Lance haven\u2019t pursued it with any interest because it happens to be located about 500 feet above the ground. Are you a bad enough dude to cut through the city\u2019s bureaucracy and build a something high enough to get to it?<br /> By the way, the merlins know of it too and have the same idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>242) It took 19 months, $23,000 in bribes and campaign contributions, countless dollars on the actual construction itself, and the crushing of two different labor unions, but you've finally gottent things underway. Your workers have built all but the last floor, but something's up: Every day, all the work on the last floor disappears, right into the ether. There's no evidence of sabotage, it's just like the work never happened. This project is getting expensive, and if you don't want to bankrupt yourself, you'd better figure out what the Hell's going on, and <i>fast</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:32:49-08:00","id":999836,"title":"","content":"243) You hear about the Nosferatu primogen\u2019s secret herd? They\u2019re LARPERS! The Harpy\u2019s childe\u2019s roommate\u2019s ghoul saw him at a D&amp;D event \u201cdressed up\u201d like a rotting lich. Everyone apparently loves the effort he puts into his cosmetics.<br /> Of course, now every Nos and even some Kindred from other clans are starting their own LARP groups. I get it. You want to let the mask down and maybe even get some compliments on how ugly you are. Maybe even show your fangs and hear the Kine go \u201coooohhh\u201d without running away in terror. How long do you think the Prince is going to sit on this before putting her foot down.<br /> <br /> 244) Welp, the LARPERS are hunting us now. Apparently these nerds aren\u2019t as blind as some of us would have liked. First it was just the people who were making them their herds. Good riddance. Saves the Hound the effort of hunting them down and bringing them to the Prince for violating the Masquerade.<br /> Then they starting hitting everyone else. You know that elder with the tattoos? Right, Rodrigo. He was out with his ghoul, Cynthia, doing whatever it is elders do, when these teenagers, fucking teenagers mind you, bust swords and axes out of their backpacks and start hacking at him. He had his own hidden in his cane, and Cynthia said he fought hard, and he was a swordsman back when that title meant something, but she saw him get his head cut off before running as fast as the blood would take her. <br /> I\u2019ve heard some rumors here and there that other Kindred are ending up meeting the end. Apparently all that time playing with toy swords is pretty good training for the real thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:44:59-08:00","id":999841,"title":"","content":"245) You know Robert\u2019s Rules of Order? It\u2019s that things that groups do when people say \u201cthe Chair recognizes douchebag number three.\u201d Well the Invictus elders are into it in a big way. Part of the rules includes having a secretary that transcribes the minutes of every meeting. And you know Nathan, that mid-level Invictus asshole? Yeah, apparently he was ordered to be the secretary. Yeah, and now the book he was keeping everything in is\u2026lost. Stupid fucker forgot the damn thing at a bus stop.<br /> So a Masquerade breach is out there that also contains what the Invictus top dogs have been discussing for the last several years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:58:15-08:00","id":999848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Icon787</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=999841#post999841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">245) You know Robert\u2019s Rules of Order? It\u2019s that things that groups do when people say \u201cthe Chair recognizes douchebag number three.\u201d Well the Invictus elders are into it in a big way. Part of the rules includes having a secretary that transcribes the minutes of every meeting. And you know Nathan, that mid-level Invictus asshole? Yeah, apparently he was ordered to be the secretary. Yeah, and now the book he was keeping everything in is\u2026lost. Stupid fucker forgot the damn thing at a bus stop.<br /> So a Masquerade breach is out there that also contains what the Invictus top dogs have been discussing for the last several years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I'm not sure who's the stupidest asshole there. The secretary for not using personalized shorthand to keep his transcriptions encoded in the first place (and ensuring his continued value as the one keeping the records secure) or the elders for appointing such an idiot in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:15:43-08:00","id":999857,"title":"","content":"246) Diablerie. Amaranth. Devouring the Heartsblood. The super delicious cannibalism dessert.<br /> It\u2019s heinous. It\u2019s evil. But there\u2019s a nomad passing through who talks about Many, a Kindred living out in the wilderness. Many spoke with the nomad for several nights, regarding diablerie and how with the proper purity of the soul it can be a joining instead of consumption. Ascension instead of Dissolution. There might be something to that as the nomad tells of seeing white veins in his aura, and sensing holiness in its presence. The nomad also says that it never once had to drink blood for the week that they spent together.<br /> The nomad says that Many will let you stay with it for as long as you like. If you want to strive towards Unity he will teach you. If he finds you worthy you will join each other through diablerie. You might think it\u2019s just a canny elder stealing the souls of naive licks but Many always allows the student to diablerize it and it\u2019s never the other way around. The student then takes on the name and existence of Many and waits for the next student to arrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:54:51-08:00","id":999901,"title":"","content":"247) An unpopular, but canny, Nosferatu has managed to get the Invictus to grant him multiple room-sized territories in several hotels, motels, and ghetto apartments. Since none of the buildings themselves fall under specific Invictus control, everybody thought he was just setting up a series of saferooms and backup havens. In fact, he's started a business venture; vampire fast food, for the rich, the desperate, or the lazy.<br /> <br /> All the rooms have been soundproofed, their floors and furniture are either wipedown-ready or instantly replacable, cellphone jammers have been installed, and all the entrances/exits and LOS are compromised or favor the intruder. The landlords are Dominated into placing the most disappear-able guests into those rooms. For a small(ish) fee, a vampire is given access for an hour. For a <i>large </i>fee, a vampire is given until sunrise.<br /> <br /> The Invictus is split on whether to knock the venture down to discourage future smartasses from exploiting fealty boundaries, or to snatch up the idea and just franchise the little turd out of existence.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu has also been dropping hints that this is only the first custom-prey-oriented idea; his followup is using long-term Dominate, Nightmare, and Auspex to create groomed, tailored prey humans (for a <i>very </i>large fee, by commission only).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:29:50-08:00","id":999950,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=34503#post34503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) A local member of the Ordo Dracul claims a breakthrough in his research. His claim is that he explain and reverse the Curse scientifically. The Circle and the Sanctum both oppose this &quot;Breakthrough&quot; as it undermines their own beliefs in the vampiric race.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 248) An heretical branch of Lance Sanctum which ascribes to Radical Arminianism that transcend apparent damnation, and is in fact able to enact miracles that cure the Curse. The Orthodox Lance Sanctum wants to burn the heretics at the stake, the circle of the crone are just as deeply offended, and the ordo Dracul want to practice vivisection and the dissection on those performing and receiving the miracles. Frighteningly, for all three factions and perhaps all vampire-kind, those restored to mortality seem to have their flesh, blood, and bone act as a Banes to all vampires and after their transformation are immune to all further vampiric powers. Could this actually be salvation, or is something sinister going on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-08-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T19:26:05-08:00","id":1001593,"title":"","content":"249) One of the biologicians of the Ordo has spent a century breeding a new type of Kine. Through eugenics and stolen blood magic he has created humans who can condense their blood like the Kindred do vitae. Each mortal holds double their total health boxes of blood. In addition, given plenty of water and enough food, the mortal can replenish his total blood supply in a few hours.<br /> The dragon who created these Kine only has three of them so far. He\u2019s currently planning a large scale breeding project to make more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:38:40-08:00","id":1001773,"title":"","content":"250) The local Methodist based hunter cell have new clean-cut middle-class members from outside of town who seem exceptionally vampire savvy. They noticed the Lance Sanctum Mekhet that monitors the group to make sure any vampires sloppy enough to gain hunter attention are quarantined for extermination, or disappear into a staked sleep of ages. The Mekhet was disturbed that they seem impenetrable to Auspex and saw him even through his Obfuscate. They left an envelope with a letter to the local Lance Sanctum claiming that they are God's judgement upon the local vampires who have fallen from their roles to frighten the wicked toward righteousness.<br /> <br /> Else where a Carthian gangrel recognizes one of the new hunters as their Lance Sanctum grandsire from a few few cities over, but that can't be can it? This is a living human, without the beast.<br /> <br /> In truth these new hunters are former Lance Sanctum Vampires from a radical sect in another town that have been transformed via Miracle into humans who are immune to vampire power and whose flesh, blood, and bone act as a Banes to all vampires. This is the aftermath of the below story line if not &quot;properly cleaned up&quot; in someone else's town.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=999950#post999950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">248) An heretical branch of Lance Sanctum which ascribes to Radical Arminianism that transcend apparent damnation, and is in fact able to enact miracles that cure the Curse. The Orthodox Lance Sanctum wants to burn the heretics at the stake, the circle of the crone are just as deeply offended, and the ordo Dracul want to practice vivisection and the dissection on those performing and receiving the miracles. Frighteningly, for all three factions and perhaps all vampire-kind, those restored to mortality seem to have their flesh, blood, and bone act as a Banes to all vampires and after their transformation are immune to all further vampiric powers. Could this actually be salvation, or is something sinister going on?</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-11-2016, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T18:08:03-08:00","id":1002022,"title":"","content":"251) A Ventrue of the Ordo Dracul has finally found a way to completely tame the Beast through a custom devotion. It channels the psychic energy of the id and redirects into the surrounding area, leaving the Beast calm.<br /> Of course, violence has spiked in the city. People are becoming more and more paranoid, rarely leaving their homes. In fact, the Ventrue has a haven in a part of the city where people have begun to turn\u2026feral.<br /> <br /> 252) A powerful ghost (or spirit if you prefer) offers a potential solution to a city afflicted by the Strix. The ghost will not only aid the Kindred with identifying the possessed, it will also devour any weakened owl that the Kindred bring to it. Of course everyone sees the parallel with diablerie and many of the wiser vampires worry what creature might be created from this process. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T21:20:23-08:00","id":1002459,"title":"","content":"<b>253)</b> Among the local Circle of the Crone, one of the Fools takes their appointed role a little bit too exuberantly. Styling themselves after the infamous Loki, they have decided to bring Ragnarok (death of the gods) to the rest of the domain. Unfortunately the Circle of the Crone philosophy is no stranger to portraying vampires as a form of deity, which means that this Fool is basically planning to eradicate all kindred in the city, using whatever symbolic representation of fire giants he can get his hands on. It goes without saying that they must be stopped; but how does one locate a powerful warlock with a passion for trickery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:20:14-08:00","id":1012102,"title":"","content":"254) Little Shop of Horrors<br /> Well, some Gangrel elder was making a mandrake in a hidden section of the local park. Somehow, the plant ate the Gangrel. No, I have no idea how that happened. It's spreading, choking off the local plants. Already the animals and some of the homeless are starting to disappear. Are you a bad enough coterie to grab some weed killer and put this thing down. <br /> <br /> 255) Hostile Terraforming. <br /> The Kine don't go to the park anymore, not after all those missing persons reports. The Mandrake has taken over a huge chunk of the area. The know that coterie the Prince sent in to investigate? The survivor swears that the plants were trying to communicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T18:20:10-08:00","id":1021099,"title":"","content":"256) One of the Prince's mortal descendants, a famous action star, is in town shooting the next season of the TV series he stars in. The prince has ordered you to keep him safe and out of trouble. The problems? first, he's kind of a macho blockhead with a tendency to get into fights with paparazzi and such. Second, the TV series is Lupus: the man wolf legacy, a show about a heroic immortal werewolf fighting evil across history and it just so happens that the actor bears a strong resemblance to the human form of one of the high ranking actual werewolves in the city, and the CGI wolfish forms of the TV character look like him too. So when one of the real werewolf's rivals creates a case of mistaken identity to cause trouble for them, it is up to you to keep the blockhead actor safe from angry werewolves, while making sure he doesn't learn enough about them to become a threat to THEIR masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T18:56:57-08:00","id":1021763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1021099#post1021099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">256) One of the Prince's mortal descendants, a famous action star, is in town shooting the next season of the TV series he stars in. The prince has ordered you to keep him safe and out of trouble. The problems? first, he's kind of a macho blockhead with a tendency to get into fights with paparazzi and such. Second, the TV series is Lupus: the man wolf legacy, a show about a heroic immortal werewolf fighting evil across history and it just so happens that the actor bears a strong resemblance to the human form of one of the high ranking actual werewolves in the city, and the CGI wolfish forms of the TV character look like him too. So when one of the real werewolf's rivals creates a case of mistaken identity to cause trouble for them, it is up to you to keep the blockhead actor safe from angry werewolves, while making sure he doesn't learn enough about them to become a threat to THEIR masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>257.) Complicating matters, the producer turns out to be one of those life Mages, with an obsession over natural selection, who's specifically <i>trying</i> to get you and the wolves to kill each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T17:08:38-08:00","id":1030870,"title":"","content":"258) Someone has the prince under blood bond, how long before the city notices? And will they try to bring a fairer city about or merely look out for themselves?<br /> Replace prince with any high ranking member of the hierarchy if you want something a little more low key, maybe a Mekhet is using night long Auspex to monitor the Primogen for their own reason with their unwitting spy unaware of their roll in what is to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:44:21-08:00","id":1031240,"title":"","content":"259) My name is Vlad and I am an addict. <br /> <br /> Some neonates have started an addiction group based on the 12-steps (Like Alcoholics Anonymous, Narcotics Anonymous, and Overeaters Anonymous). The group started with only five members but some other licks have started showing up. It also seems to be working for them. They still need to drink blood, of course, but none of them have frenzied during a feeding and they seem to have a better control over the Beast. One of the harpies even mentioned seeing leaders of the Carthians and the Invictus walking into the meeting together. <br /> The Kindred of the city are divided on opinion, as usual. Some think its a great idea. Some think denying the Beast will just lead to a massive relapse that will involve a Masquerade breach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:53:38-08:00","id":1031246,"title":"","content":"260) An elder Ventrue has opened up a life coaching practice. She happens to use high levels of Dominate to rewrite individuals minds. If you're overweight, she will give you a minor compulsion to exercise. If you are struggling with addiction, she will give you an aversion to the sight of drugs. All of this is just experimentation and training for her Great Work. She will use Dominate on a Kindred to recreate the Beast insider their mind into...well, she's not sure yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:10:17-08:00","id":1031253,"title":"","content":"261) Word through the grapevine is that the Prince's sire is coming this way. Yeah, I thought he was too ancient to have one too. Think that's why he called for three blood hunts in as many weeks and purged the primogen council? Maybe he's trying to clean house before mommy gets home. <br /> <br /> 262) Golconda is a place. No really! Forget what you heard about personal development and becoming one with your humanity again. Golconda is a real place in the world that you can go to where the Beast is silenced, where your need for blood is finally filled. Hell, you might even be able to walk in sunlight again. <br /> It is so true! My sire's ghoul's cousin's roommate's blood doll heard it from the Prince herself. No one leaves there though because if you do, you go back to being a monster. <br /> <br /> 263) By the way, find out why Golconda is the way it is and send me an email or something. Let's make it that way over here. Maybe we need to sacrifice a unicorn at the center of some leylines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:10:29-08:00","id":1031254,"title":"","content":"261) A tomb was recently unearthed, dating back to the Neolithic period, unusually ornate and advanced for the period, containing a single, perfectly preserved corpse. That corpse has disappeared en route to the Smithsonian, and the Elders of DC have been quietly disappearing.<br /> <br /> 262) The cause of the disappearing Elders has been made clear: An ancient Vampire, perhaps the oldest one yet know, has revealed herself as the God-Queen Ereshkigal. She is a terror of blood and death that even the Arisen and Magi of DC can barely hope to contend with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:29:29-08:00","id":1032946,"title":"","content":"263) A young but influenceful Dragon has asked an unusual boon of the Prince, to be named Regent of the sun lit city. He offers to keep an eye on the city by day and warn of any dangers he finds in return for hunting rights and the authority to act as he sees best in the absence of any other Kindred authority, something he has been doing anyway.<br /> <br /> 264) A group of influenceful Kindred announce that they require the procurement of a Mage, a competent fighter, a thief and a man of the cloth (or suitable substitutes). Please arrange for their investigation free disappearance and all other such matters. Prior to their disappearance they should all meet in a tavern.<br /> <br /> 265) A Dragon has discovered a new Scale.<br /> Invigorating Heartblood.<br /> Prerequisite Coil: The Vast Dynasty.<br /> Procedure: The Dragon extracts blood directly from his heart using a pump and his own will. Atempting the prosess courses one Agrivated Damage and each roll costs one Willpower.<br /> Roll Resolve+Stamina with a target number of 5 but subtract 1 die for each roll after the first, for each success one Vitai is extracted by the pump, when extracted the Vitai lasts one night pre point of Blood Potency of the vampire and losses one point of Blood Potency an hour. The vampire does not have to use all his successes and most stop at 5 Vitai.<br /> Outcome: Known uses so far include: when injected into the heart of a Revrent roll Blood Potency and uplift as an embrace would on a pass, if fed to a human or ghoul it grants the ghoul state for a number of months equal to Blood Potency with no other costs after which the ghoul may mentain the state as normal, when injected into the heart of a vampire in torpor the vampire will awaken on a success on a roll of combined Blood Potency of the the sample and the torpored vampire, finally the sample is still Vitai but does not course Blood Bond or Addiction and allows anyone who drinks it to learn Disciplines as though they were being trained by the doner for a number of months equal to Blood Potency.<br /> The possibility of granting loved ones immortality without Vinculum has attracted the intrest of many young Kindred and some Elders have also signalled their intrest in sampling this product.<br /> (I know this doesn't look impressive but it's very flexible so I don't want to make it too powerful)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T21:38:57-08:00","id":1033875,"title":"","content":"266) Tonight the diablerized corpse of a popular Ancilla and friend of the Prince is found on the stage of an abandoned theater. He is seated in a chair identical to the one favored by the Prince in Elysium and wearing stolen clothes belonging to the Prince. His long dead skin shows its age in fragility. It sloughs off in a shower of pale motes at the slightest hint of a draft to reveal shriveled, dark muscle and sinew. His fangs are broken in half with bright red rose petals filling the gaping mouth. The fragile body is blindfolded and wrapped loosely in barbed wire. The wire is rigged to support the withered right hand and hold up an old fashioned scale. A goblet full of an unidentified Kindred's blood sets on one side balancing a bowl full of old silver coins. The name of a Kindred in the city has been written on the face of each coin and &quot;innocent&quot; or &quot;guilty&quot; is on the back. A letter addressed to one of the player's characters is tied to the other hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12879-irenegrayle","name":"IreneGrayle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:36:40-08:00","id":1035792,"title":"","content":"267) You know Lacey Saville? Yeah the Draugr that the Prince put a blood hunt on. Well apparently both the Nosferatu Primogen and one of the unaligned are both claiming to have iced her a few nights past. A dragon said he was attacked by Lacey last night in the Rack a couple hours before dawn but an Invictus lick claims he killed her in the Barrens yesterday a little after sundown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:43:46-08:00","id":1035798,"title":"","content":"268) Every few nights Lucy attempts to kill herself. She succeeds. The first time she chained herself to a park bench and waited for the dawn. She woke up in an alley nearby after nightfall. The next time she picked a fight with a lupine in the city\u2019s park. She woke up in the suburbs in an old lady\u2019s backyard. Time and time again, through multiple ways of suicide that led to what should be a Kindred\u2019s final death, she succeeds and awakens the next night at sundown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T16:56:44-08:00","id":1035895,"title":"","content":"269) When out feeding you pick up that another club goer is Kindred, undeterred you continue without bothering them. They meet up with you as you're leaving and you realise it's the Prince.<br /> 270) Someone has dealt with that hunter cell, that's a relief because they were doing some damage. What happens when they start up again as Ghouls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T17:23:14-08:00","id":1035899,"title":"","content":"271) For some reason the Prince has putting an unusual amount of effort into driving an Italian bistro in the nightclub district out of business. As far as anyone can tell, the bistro and it's owners are completely mundane with no trace of kindred or other supernatural connections, and the prince doesn't seem to have any political or financial reason to sink it, he just seems to hate the place for some reason.<br /> <br /> Which is why he has sent to your coterie to intercept a famous food critic who is set to review the place and make sure he gives them 0 stars and a poo emoji... but why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:58:19-08:00","id":1036856,"title":"","content":"272) The herd has picked up on a tag used by a group of kindred that are trying to fix up their territory (they may have benevolent aims or just be trading easy feeding for income) and have started using it as a protest symbol. By the time kindred work out who's behind this false flag operation it's started to spread throughout the city.<br /> <br /> 273) An alliances of Meket and Nosferatu have laid claim to some choice territory, anyone who enters unbidden falls to an unseen attacker. The Prince is not happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:48:34-08:00","id":1036981,"title":"","content":"274) A Kindred, Duke Karsh, and his coterie, have come to the city. He proclaims himself Warlord of the Invictus, a title of the elders of the city\u2019s Inner Circle have never heard. He is here on a recruitment drive. Blood and funds will be provided to any Kindred who enlists in his army and survives his rather grueling training regimen.<br /> Once they are ready, Karsh will lead them to a city on the other side of the country to conquer it in the name of the Invictus. Titles, territory, and herds will be given to the victors. He also invites the Dragons and the Lance to the fight, and many neonates are taking him up on the offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:34:44-08:00","id":1037005,"title":"","content":"275) Peacemaker<br /> A Kindred with a third eye in her forehead has come to the city. She presents herself at Elysium and makes a passionate speech for Kindred to cease their fighting and scheming against each other and focus on attaining peace both amongst each other and with their Beasts. There might be something to this as even the most cold hearted monsters of the Kindred report their Beast barely stirs in her presence.<br /> The next Elysium she comes with a Kindred in tow who is well known to be a wily Draugr. Apparently with her help the Man has reemerged and now he begs the Prince absolution for his crimes and a place in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:29:03-08:00","id":1037029,"title":"","content":"276). one of the local Ancilla, who is high up in whichever covenant the ST needs him to be, has a problem, you see, one of his latest projects required him to work with some FBI agents of varying levels of corruption. The problem is that the ancilla was wanted by the FBI back in the 60s and 70s, for what he won't say, before his embrace and by sheer bad luck, one of the agents he was working on the project with was an agent that had been assigned the hunt for him back in the 70s.<br /> <br /> The agent recognized him right away, even though the ancilla didn't remember him at first, and now the ancilla needs the PCs to take care of the problem before the agent figures out how the wanted fugitive has managed to stay young looking for so long and becomes a threat to the masquerade.<br /> <br /> Of course, having some federally verified blackmail info on a high level covenant official could be useful too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:14:55-08:00","id":1040303,"title":"","content":"277) The Prince has decreed the outcome of a Covenant leadership contest. The Covenant is angry about this outside interference and insists on deciding for themselves but the court is ignoring their objections. Did the prince have a plan or was this just stirring things up for the sake of it.<br /> 278) Reverents are on the rise (yes I'm aware of the pun) and the Maskarade is weakening under the strain. Heavy restrictions are being placed upon feeding in order to stem this endemic until the source can be found.<br /> 279) The group is required to attend a meeting with non kindred supernaturals, they aren't told why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:46:55-08:00","id":1051517,"title":"","content":"280: Vampires\u2026IN SPACE!<br /> The Prince of Orlando has called a blood hunt. The only problem is that the target has stowed away on a rocket launched out of Cape Canaveral last week. Of course there\u2019s a night launch going on next month that might be able to hold a little extra weight from one or two Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T19:19:54-08:00","id":1055505,"title":"","content":"281:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/politics/features/2016-01-20/what-kind-of-man-spends-millions-to-elect-ted-cruz-\" target=\"_blank\">Robert </a>Mercer, the money mastermind behind Beirtbart, is a member of a Strix worshiping cult, which should have been obvious to the kindred given his <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/politics/features/2016-01-20/what-kind-of-man-spends-millions-to-elect-ted-cruz-\" target=\"_blank\">obsession </a>with owls. So in other words, the Strix control the guy who controls the guy who controls president Trump. This won't be good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:02:14-08:00","id":1055691,"title":"","content":"I admit I didn't read all 281 plot hooks, so it's possible that this has been done before. Still!<br /> <br /> 282) Your Covenant has finally decided to knock over a neighboring domain and assist the Kindred there loyal to your Covenant in taking power. It...didn't work. A high ranking refugee from your Covenant in that city has escaped to your city, but she's being kept hostage by the rival Covenant's presence in your city. She has very important information that will assist your Covenant, as well as being a high ranking member herself. But trying to rescue her might overthrow the peace in your city. Your Elder has tasked you with rescuing her discreetly. How will you manage this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T15:51:33-08:00","id":1056351,"title":"","content":"<b>283) </b>Talks of open revolution are being flung around nearly every faction except for the Carthians. For reasons unknown, every vampire over the age of 150 has had their powers effectively switched off. The vitae continues to animate their dead bodies each night, but beyond that, they are just as powerless as an ordinary human. The only vampires who have retained their powers are neonates and early ancillae, who are over joyed by the fact they don't have to be afraid of centuries old elders threatening to have them staked and baked for stepping out of line!<br /> <br /> As we said, nobody knows exactly how this happened, but a mixed coterie of Carthian and Circle members was reportedly missing just a few weeks before this predicament occurred!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T06:58:10-08:00","id":1060856,"title":"","content":"<b>284)</b> Your Covenant is in an uproar - somehow, mere humans have appropriated their secrets and turned their own powers against them. How are kine able to access the secret abilities of Kindred?<br /> Some examples:<ul><li>Lancea Et Sanctum: The local churches have become far more dangerous ground - their members and ministers have been witnessed to turn the dark miracles of Theban Sorcery upon those Faithful who wander near or try to carry out their sacred purpose as God's Scourge.</li> <li>Invictus: The halls of power are increasingly closed off - a different conspiracy is securing key individuals with potent Oaths of their own, undermining the First Estate's influence and ability to maintain the Masquerade.</li> <li>Carthians: Entire neighborhoods have been declared Barrens as community centers meet and protect their areas with the recognizable weight of Carthian Law.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T20:07:14-07:00","id":1073999,"title":"","content":"285) Festival of Blades<br /> The Crone has disappeared. Well not all of the them. The lowest level members are still around, all of them confused about where all the power players of the covenant have gone. The harpies have sent the rumor mill spinning, of course, but no one really knows. That is until a lupine comes to the city telling any supernatural that will listen that her pack was destroyed by a coterie of vampires who can turn into creatures of metal and bone. She reports that they're out in the wilderness, killing each other, and becoming more and more monstrous with each of their covenant mates that they kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T20:15:52-07:00","id":1074003,"title":"","content":"286) Succession<br /> Nomad rumors tell of a city where they do things...differently. When a Prince is killed or enters torpor the city's elder's convene an Elysium where any vampire, from elder to neonate, can take a mystical test to judge their fitness to lead of city of Kindred. The test is called the Black Spiral. A mystical journey where the Kindred suffers unspeakable ordeals and parleys with deranged spirits. Most who walk the Spiral and return are left broken, insane husks. But eventually one of the Kindred returns sound of mind and body and is welcomed as the next Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T09:53:04-07:00","id":1074199,"title":"","content":"287) Some strange blood-born parasite has been spotted in the domain. It takes over a human host, slowly beginning to control their actions as starts replacing more of their blood with itself. Eventually, a human is nothing more than a puppet of the parasite, completing its strange goals until its host is killed. Then it vacates its old body and hunts for a new home, leaving an exsanguinated corpse - and threatening the Masquerade. And now, some fool Ancilla had the great idea to try and drink from one of parasite's hosts. And then share their corrupted Vitae with their Ghouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T09:09:44-07:00","id":1075496,"title":"","content":"<b>288)</b> Well, shit's fucked! Belial's Brood decided to go full blown public with their activities. I guess when you perceive yourself as a literal demon, you don't care about mass panic and wanton destruction. Anyways, the Princes are unable to convincingly spin this off as a mundane incident. The masquerade is rapidly deteriorating and, in less than a month, the whole country will know that vampires exist. After that, the rest of the world is sure to follow. That's when the Kindred receive contact from the most unlikely allies; the government itself. Turns out they know all about vampire society, they have numerous organizations dedicated to keeping them in check. And now they're 'offering' a chance to work together and stamp out the Brood while there's still time.<br /> <br /> Now, vampire coteries and hunter cells must put aside their differences in order to stop the world from plunging into darkness. Assuming the national leaders don't nuke everybody back to the ice age!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T20:58:11-07:00","id":1076793,"title":"","content":"289.) The Prince wakes up for the night to find that the fancy hotel used as both his Haven and the main Elysium is crawling with police and federal agents due to a famous rock star dying under suspicious circumstances on the property during the day, and the prince has assigned your coterie to get rid of them.<br /> <br /> 290.) The dead rock star is the Dhamphir son of the prince of the next domain over, who thinks the your prince may have had something to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:40:35-07:00","id":1077692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1076793#post1076793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">289.) The Prince wakes up for the night to find that the fancy hotel used as both his Haven and the main Elysium is crawling with police and federal agents due to a famous rock star dying under suspicious circumstances on the property during the day, and the prince has assigned your coterie to get rid of them.<br /> <br /> 290.) The dead rock star is the Dhamphir son of the prince of the next domain over, who thinks the your prince may have had something to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>291.) The prince from the next domain over is in fact the one who ordered him dead, looking for casus belli to start a war. The players can either expose the truth, and risk a war anyway, or take advantage and try to profit off the coming war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T13:56:05-07:00","id":1077906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1077692#post1077692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">289.) The Prince wakes up for the night to find that the fancy hotel used as both his Haven and the main Elysium is crawling with police and federal agents due to a famous rock star dying under suspicious circumstances on the property during the day, and the prince has assigned your coterie to get rid of them.<br /> <br /> 290.) The dead rock star is the Dhamphir son of the prince of the next domain over, who thinks the your prince may have had something to do with it.<br /> <br /> 291.) The prince from the next domain over is in fact the one who ordered him dead, looking for casus belli to start a war. The players can either expose the truth, and risk a war anyway, or take advantage and try to profit off the coming war.</div> </div> </div> </div>292.) It was in fact a high status Kindred in your city (Primogen, Seneschal, et al) who arranged the murder, hoping the blame would be put on your Prince so that he could seize praxis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:34:35-07:00","id":1077925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1077906#post1077906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 292.) It was in fact a high status Kindred in your city (Primogen, Seneschal, et al) who arranged the murder, hoping the blame would be put on your Prince so that he could seize praxis.</div> </div> </div> </div>293) Your source for all this information, and involuntary companion, is a Strix eager to see the chaos unleashed, no matter what your choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:18:06-07:00","id":1078107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1077925#post1077925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 293) Your source for all this information, and involuntary companion, is a Strix eager to see the chaos unleashed, no matter what your choice.</div> </div> </div> </div><s>294) It turns out that <i>you</i> were the one behind everything all along, and that you were actually the First Vampire, afflicted with amnesia.</s><br /> <br /> 294) You've skipped town after a power struggle that was too convoluted for even an Elder to follow, and have to set yourself up in a new city. Problem is, it's dominated by an obscure clan of Kindred that doesn't take kindly to strangers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T22:46:18-07:00","id":1078187,"title":"","content":"295.) all of the above are partly true. The other prince did put out the hit on his own son, but only because of bad intel claiming the son was giving sensitive information to your prince, which was given to the other prince by by the high status local kindred, who plans to ally with the other prince to overthrow the local prince. The strix giving you the intel has it's own plans, which probably aren't good for anything but itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T13:17:15-07:00","id":1079020,"title":"","content":"296) Everything is becoming a convoluted mess so you and your coterie decide to weather the storm by hanging out in the subbasement of a local nightclub, playing video games for two months and only coming out for a tiny bite from some drunken club patron to keep you going. When you come out you find a city empty of Kindred. No Prince, no elders, no Danse, no Masquerade. In that convoluted mess of a war the Prince, the Strix, and every Kindred in the city and in the neighboring domain have killed each other or driven themselves into torpor. Hunters killed off the last stragglers. You find out this information from one of the last ghouls who is quickly going mad from lack of Vitae and will do anything for a drink.<br /> So, the the city is your playground with no fear of repercussions from your own kind. What do you and your coterie do with unlimited freedom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:09:49-07:00","id":1080436,"title":"","content":"297) So, apparently being in charge of a city devoid of vampires, with a bunch of bored hunters with nothing to hunt, kind of sucks. Not to mention, apparently some giant magic space computer(?) called the &quot;God-Machine&quot; apparently needed to have vampires around for some reason or another. The thing has offered you a choice: Step into its &quot;time splinter&quot; and fix things, and any memory of events as they transpired will be erased. Refuse, and the God-Machine will alert ever Hunter in the area to your hideout.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T03:22:02-07:00","id":1080804,"title":"","content":"<b>298)</b> So the Ordo Dracul, you know those guys, right? Bunch of mad scientist vampires seeking to become the perfect being? Well, it turns out they're really big fans of Jojo's Bizarre Adventure and have used the energy contained in the ley lines to create a stone capable of not only eliminating a vampire's weaknesses completely, but also dramatically amplifying their supernatural powers by <i>hundreds of times</i> their normal capacity. Any vampire who utilizes the stone would become a perfect being with no discernible limits to their abilities. There's just one problem in that the stone was stolen before its power could be unleashed and nobody knows exactly who's responsible. The most likely culprits are the Mage cabals and some incredibly ballsy Hunter cells. But what if there's more at play here than the usual suspects? Investigations into the scene of the crime have turned up a strange piece of evidence left behind. A small discarded cog smeared in what seems to be human blood was found half buried in the center of the ley line's convergence point and it's giving off more energy than the Ordo Dracul have ever encountered before!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-19-2017, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:05:14-07:00","id":1084617,"title":"","content":"<b>299)</b> Mute with Horror<br /> <br /> A reclusive Nosferatu ancilla contacts the coterie about setting up a network of clandestine media contacts. The vampire, a mute, has decided after many years to embrace their Curse (their unnerving taint is carried not through voice or aspect, but through writing) and wants to branch out a home horror ghost writing hobby into a respectable commercial venture.<br /> <br /> Characters will be responsible for introductions/establishing secure lines of communication to writers, publishers, and/or printers, and making sure there's no Masquerade leaks (or preparing an argument against an establishment worried about <i>potential </i>Masquerade leaks). They also have to deal with the fact that all communication (even sign language) is phrased in an extremely ominous and threatening manner, regardless of their employer's intent, so that sheepishly cheerful grin continues to come off as slasher-ey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T17:08:01-07:00","id":1086885,"title":"","content":"300: Family Reunion<br /> An invitation has been sent out by mail, texts, and in the half remembered dreams of torpor to all members of a bloodline. Of course the invitation included a nearly insurmountable compulsion to journey to a specific city, otherwise no right minded Kindred would go anywhere near an extremely powerful elder. The progenitor of the bloodline wants all her childer to meet there but what she actually plans to do once everyone has arrived is anyone's guess. Most of the Kindred come along with coterie members armed to the teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:06:44-07:00","id":1086965,"title":"","content":"<b>301:</b> Something strange is going on and the Prince has put the domain on high alert. Over the last couple of months, every vampire within two neighboring cities has gone missing without a trace. Nobody seems to know what happened to them. Then, not long after the second city's population vanished, a drifter rolls into our domain from their direction. That's when the Mekhet sent to investigate him report that his aura is solid black and is emitting dozens of screaming voices!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T12:41:30-07:00","id":1098191,"title":"","content":"<b>302: A Vintage Fit for Lords</b><br /> <br /> A Crone ancilla, a local vintner of some renown, has not been seen in some time; their last sighting was on their mandragora plantation. The only clue to their disappearance so far are 1) any mortal sleeping on-site has weirdly vivid dreams, and 2) that many of the thorns on the rose trellis orchard-maze have begun to turn a tarnished silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T12:46:27-07:00","id":1098194,"title":"","content":"303: An elder your coterie once did a favor for has met final death, and you have been invited to the reading of his will by his ghoul, who is now in your service, in addition to whatever his former master has left you. The elder had quite the collection of interesting and useful items and anyone of them could have been left for you and your coterie, but you also remember him having a rather off beat sense of humor and he particularly loved The Frantics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 05-29-2017, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T19:16:27-07:00","id":1098314,"title":"","content":"<b>304: What's With all the Gangrel?</b><br /> <br /> Out of towners are nothing new, especially for a large city like (INSERT NAME), but the kindred have begun to notice something very unusual over the last several months. Every week on Monday, a new Gangrel wanders into the domain from parts unknown. And unlike typical Gangrel, they don't appear to be drifters. They've come here to stay, or at least maintain a presence for longer than expected of them. Their steady population increase is starting to make the other clans nervous, but after the Prince initiated a border patrol, they just began smuggling each other over. The Gangrel are planning something and it's up to your coterie to figure out what!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T06:50:09-07:00","id":1099135,"title":"","content":"A hooking to be used in conjunction with the world if darkness mirrored and bleeding edge supplement material. <br /> <br /> 305. Its the future and the masquerade is long dead. You live in &quot;The No Mans Land&quot; a former state in the u.s. of whom the entire population was embraced in the span of a week. &quot;How did we get here?&quot; Is the constant unspoken question in everyone's mind. Do you want to find out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T09:07:13-07:00","id":1099172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1099135#post1099135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A hooking to be used in conjunction with the world if darkness mirrored and bleeding edge supplement material.<br /> <br /> 305. Its the future and the masquerade is long dead. You live in &quot;The No Mans Land&quot; a former state in the u.s. of whom the entire population was embraced in the span of a week. &quot;How did we get here?&quot; Is the constant unspoken question in everyone's mind. Do you want to find out?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm guessing blood taxes are involved, otherwise, how are they feeding without any humans around? Draining the lowest BP vamps after they feed on animals and rationing the Vitae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T15:30:18-07:00","id":1099307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1099172#post1099172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm guessing blood taxes are involved, otherwise, how are they feeding without any humans around? Draining the lowest BP vamps after they feed on animals and rationing the Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>should have thought that a bit thoroughly. as far as realism goes, assuming coteries don't venture into neighbor states to feed, I could imagine the us government just parachute drops blood in crates through out the state. Then of course the part of me that just throws realism out the window says to imagine Mad Max, but at night, and with vampires. A literal tourist trap if you will.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T20:50:00-07:00","id":1099381,"title":"","content":"306) A werewolf pack that the Invictus prince sometimes contracts out to recently had a hunt go very badly. The wolves managed to get away from all the cops, feds and Peruvian gangsters after them, but in the process they trashed a row of stores and an apartment complex owned by the high priestess of the Circle. The prince needs your coterie to find the pack's hideout and get them to explain things before the Acolytes start burning things down themselves","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 06-02-2017, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T23:22:36-07:00","id":1099401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1098314#post1098314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>304: What's With all the Gangrel?</b><br /> <br /> Out of towners are nothing new, especially for a large city like (INSERT NAME), but the kindred have begun to notice something very unusual over the last several months. Every week on Monday, a new Gangrel wanders into the domain from parts unknown. And unlike typical Gangrel, they don't appear to be drifters. They've come here to stay, or at least maintain a presence for longer than expected of them. Their steady population increase is starting to make the other clans nervous, but after the Prince initiated a border patrol, they just began smuggling each other over. The Gangrel are planning something and it's up to your coterie to figure out what!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 307) What's With All the Daeva?<br /> <br /> Making connections and managing people are what all vampires do all the time, but the Kindred have begun to notice something very unusual over the last several months. The Daeva were always known for their wantonness, their brand of the Curse encouraging them to broaden their herd, but it seems they're absolutely determined to go over their Dunbar's number. Not only does the huge network of people give the Daeva a big social leverage, the Vitae they gain is nothing to scoff at either. But such political and survival benefits seem to only be a side-effect, as the Serpents are not picky about whom they newly associate with. Are the Daeva planning something big? Or are they being driven by some unseen force? Or are the other vampires, being callous and paranoid wrecks, overly reacting to what are just honest friendships?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:24:17-07:00","id":1099484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1099307#post1099307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> should have thought that a bit thoroughly. as far as realism goes, assuming coteries don't venture into neighbor states to feed, I could imagine the us government just parachute drops blood in crates through out the state. Then of course the part of me that just throws realism out the window says to imagine Mad Max, but at night, and with vampires. A literal tourist trap if you will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, vampires only need a single point of vitae to rise each night (less if you're with the Ordo Dracul), so as long as they conserve their energy and don't go flaunting their powers, it really wouldn't cost that much blood to sustain them. The problem comes from an entire state in the US being embraced. That would still constitute a population of several million vampires concentrated in one area. I'd recommend dropping the crates during the day, to prevent ambushes from desperate vamps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-02-2017, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:39:42-07:00","id":1099491,"title":"","content":"probably still a significant amount of diablerie going on as well though, since they'd all still be constantly hungry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T10:42:48-07:00","id":1099571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1099381#post1099381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">306) A werewolf pack that the Invictus prince sometimes contracts out to recently had a hunt go very badly. The wolves managed to get away from all the cops, feds and Peruvian gangsters after them, but in the process they trashed a row of stores and an apartment complex owned by the high priestess of the Circle. The prince needs your coterie to find the pack's hideout and get them to explain things before the carthains start burning things down themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>Talk about shit assignments &lt;.&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T19:32:09-07:00","id":1101082,"title":"","content":"308.) Unsolved Mysteries has been rebooted, in a way that embraces both the creepiness and the the 80s/90s feel of the original, and has become a hit with the kine. Problem is, many of the true crime segments of the show (which many would say were creepier than the paranormal stuff) are about the doings of human and ghoul agents of powerful kindred, including a local elder who has hired your coterie to knock the show off the air again. But be careful, a masquerade breach around this particular show would be catastrophic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T12:03:53-07:00","id":1102062,"title":"","content":"<b>309) It Burns When I Feed:</b> Something has tainted the city's mortal population, making the act of feeding very problematic for any kindred in the area. The blood scorches the body like a potent liquor the moment the vampire consumes it; and since the blood is absorbed throughout the entire body, you can see how this would be less than pleasant for any hungry kindred! The effects are only temporary (1 minute per point of vitae consumed), but it can still knock you on your ass if you aren't tough enough to endure it. Somebody needs to find the source of this curse and put an end to it before the kine start to notice the unexplained convulsions happening around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T05:22:44-07:00","id":1103087,"title":"","content":"310) A high neonate/low ancillae who has been relatively successful in building up an influence base has made an unexpected move, turns out she had a submissive streak to put a ghoul to shame and her time in the Ordo was spent finding a to keep a ghoul from forming Vinculum so he could learn her clan disaplins while she arranged his embrace into his choice of prestigious bloodline. Now a neonate has entered the dance macabre with a disaplin spread to envy, an impresive power base for so independent a neonate and the city's eyes upon him, poor guy doesn't stand a chance, good luck convincing him you're genuine in your offer to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T12:28:09-07:00","id":1103880,"title":"","content":"311) A Carthain Venture who really misses the 70s has dominated whichever famous spoiled heiress the ST prefers into becoming the new Patty Hearst, The Archbishop is amused, but thinks this could turn ugly for the local kindred quickly and wants your coterie to get the girl back and deprogram her for return to her family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T21:16:29-07:00","id":1106403,"title":"","content":"312) <a href=\"http://www.torontosun.com/2017/06/10/draculas-castle-closed-as-bears-take-over-grounds\" target=\"_blank\">Bears have taken over Dracula's castl</a>e, the ordo has sent you to find out why.<br /> <br /> 312a) OH SHIT! GHOUL BEARS!! (ghoul bear, winnie the ghoul bear...)<br /> <br /> 312b) the werebears claim they are here to call in a favor Dracula promised them centuries ago and demand to see him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 06-22-2017, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T00:43:42-07:00","id":1107929,"title":"","content":"313) A member of the Ordo Dracul has finally managed to get a Reverent to deablarise a sample of Pijavica (don't ask where he got it, he won't stop talking for some time if you do and you won't get the answer you wanted). Now he needs someone to train them in the basics of being a proper kindred while he writes up his final draft, try not to let the politics get to you, some people are claiming this is just a Grangal of some sort and the whole is this a new/revived clan (and therefore entitled to the same rights as the other five) debate is likely to explode before this Dragon has resurfaced. Meanwhile some of the city's other Reverents are demanding membership and your soft hearted charge feels obliged to help them out, this could get out of hand fast and then someone jokes that your Dragon benefactor is probably writing a paper on the fallout, that can't be true right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T10:39:38-07:00","id":1108819,"title":"","content":"314) The ghoul used by a prominent Elder to deal with modern internet-based correspondence (ie to check her email, messager, and read news using the computer) has disappeared. The Elder is obviously furious and is offering a small favor to any kindred that returns her ghoul. For a coterie with fairly good investigative skills or access to those with police resources he isn't hard to track down based on his debit card use or his cell phone, which he isn't answering. What is troubling is what the coterie sees lurking outside the shabby hotel window where the ghoul is hiding, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults?p=1108502#post1108502\">Slenderman</a>! The ghoul has Slender Sickness, and is now stalked by this horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-28-2017, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T04:20:32-07:00","id":1109690,"title":"","content":"315) Some idiot neonate was up too late (early?) and too hungery at some party, one frenzy later and the police arrive to find her covered in blood and flipping off the sun. Where as this in its self would be bad enough she proceeded to tell them (and the small crowd that had gathered) that she was a vampire, fortunately not going into detail, and rambled on about cover ups and conspires before calling over a preast from the crowd to hear her confession (again lacking details, just that she knew this might happen) and burning up on her way to the station.<br /> Ghouls being a thing this was mostly hushed up before sundown but the court is furious about the whole thing so keep your head down ok.<br /> 315b) Dumb bitch has become a trend setter! Suicide by sun is the hip way for the dead to die, we're not seeing the Maskarade breaches of the first time repeated but the Dance Macabre is loosing kindred from all ranks and clans. It's mostly the young but some big names have met the dawn. Sun partys where everyone stays the day with the option of stepping out side at the end are the hot new thing, allegations of Dominate use are rife and many Dragons are finding themselves on gust lists they didn't know existed and ask to explain their philosophy not out of interest but simply for the spectacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T16:38:43-07:00","id":1113937,"title":"","content":"316) You are sent to find out why the Dragon normad who arrived pre-evening hasn't presented himself to the prince as arranged, when you find him he tells you there is a time loop in play and he's been through all this before before asking if he can rely on you to do what he says? What do you do and is he telling the truth or having fun at your expense?<br /> 317) Why are we still keeping the Maskarade? This dumb neonate is willing to go on air and tell the world about Kindred, the court doesn't want it to happen but can't allow anyone to get the idea that they can hold the Maskarade hostage.<br /> 318) Something is hunting Vampires. Open the CofD book to page 140 and get to work on a Horror.<br /> 319) Rumor has it a near by city has come down with a terminal case of the Strix. That whole city is empty of Kindred and awaiting occupation, whenever you're ready.<br /> 320) Your Haven is trying to kill you. Is it a ghost? A rival? A legitimate run of bad luck? Whatever the reason it has to stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 07-13-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T17:57:38-07:00","id":1113963,"title":"","content":"<b>321)</b> All the domain's Kindred are falling into Torpor and not waking up on their own. Vitae will get them running, but they fall back into Torpor after a few nights. No one is sure how this &quot;sleeping sickness&quot; is spreading, or how to stop it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T18:52:00-07:00","id":1113977,"title":"","content":"<b>322)</b> A number of Acolytes are stirring up a ruckus at the local court, picking fights with members from all of the domain's Covenants and killing seemingly random people on the streets. A brief investigation shows that the Acolytes have little to no contact with each other and that all the people killed have been ghouls. One of the Acolytes are a bit more talkative and claims that she's receiving orders in her dreams from a mysterious figure she identifies as the Hag. Presumably the other Acolytes receive similar orders.<br /> Are the orders really from one of their religious figures? Why have particular Kindred and ghouls been targeted? What is the end goal of these mysterious orders?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T12:34:12-07:00","id":1115632,"title":"","content":"323) Someone (probably a Dragon or Acolyte but use whatever works for your chronicle) has found a way to make glass that allows all visible light through very clearly but weakens the effects of of sunlight on vampires.<br /> Of course anyone who could afford it wants some in their haven and of course someone would get to work on a big glass house but now the Ordo has made a 24 hour Elysium open to anyone supernatural. The Lancea Sanctum are calling it a Maskarade breach, the Inviticus are desperate to find a way to stop the Dragons being the defining example of kindred kind to the outsiders, the Movement have expressed guarded approval of such openness and the Circle are a mixed bag, on the other side the Mages have a few regulars, the wolves rarely show up but behave well enough when they do, an odd bunch that don't seem to end up on the other side of a door they walk through as often as they should seem to enjoy it, a woman who always seems to be present monitors everything but never explains herself is subject to some speculation and this guy who claims &quot;we're all children of the Dark Mother&quot; seems genuinely happy this has happened.<br /> Stop/guard/exploit/monitor it.<br /> 324) That new TV show about vampires/a vampire has everyone talking, be on the biting edge of Elysium fashion in both dress and attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 07-13-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T16:21:11-07:00","id":1117002,"title":"","content":"325)<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Worm from the WtF Predators book is what happens when a Nos elder uses the Terrible Flesh Devotion from Night Horrors: Immortal sinners long enough... Guess how long the local Nos primogen has doing that devotion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T23:45:06-07:00","id":1117112,"title":"","content":"<b>326)</b> You a fan of the Blood Rayne series; you ever played the second game? Well apparently, the Acolytes have, and they decided to emulate the Kagan Cult's master plan. That is to say, grinding up a bunch of society's unwanted low lives in order to produce an alchemical blood cloud that blots out the sun! Hobos, prostitutes, drug addicts, gang members, runaways, drifters, anybody who society has cast off has been going missing from the city. Rounded up off the streets and shipped to processing facilities where they are hacked to pieces and ground into a fine paste. This is going to be one of the biggest Cruac rituals in recent history, one powerful enough to initiate a city wide vampire apocalypse!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-17-2017, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T14:33:02-07:00","id":1117441,"title":"","content":"<b>327)</b> The mortal mayor of the city is a widower who has recently remarried a relatively young amazingly beautiful and charming woman who has secretly gotten him involved with the underground nearly anonymous swinger's scene. That's how an indiscreet Davae Casanova that knows your coterie ended in an intimate situation with her as the husband watched... Strange thing is that her blood was supernatural, and not in a vampiric way! He says she tasted like wax and petroleum jelly. A &quot;bit of research&quot; (which is to say a quick internet search of local news) reveals the mayor met her via some <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1117279#post1117279\">new internet dating site</a> and the three decade age difference caused quite a stir (The mayor is in his late sixties).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-17-2017, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:24:28-07:00","id":1120918,"title":"","content":"<b>328) </b>So one member of your coterie has lived in the same apartment building for the last 30 years, and it has changed owners and superintendents several times in that period, and it being the big city no one speaks with their neighbors. One night a parchment note written in a flowing script was slid under that coterie member's door<br /> <br /> &quot;Good evening my youthful neighbor,<br /> <br /> For thirty years we've respected each other's privacy, and I have appreciated your discretion as I am certain you've appreciated mine. In a week we'll both be killed with flames if we don't clandestinely move to somewhere more secure. I mention this to you because I've grown quite attached to you over the years; I want you to be safe and would like to stay neighbors if possible. If you'd like to meet at [insert site where vampire commonly watches touchstone], to discuss our moving arrangements I'll be waiting there by the time you read this note.<br /> <br /> Sincerely,<br /> Mary Aminov&quot;<br /> <br /> One of the reasons you never have to move is because the owner and superintendent of the build chances almost every other year, and without interacting with your neighbors no one would notice your ageless nature. You've never taken notice of what you presumed were your mortal neighbors either, but if you meet Mary Aminov you find she's a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1120890#post1120890\">little old lady</a> who lives down the hall from your apartment. She must have noticed your ageless nature after 30 years of watching you...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-17-2024, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T16:31:57-07:00","id":1132836,"title":"","content":"329) Someone has pissed off an elder! Don't worry it's not you but the killing spree underway could have come from a Hollywood script. Already the city is down more than one power player and no one you have an in with knows when it might finish, try not to get roped into anything stupid.<br /> 330) You were standing too close to a ranting Prince and found your self being pointed at! Turns out you were just a hypothetical someone who should be able to do the simple task this poor Ancilla has failed at and when she tries to defend/explain what happened the Prince promotes you to shut her down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T18:16:01-07:00","id":1132876,"title":"","content":"<b>331)</b> This is bad, really, really bad. The kindred of the city have been noticing a strange phenomenon as of late. Every night, a randomly selected vampire fails to rise on their own, Being trapped in torpor unless they are force fed vitae to kick start their awakening. There's no way of knowing who is going to be affected next, or why it happens in the first place. But the Prince can't keep tabs on everybody (and may not even be trying to). If somebody doesn't put a stop to this, there's a good chance the entire kindred population is faced with two inevitable outcomes. Either they all resign themselves to eternal slumber, or they become addicted to vampire blood!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T09:48:10-07:00","id":1133052,"title":"","content":"So has anyone used or is planing to use anything we've come up with in this thread and if so how did it go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T11:15:18-07:00","id":1133091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1133052#post1133052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So has anyone used or is planing to use anything we've come up with in this thread and if so how did it go?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would need a thread of it's own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T12:41:47-07:00","id":1133118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1133091#post1133091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would need a thread of it's own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you've used so many?<br /> Not knowing why the other threads got merged together last time there was a split off I don't want to risk it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:39:26-07:00","id":1134179,"title":"","content":"332) A personal fight has managed to boil over into a full-blow war. The twist? The leader of all three sides is a singular member of the Circle of the Crone, who has split her mind into three pieces, which previously worked together in concert as a powerful one-vampire coven, but have now fragmented, taking the local Circle with them. Each part of the conflict knows the plans of all the others by virtue of having direct access to the enemy's leader, resulting in every fight becoming a drawn-out, blood-soaked travesty that threatens to consume the entire city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T20:19:21-07:00","id":1134338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1134179#post1134179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">332) A personal fight has managed to boil over into a full-blow war. The twist? The leader of all three sides is a singular member of the Circle of the Crone, who has split her mind into three pieces, which previously worked together in concert as a powerful one-vampire coven, but have now fragmented, taking the local Circle with them. Each part of the conflict knows the plans of all the others by virtue of having direct access to the enemy's leader, resulting in every fight becoming a drawn-out, blood-soaked travesty that threatens to consume the entire city.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsugumi_Ohba\" target=\"_blank\">Tsugumi Ohba</a> would be proud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T03:42:57-07:00","id":1135722,"title":"","content":"A Dragon in the city claims to have come up with a 'cure' for Vampirism! A 'failure' in his eyes, it supposedly removes all traces of vampiric weakness - along with any benefits. In addition, it only works for a limited time. He was just about to discharge it, when a particularly ambitious coterie mate of his saw a chance: DOWN with the Invictus, viva la revolution!<br /> The plan is simple: inject the Herds with this serum (just put it in their food), so any Kindred feeding on them is turned human again! Now-human Invictus would not stand a chance against the Carthians, who'd naturally assume the lead. Or so he reasons.<br /> The Dragon agrees to help them in return for more freedom in the his research. However, when put into action, some factors complicate the plan:<br /> The Humanization only lasts a certain time - the more powerful, the shorter the amount of time they are human. Elders wouldn't even stay human for more than an hour. Still, more than enough to take them down, right? However, there is no reliable way to tell when they turn human: It might kick in with a delay of a minute, or a day, or not at all in some cases.<br /> Finally, someone royally screwed up, and tainted the water supply with the serum- drinking blood at any time for two weeks carries the risk of being turned human - donated blood has just become much more valuable thanks to the date stamp on it.<br /> <br /> Now, the two's coterie tries to sabotage any attempts at making sense of the events, because they know that if they are found out, they are dead for good.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the whole thing has one more problem: any kindred that turns human and back again? Starts at 0 Humanity, and stays there for a week.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T19:15:02-07:00","id":1140390,"title":"","content":"334) Just a simple tale of a man who hates an animal. <br /> A gangrel elder hires the coterie to help him hunt a lupine that ate his leg a year ago. This lupine is gigantic, albino, and has a taste for vampire flesh, and its territory is in the swamps. Your coterie jumps at the chance, figuring it'll be an easy job and will get you much support from the elder in the future. Of course, after several nights in the swamplands the elder starts to show just how obsessed he is with killing this creature. <br /> <br /> 335) One of your coterie members gets permission from the Prince to sire. They choose a soft-eyed girl that they claim to love. Of course once they embrace the girl they tell her all about being a vampire and the powers of the blood. The girl, not being ready to abandon her mortal life and not being the smartest crayon in the box, chooses to embrace her whole family...all 5 of them. The girl has no willpower left, to the point where she can barely leave her haven to feed, and there's also 5 other licks who are freaking out about not being able to get a suntan ever again. Does your coterie try to train them in the ways of the Danse, cut them loose, or just dust them all before the Prince finds out?<br /> <br /> 336) A coterie of powerful Kindred has come to the area but has stayed in the wilderness outside the city limits. The Prince didn't seem to mind at first, but then half the factory district went up in flames one night. Then a couple high level employees of the local energy company were found in a motel with their throats ripped out. And then someone snuck into the sewers and sabotaged the pipes leaving a quarter of the city without water for two days. The coterie isn't denying being the instigators, and they proudly state they are causing these actions to retake the land for Mother Gaia, after eliminating the worst of the polluters from the city's population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T13:55:41-07:00","id":1140629,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">337) Due to Hurricane Irma, or some other natural disaster, a nearby city has been devastated. Their Kindred population has fled as refugees to your city. The problem is that there are more refugee Kindred coming in than there is native vampires.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">338) A black metal band that was on tour came to town a week ago, kidnapped a vampire, forced her to embrace them all, and then diablerized the Kindred before hitting the road. Since then they cancelled their tour and went to ground. No one knows where they are. The Kindred they killed was the Prince\u2019s childe. Try to bring them back alive. </span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T23:42:04-07:00","id":1141332,"title":"","content":"<b>339)</b> <b>Party Crashers:</b><br /> <br /> The Prince is hosting a grand party which will culminate in dividing up territory in the domain to the various covenants present in the city. There's just one problem; your covenant never received an invite. It's time to crash this party and remind everybody that your people will not be steam rolled into submission. Unfortunately, the Prince isn't planning on letting you in through the front door, or any door for that matter. You're going to need a more clever way to sneak past security. And once you do that, it's a simple matter of making the Prince look like a fool in front of every kindred in the city!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>340) The Bouncers:</b><br /> <br /> The Prince is on the verge of weeding out a covenant they've had a particular grudge against for who knows how long. They are preparing to host negotiations for dividing territory up among the other covenants, but the offended kindred got word of the operation and are staging an infiltration to sabotage the negotiations. Your coterie has been assigned to security detail to ensure nothing goes wrong and the Prince is able to rid themselves of this menace once and for all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2017, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T07:14:31-07:00","id":1141396,"title":"","content":"<b>341:</b> A source has given you a powerful piece of information: The names of every hunter in the area, as well as the names of several organizations they belong to. Of course, this only makes your coterie a target, as the area hunters know that the information is in your hands. You only expected a few idiots with a shotgun or two, but then you faced down a man in black that turned one of your associates into a bloody smear with a weird looking machine. It's gonna be a long night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:50:04-07:00","id":1149526,"title":"","content":"342) The Prince is in love like this neonate can walk into her haven at will and shit! She hasn't neglected any of her duties for him and he seems an alright guy who hasn't taken any liberties but someone's going to do something to try and exploit this and you hope you don't get called in to help them.<br /> 343) Word has come that the Dragons and the Movement have teamed up in a number of cities to inact the same form of government, it seems someone wants data from more than one source.<br /> 344) It's official, \u017diva is not a Coil of the Dragon, you can't count it towards your rank and the Ordo in no way cares who knows what rank in it. Want to learn something amazing my non-dragon friends?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 10-13-2017, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T16:54:08-07:00","id":1150031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1133118#post1133118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not knowing why the other threads got merged together last time there was a split off I don't want to risk it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a disagreement over coordination, and that is the most that needs to be said on the matter, less we angry the mod gods.<br /> <br /> I reckon most would enjoy the trend you propose, though my experience is that getting them off the ground is rare. Still, I'd read them for what it is worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T22:10:57-07:00","id":1150072,"title":"","content":"<b>345:</b> Aliens aren't real, they're a myth made up to explain away all the crazy stuff that happens in the shadows. That's how it's always been as far as you can tell.<br /> <br /> Until you saw the flying saucer land and the little gray men stalk out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T01:45:31-07:00","id":1150100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1150031#post1150031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I reckon most would enjoy the trend you propose, though my experience is that getting them off the ground is rare. Still, I'd read them for what it is worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll start then. I've used 264 with a short Invitus game.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A group of influenceful Kindred announce that they require the procurement of a Mage, a competent fighter, a thief and a man of the cloth (or suitable substitutes). Please arrange for their investigation free disappearance and all other such matters. Prior to their disappearance they should all meet in a tavern. </div> </div> </div>The party did great, they set up a fake profile for a rich eccentric who needed such people to help with his rare book collection and managed to get some good rolls on their serch for a psychic/mage even after the first one they found noped out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T12:37:42-07:00","id":1150192,"title":"","content":"<b>346:</b> Your group was instructed to accomplish a task--one important enough to find them partnered with a gaggle of mortals working toward the same ends (escort/courier mission against odds, police investigation, corporate takeover consultancy group, etc.). Fortunately it looks like you'll succeed. Unfortunately your vampiric nature has come to the attention of one competent mortal: who seems to have been a ghoul or knows enough as such, <i>says</i> they do not have a master, and is quite pleased with that state. You'll definitely need the help to finish the job, and the mortal wants your word of nothing getting back about them in exchange for the &quot;favor&quot; of completing things satisfactorily. <br /> <br /> Now what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T06:16:05-07:00","id":1151628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1150100#post1150100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll start then. I've used 264 with a short Invitus game.<br /> The party did great, they set up a fake profile for a rich eccentric who needed such people to help with his rare book collection and managed to get some good rolls on their serch for a psychic/mage even after the first one they found noped out.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Best make a new trend. Don't want to clutter this one. (personal opinion.)<br /> <br /> 2) You actually used that one? I would read that as someone being witty and not as a 'genuine submission'. What was the fighter's backstory in a modern setting? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T08:35:06-07:00","id":1151649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1151628#post1151628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Best make a new trend. Don't want to clutter this one. (personal opinion.)<br /> <br /> 2) You actually used that one? I would read that as someone being witty and not as a 'genuine submission'. What was the fighter's backstory in a modern setting? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>A boxer I think, they told him he was being hired as a bodyguard/security. The mission was a test by an Invitus high up to find a group of vassals who could think out side the box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T10:02:53-07:00","id":1151959,"title":"","content":"That's gas. Pretty silly Invictus, getting involved with a Mage though. :O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T12:55:18-07:00","id":1151999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1151959#post1151959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's gas. Pretty silly Invictus, getting involved with a Mage though. :O</div> </div> </div> </div>It was only a psychic and they were judging on how they did it as much as what they did. Who wants an errand neonate who can't sort out a problem like that out for themselves anyway?<br /> <br /> 347) The Prince is a Dragon, she didn't tell the Invitus that she was going duel covenant and the Sanctified are furies to find out the real reason she was giving so much weight to their &quot;these sites need a round the clock response&quot; argument. Time to work out who still has influence.<br /> <br /> 348) A respected member of the Ordo Dracol has published his thesis on the Vitae requirements of the Disciplins and their effect on the mindset of the clans, it's very interesting if divisive work.<br /> <br /> 349) There's blood in those there towns! Kindred with their own transport have taken to taking up Heven outside of the city limits and commuting, this new Blood Rush is a Masquirade breach waiting to happen! The Church wants it stopped before something goes wrong, the Invitus wants it stopped now that they have helped themselves to the best bits to keep the riff raff out, the Dragons were already hunting out there apparently but don't feel they can get enough data on kindred movements to make up for the loss of easy feeding, the Carthians think they can beat the Invictus away from the city and the Circle say let it happen.<br /> <br /> 350) Your actions freed a trapped Strix, it thinks that as a being of fireless smoke someone is due 3 wishes.<br /> <br /> 351) The Prince will grant you one boon each just don't try and regain those memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T13:01:14-07:00","id":1152266,"title":"","content":"352) For the past two months a recently awakened Elder has been a member of the Carthian Movement, an Invictus Elder noticed him from their surveillance last night. The new Carthian Elder seems to genuinely be onboard with the aims of the Movement and is potent enough that he could tip the scales in a fight unless the Invitus comited their own Elders to the fight.<br /> <br /> 353) Something has caused every torpored vampire in the city to awaken, stakes are healed out, reverents long forgotten stir once more and whether voluntary or involuntary every kindred sleeping the ages away is now up and hungry. The city can't support this many vampires.<br /> <br /> 354) The prince doesn't have time for this shit, as a kindred with no obvious bias it's now your problem. Sort out whatever dispute you've been given with the full authority of the court!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T18:21:20-08:00","id":1168690,"title":"","content":"355) The high priestess of the Circle has somehow roped your coterie into tracking down one of this season's hottest toys for their Dhampir child. Chaos ensues (think jingle all the way with vampires)<br /> <br /> \u200b356 ) so the toy you got for the Dhampir is possessed by a nasty spirit, and the circle wants your help dealing with it before the High Priestess's child gets seriously hurt.<br /> <br /> \u200b357) With the help of the local werewolves you have traced the spiritual possession of the toy back to it's manufacturer. the mysterious Avalon Incorporated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T23:44:05-07:00","id":1231034,"title":"","content":"358) The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/18795-post-your-scales-of-the-dragon-forum-port?p=1231030#post1231030\">Thinning the Blood Scale</a> was first discovered by a Hematologist Mehket Dragon seeking a way to embrace without Clan Weaknesses. She considers it a mixed result with enough utility that she traded its secrets for another Dragon's research, and thus while it isn't a mainstream Scale by any means, within the Pacific Northwest Cacophony the unsubstantiated rumors of Dragons collecting unwanted and insolent Fledgelings to feed their Revenant childrer to uplift them via Diablerie have become a bit of a boogie man or urban legend among vampires to scare Neonates into respectful obedience so they aren't forsaken by polite vampire society or their Sires.<br /> <br /> It is true that, as a vampire if no one would miss you, you have a higher than average chance to simply disappear in the Pacific North West, but hey that could be true for many different disturbing reasons, and Dragon ghouls grabbing unwanted vampires during the day for Revenants to Diablerize at night is no more plausible than the rumors of feral Circle of the Crone Gangrels joining forces with savage werewolves that hate all things made by man snatching evanescent outcast vampires for profane Wildhunts in the woods which end with Diablerie, or the rumor that Antediluvian Elders from ancient lost Clans that lived among the Salish speaking natives are responsible...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-29-2018, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T04:49:15-07:00","id":1231761,"title":"","content":"<b>359)</b> Some big time Invictus got themselves ashed and now their burn-book is missing. That thing has dirt on <i>everyone</i> in the Domain, and not just GPS coordinates on where the bodies are buried, but who done it and how. Now there is a scramble to find it before someone's rivals do.<br /> <br /> <b>A)</b> From bad to worse - the thing has ended up in the hands of the FBI, and mortal forces in the area have been so spooked by the internecine Kindred warfare that they are taking extra precautions. <i>No one</i> has any tools with eyes on the prize, and someone better grab it quick, before the Feds decode it and have a frighteningly detailed documentary on the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> Turns out some a-hole <i>Strix</i> is behind the leak. They're interested in seeing how the region's vamps will adapt to having a floodlight shined on their affairs, and the Owl is acting interference to any attempt to locate the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-02-2018, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T15:54:26-07:00","id":1231966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1231761#post1231761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>359)</b> Some big time Invictus got themselves ashed and now their burn-book is missing. That thing has dirt on <i>everyone</i> in the Domain, and not just GPS coordinates on where the bodies are buried, but who done it and how. Now there is a scramble to find it before someone's rivals do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too read Reap the Whirlwind.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T18:36:12-07:00","id":1232011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1231966#post1231966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I too read Reap the Whirlwind.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, is that the plot of a book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T16:04:16-07:00","id":1232735,"title":"","content":"<b>360)</b> It's the 4th of July and the US President is on TV. No, not the current one - one of the old ones, like on the currency, old. Turns out, some nitwit Kindred back in the day Embraced them and then tried to keep the whole thing under wraps. Now the former President is back, claiming to have transcended their condition and is pissed at the current state of the nation. This is going to be an interesting election cycle...<br /> <br /> <b>A)</b> The Invictus are collectively shitting bricks. Someone let this <i>epic</i> violation of the First Tradition get this far, and there is no way the genie is getting back in the bottle. Or coffin. Coteries are being scrambled to try to vainly contain the situation, figure out who screwed up, and burn the trails to any higher ups.<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> The Lancea Et Sanctum are furious over this blasphemy - a Kindred claiming to have discovered a way of defying God's Curse and purpose for their kind. Their auguries indicate the ex-President is indeed Kindred, even as they walk in the daylight. How is this possible?<br /> <br /> <b>C)</b> The Circle of the Crone are nervous, not only for the increased attention, but also for someone so public claiming to have transcended their nature.<br /> <br /> <b>D)</b> The Carthian Movement is in conflict - some think the political ramifications are disastrous, while others scent opportunity - what might Carthian Law backed by an entire <i>nation</i> accomplished?<br /> <br /> <b>E)</b> The Ordo Dracul are intrigued. This Kindred is able to wield their powers, yet has defied the sun on live camera. Have they uncovered secrets worth copying, or is this a dead-end heretical Coil?<br /> <br /> [The President in question isn't really important, though which one it is can add some flavor. One of the Founding Fathers is best for the historical commentary on modern times, while Abraham Lincoln is pop-culturally amusing]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-05-2018, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T16:39:56-07:00","id":1232744,"title":"","content":"Amusing as in Abraham Lincoln Vampire Hunter amusing? <a href=\"https://m.imdb.com/title/tt1611224/\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.imdb.com/title/tt1611224/</a><br /> <br /> Or the hilarity that will ensue about an American politician walking around with a large portion of their brain missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T17:13:32-07:00","id":1232751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1232744#post1232744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amusing as in Abraham Lincoln Vampire Hunter amusing? <a href=\"https://m.imdb.com/title/tt1611224/\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.imdb.com/title/tt1611224/</a><br /> <br /> Or the hilarity that will ensue about an American politician walking around with a large portion of their brain missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in - who could tell the difference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:57:45-07:00","id":1233282,"title":"","content":"Not sure if it would work, but what about a story hook involving reversed horror story on the vampire, starring a really experienced cainite heresy cell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T15:18:25-07:00","id":1233287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1233282#post1233282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if it would work, but what about a story hook involving reversed horror story on the vampire, starring a really experienced cainite heresy cell</div> </div> </div> </div>There might already be one. I recall in the jokes thread a knock-knock joke that ended with &quot;Who is Cain?&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T15:32:28-07:00","id":1233290,"title":"","content":"Oh ok lol. Was it brought into this thread, or did never turn into a fully fledged story hook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T16:11:35-07:00","id":1246797,"title":"","content":"361) A new prince has just taken power after a nightly civil war between the covenants ended. He's a brute pure and simple, but he is powerful enough that no one in the city wants to tangle with him as the last Elder who did is now a torpored limbless torso with a head that the prince uses like a hunting trophy. This would be terrifying enough, but now he wants to sponsor your coterie to guide your development and help your talents bloom. Do you accept knowing that you will make enemies you probably can't handle on your own? Or do you refuse and possible reserve a space for yourself as another of the prince's trophies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","name":"Madman777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T15:16:11-07:00","id":1247513,"title":"","content":"362) A Strix has shown up, it's taken up residence in a female reverent but has offered to vacate if anyone wishes to uplift her. The Strix doesn't seem to have any agenda but will converse with the kindred of the city about kindred and Strix nature, the reverent's body is sometimes damaged but such damage seems not to bother the entity within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T14:24:23-07:00","id":1254845,"title":"","content":"363) Standard Dungeon Crawl #11496<br /> The Nosferatu have dug too deep. They have uncovered a series of artificial caves and ruins beneath the city. Carbon dating shows the ruins as millennia old. Way older than the anthropological record says that humans or Kindred would be here. Worse, all the adventurous Kindred wanted to see what the fuss was about and one of your coterie members or and NPC was taken down into the depths by some sort of lizard like monster. The bad news is that the Prince wanted the depths mapped anyway so you've just volunteered. The good news is that there seems to be strange creatures in the depths, that are able to sustain Kindred. Almost like a full ecosystem. <br /> Basically Dungeon Meshi with vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11901-icon787","name":"Icon787","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T16:09:15-07:00","id":1257853,"title":"","content":"364) The Carnival is in town, and the Prince is trying to get rid of them. Even worse, The Carnival wants a Daeva character to join them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T06:47:14-07:00","id":1258191,"title":"","content":"365)<br /> The local Ordo messed up- as part of their experiments, they have tried to create a perfect weapon: a Kindred tailored to destroying his own kind. The found a homeless veteran, embraced him, and put him through a tight regime of training, scales, more training. They succeded all too well.<br /> They didnt expect him to overcome His guards, hunting down kindred and Going On a Diablerizing spree that even the sheriff, despite being an elder, could not hold off against. Sure, the enhancements, scales, potions Etc are going to wearing off in a few days, leaving him just a moderately-powerful Fighter With A Lot Of Experience, but no one knows this except for a few Defiant, and who knows who he will target meanwhile? <br /> And will the Coterie use this Situation to garner favour with the powers that be, or are they seeking a Revolution? What will they do when they find the recipe to unlimited physical might?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T00:39:42-07:00","id":1259364,"title":"","content":"366)<br /> The Prince has forbidden cellular phones from Gatherings after a few neonates have gone &quot;missing&quot;. The cacophony whispers that they didn't disappear, instead their cloths and phone were found dusted with their own cremains. Rumors say the last image on their phones were selfies in the same spot and cloths as their cremains were found, and that the phone had a new camera app called &quot;Nite Owl Pics&quot;, a camera app which claims to be optimized for poor or artificial light, &quot;Perfect for Immortalizing your Night Life&quot; is their slogan. The juiciest and most insane whispered detail is the phone had an Aura, and that aura had Diablerie stains!! The Keeper of Elysium has been treating phones as weapons since these incidents have occurred, and several Elders have nearly gone mad with technophobia, purging their havens of anything electronic and &quot;dining in&quot; as much.as possible. No one is sure if a Strix has an Embodiment or Dread Power which allows it to Diaberize vampires through the app (though that is the most popular speculation), it is technological Devotion, Scale, Miracle, or Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Coincidentally the rate of Spontaneous Embraces among night-club goers has risen, especially since a few seemed to have died in their sleep without blood-loss, and after investigating deeper those Spontaneously Embraced happen to be of the same clans as the vampires which died under those strange circumstances. The mortals also took selfies the night before they died in their sleep without blood-loss, and the selfie has the same minute on the timestamp and was taken with the Night Owl Pics app. The selfies stand out enough to be noticed because the person's eyes appear glowing yellow with dark black iris slits. Even after this is all discovered and pieced together, it only raises more questions....<br /> <br /> The App is available for free for download in Google Play, with a 3.4 star rating and over 90,000 downloads. Its icon is a shadowy black cartoon owl winking with a smile, with the letter of the apps name spelled with pink neon lights. The app's company is de Vil LLC, a privately traded company based out of PO box in the isolated town of Rachel Nevada, and an IP address in Nigeria...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-01-2019, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T22:54:26-08:00","id":1274307,"title":"","content":"367)<br /> A new vampire whose never been your city before. He goes by the moniker &quot;Doctor Zlato&quot; and is a strangely mannered Mekhet Ordo Dracul, who according to the cacophony was originally an Alchemist in 17th century Prague. Currently he is known for three things: Being quite an expert of supernatural sites, having a network of haven safe houses around the world that he loans out as favors, and has has the connections to make secure discrete vampire or relic transportation between cities and countries. Those interested in leaving their current city or acquiring exotic mystical relics from afar are often drawn into his circles of influence because of these two latter traits. <br /> <br /> In this particular visit he came to town bearing mystically useful gifts well suited for all the right people to gift to, and authentic letters of introduction vouching for him from vampires with meaning connections to elder vampires of this city. Many are suspicious of him but he gains favor with others. After he has procured a few haven spots for his travel network, he begins questioning younger less prestigious vampires about modern urban legends of the supposedly haunted or cursed sites. He doesn't seem particularly interested in ghosts themselves, though the history at the actual site that interest him. Following him is quite difficult due to his mastery of Obfuscate, but if he was able be followed to his haven he simply use a Devotion that appears similar to Unmarked Grave but can be used indoors without enough space to meld into and doesn't emerge from a location which can be be found. <br /> <br /> Since he has arrived he's never been seen hunting, but whispers from Kindred whom keep apprised of the of homeless community spin tales of vagrants squatting in abandoned structure disappearing has increased to a rate which implies supernatural feeding devouring a while person each night, even if a night or three are skipped later a similar sized group a vagrants will disappear all at once.<br /> <br /> He has the Devotions <i>Embrace to Genius Loci</i> and <i>Go to Nowhere.</i> He has a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1274149#post1274149\">Hungry Doorway To Nowhere</a> with him, which he uses for safe haven in the day and freely gluts himself on the vagrants it collects for him so he can leave each evening. He is looking for a Strange Place which has the Awakened Environment so he can make another Hungry Doorway To Nowhere for one of his many Childer in Eastern Europe, but is also happy to extend his research into other supernatural location based Devotions. <br /> <br /> If the domain of Seattle isn't already defined within your Chronicle, might I recommend several of Doctor Zlato's childer be involved in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1098658-city-concept-ruled-by-ordo-dracul?p=1099840#post1099840\">Ordo ruling council of Seattle</a>, and he has has contributed in their research to make the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1120091-2e-site-based-devotions\">Memory Biopsy Devotion</a> there, and that Doctor Zlato is intending to gift the Hungry Doorway To Nowhere to his Elder childer there instead of Europe?<br /> <br /> Anyway, this turns into a story in several ways, the PC could want to deal with Doctor Zlato, or perhaps they object to the increase of disappearances of the homeless and blame him without enough status to accuse him without solid proof which is very hard to get. Perhaps the PCs are in a horrible situation and you can use Doctor Zlato and his Hungry Doorway To Nowhere to allow them escape the city when that seems impossible assuming they PCs are willing to bring human sacrifices so he can have they egress to Seattle and have Memory Biopsy remove their knowledge of how they got there due to Doctor Zlato's connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T03:43:59-08:00","id":1276594,"title":"","content":"368. One or more Strix have decided to get into the holiday spirit. Re-enactments of the nactivity and their own take on Santa and Christmas songs have been arranged to torment the kindred of the city. Will it end after the 12 nights of Christmas or do they wish it to be Christmas every day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T13:16:49-07:00","id":1301387,"title":"","content":"The local Ordo is pretty sociable, compared to the stereotype: they throw parties and are somewhat involved in politics - mostly kine politics, and usually focused on acquiring property, though. They have worked hard to establish malls, parks, homes, even brothels and clubs (reasoning that those are prime hunting grounds), a hospital (perfect for experimentation and blood acquisition), and more. What is weird is that they do not contest these areas as they should: they're fine with sharing hunting grounds, use ownership of buildings as bargaining chips in deals, and even gifted a beautiful park to the Carthians (&quot;Perfect for summernight conventions, parties, community meetings and the like!&quot;). Some Kindred joke that the Ordo Dracul is filled with people who like to build toys and then throw them away to start on a new project, being more interested in the act of constructing than poessesion.<br /> The true reason for this behaviour is known only to the highest-ranking and oldest of the Defiant and a scattering of their Sworn: they had gotten their hands on some obscure and ancient geomantic formulae some decades ago, and since then ceaselessly worked on their 'Testrun'. They essentially shaped the city over the years to change flows, connect Dragon's Nests, even create new ones. And finally, their work bore fruit - unexpected as it was.<br /> <br /> A huge section, nearly a quarter of the whole city, is extremely dangerous to Kindred: their Vitae grows inert, leaving them sluggish, weak and slow. They cannot feed there, and are incapable of using their vampiric abilities. Essentially, it strips them off all their power - and it affects mainly the Lancea et Sanctum.<br /> While the city's other Kindred have no idea how or why this happened, they try everything in their power to find out and use that knowledge to extend their sphere of influence. The Ordo, meanwhile, tries to hide their involvement, while furiously taking notes of the effects. They can easily hide their fervent interest under the mantle of their Covenant's bread and butter for now, but how long will that last?<br /> <br /> Worst of all: the area slowly, but surely grows. No one has noticed this yet, but once they do, the city's Kindred are sure to freak out - and the Danse will be more deadly than ever.<br /> Your Cotiere is sure to be affected one way or another: maybe their herd is within the area, maybe without access to their (Discipline of Choice, e.g. Majesty to influence Kine) one of them cannot do the tasks they were given and cease to be of worth to their sire, maybe their haven is on the fringe of being affected. But maybe the political turmoil is good for their own powerplays by using the climate as a smokescreen, hiding their schemes from sight and getting away with violations of the traditions due to everyone's preoccupation. They are free to clean up after old mistakes, or to force rivals' hands in the chaos. Then again, it might be bad for their own goals as others try to stake them for the relatively safe position of their haven, use them as guinea pigs, or an outlet for their own panic.<br /> <br /> Should they decide to try to solve this problem (no doubt for the power that would give them, as whole coteries, perhaps even Covenants would owe them a debt), they might be tricked into just dissolving the geomantic structure via demolition of a high-profile place like a city hall or a place a Covenant (or different Splat!) considers holy/important, which certainly would lead to certain fallout, political or otherwise.<br /> They also might stumble upon the Ordo's involvement: how are they going to use that knowledge? Hold it over their heads, strongarm the Ordo into doing what they want and basically order the Covenant around via blackmail? Or use it to run them out of the city, maybe even eradicating the Covenant wholesale in this city?<br /> That would certainly leave a power vacuum - and with the system thrown of balance that heavily, everything might seem possible now...<br /> <br /> Background information: This is basically a testrun of what can be done to the Ordo. Among other possible applications the Ordo considers using this to figure out how to 'ward' a place from Strix - less for safety, and more for future experimentation. Alternative plot hook: Will the effect persist or run out after a while, and will the Ordo end the experiment when they have their data, or will they utilize this weapon they've created to eradicate any opposition to a claim for power?<br /> The underlying magical rules could well be Infrastructure (doubtlessly drawing the interest of Demons and the G-M alike) or it could be ancient Irem magics (going to draw the interest of Mummies), Chthonian in nature (surely throwing the Ghosts, Bound and Reapers out of balance), or stranger yet. Maybe it is a sort of large-scale Scale, maybe a blood magic rite based on 1st Editions Gilded Cage or Domus Disciplines. As always, go with what feels best.<br /> <br /> Mechanical ideas: Every Kindred (and Ghoul) entering the affected area is treated as having Blood Potency 0 and looses access to all Disciplines and Vitae-fueled abilities. Feeding is impossible, as they can draw in new blood, but it remains inert and useless to their body. On top of that, every Kindred and Ghoul suffers the Fatigued Condition.<br /> People right outside the area can be fed upon normally. Upon leaving the area, the Kindred reacquires their abilities and sheds the Condition within an hour.<br /> <br /> Other ideas for the testrun's results:<br /> - Silencing the Beast within the area, leading to Kindred flocking to it more and more.<br /> - Infusing Vitae with Sekhem<br /> - Sending out a call for help to Reapers, who within that area treat Kindred as Ghosts<br /> - Sinking the area into the Underworld's Upper Reaches<br /> - Messing up the G-M's Infrastructure<br /> - Completing the G-M's Infrastructure<br /> - Open Avernian Gates at random<br /> - whatever else fun stuff you can come up with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T22:22:20-07:00","id":1339525,"title":"","content":"Deleted, because I'm a dumbass and meant to post in the VtM thread. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 10-05-2019, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T12:31:42-07:00","id":1340824,"title":"","content":"370) An elder Ventrue arrives in town. Long ago, he spun straw into gold for a mortal in exchange for her children, but she drove him off. In modern times, he has taken it upon himself to track down and acquire (be it ghoul or otherwise) every last living descendant she has. There are a few in the city, and either he needs help finding them, or he needs to take them from those in power. Worse, one of them might be a PC. As for what this elder does with his new servants, he only offers the occasional demand, and is otherwise kind, at least to those who obey without question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25692-joshua_lazarus","name":"Joshua_Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:25:48-07:00","id":1379595,"title":"","content":"371) An Elder or group of Elders have recently awoken in an unfamiliar world. They come from pre-galactic conquest Earth &amp; have woken to the Night Without End. Now they must find their feet in this new world, somehow without pissing off anyone too important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:26:46-07:00","id":1379596,"title":"","content":"372) The local Sheriff is a prominent member of the Invictus who has been preaching that them must adapt to survive.<br /> They have concluded that they need to acquire help for these two parts of their unlife (Sheriff &amp; Invictus) &amp; so have performed a pair of Embraces.<br /> One of a promising PI to act as deputy sheriff. One of someone who has a reputation taking random ideas &amp; adapting them to the situation.<br /> Along with the neonates of some of the Sheriff's allies these two new kindred scramble as they find their feet in this world they were pulled kicking &amp; screaming into (&amp; maybe become allied without each other).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:27:51-07:00","id":1379597,"title":"","content":"373) You &amp; your coterie comprise, if not the entire kindred population of this lovely, tropical island, then a fair chunk of it.<br /> You all have the same sire, who is currently in torpor somewhere around, &amp; thus are all of the same Clan. You're actually not really sure what the Clans are, &amp; none of the Covenants have any foothold here. You've developed your own society of sorts between yourselves, completely seperate from regular kindred society.<br /> And then, just after sundown, getting off a boat onto the island is a new vampire from a completely different Clan. You'd deluded yourselves into thinking there were no other vampires, they were unaware of any native kindred.<br /> Prepare for the cultural clash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:29:03-07:00","id":1379598,"title":"","content":"374) The Prince is dead, &amp; the battle to be the next Prince begins.<br /> Unfortunately it runs on for such a long time, attracting attention from multiple groups (mundanes, hunters, werewolves, mages, vampires from other domains, among many others), that local kindred society decide the potential Princes still in the running will jointly run things, or they'll be thrown out &amp; the city will start with fresh potential Princes.<br /> <br /> \u2022 You are encouraged to make the potential Princes as disparate a group as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:30:26-07:00","id":1379600,"title":"","content":"375) A spot of the Land of the Worms has suddenly appeared in the middle of the city. And it is growing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:31:49-07:00","id":1379601,"title":"","content":"376) The Lancea Sanctum have announced an astonishing revelation.<br /> The old, abandoned, rundown cathedral on the outskirts of town has an unusual mystical quality. Any kindred who sleeps the day away underneath it will be cured of the kindred curse &amp; return to humanity, with all the legal documentation they could possibly need right beside them when they wake up.<br /> How could the Lancea Sanctum possible know this, people ask. Well, it happened to the Bishop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:32:58-07:00","id":1379602,"title":"","content":"377) Just yesterday a local, well-known kindred died from sunlight, underground in a windowless room, in the dead of night. So, how exactly did this happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:34:05-07:00","id":1379604,"title":"","content":"378) A powerful Nosferatu never cut ties with their human relatives. Who just so happen to be a Mafia family.<br /> This Nosferatu now rules as consigliere &amp; is secretly planning to make a play for Prince.<br /> You have make managed to learn of their plans without them knowing. So how will you react to this? Will you ally with the Nosferatu, reveal their plans to the current Prince, or something else entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:35:20-07:00","id":1379605,"title":"","content":"379) You've discovered the truth behind VII, &amp; you can't wait to use this knowledge to make your names.<br /> And then, you encounter another member of VII, whose existence gives truth to a completely different rumour of the VII. And then, it happens again, &amp; again, &amp; again.<br /> What the Hell is going on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:36:45-07:00","id":1379606,"title":"","content":"380) There's a neonate kindred of a never before seen Clan in town. They are only a couple of weeks into their new unlife &amp; have just found other kindred.<br /> This new Clan causes colour to wash out of skin, hair, &amp; eyes, &amp; any of this Clan have muted emotions. They have the augmented Disciplines of Celerity &amp; Obfuscate, &amp; a Clan-specific Discipline that enables the manipulation of one's personal gravity.<br /> You have been chosen to explain just why this new kindred should join your Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:39:53-07:00","id":1379608,"title":"","content":"Alternative ideas that I've come up with for Clan-specific Disciplines to be used for the above plot are: <br /> Manipulation of light &amp; darkness.<br /> Telekinesis.<br /> Weather influencing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:42:15-07:00","id":1379609,"title":"","content":"381) You are one of the kindred living in Vatican City. You have to step carefully to avoid Malleus Maleficarum, because this is their headquarters, but you've gotten used to it &amp; it's just another part of night to night life for you.<br /> Of course, you are one of a handful of kindred in Vatican City that isn't Lancea Sanctum, something that is compared to sin by the Archbishop.<br /> Then your haven is found by Malleus Maleficarum while you are sleeping &amp; you are captured.<br /> You could break out &amp; seek refuge with other kindred while figuring who sold you out (because your captors let slip that they didn't just stumble onto you), or you could point fingers.<br /> There's probably no other way out of this mess. Unless you are really clever &amp; can find one...<br /> <br /> 382) You meet a ghoul &amp; learn that it's getting its vitae fixes by simply touching random kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:44:10-07:00","id":1379610,"title":"","content":"383) Blood is being found, completely devoid of any vitae. Meanwhile, the mundane society has found bloodless corpses &amp; started talking about a &quot;Vampire Murderer&quot;. Hunters are gathering, looking for the threat.<br /> The Circle of the Crone &amp; Lancea Sanctum seperately work blood magics &amp; both conclude that there is a blood bather (BB for short) in town.<br /> A &quot;blood hunt&quot; is declared against this BB, then a member of one of the groups hunting the BB turns up, claiming that the rest of his group is fully dead &amp; that this BB, isn't just a BB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:45:36-07:00","id":1379611,"title":"","content":"384) The Ordo Dracul &amp; Brides of Dracula have made a full alliance in the local city, sharing information, food supplies, territory, muscle, etc.<br /> They're not sure where they want to go beyond up.<br /> Are you a part of this alliance? Are you a servant of the Prince who says this alliance must end? Where do you sit in this scenario?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:47:01-07:00","id":1379612,"title":"","content":"385) You've come upon your mortal spawn to discover that they have joined a compact/conspiracy that specializes in hunting vampires (the Barrett Commission, the Cainite Heresy, Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, Night Watch, etc.).<br /> Nevertheless, you've given them your full support. No one said parenthood was easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:50:24-07:00","id":1379613,"title":"","content":"386) The *insert appropriate Covenant here* have made a miraculous discovery. A teenage kindred, who was never human.<br /> Yes, this young person was born a kindred, albeit with the ability to age &amp; mature.<br /> You have been sent to dig up this kid's history. Don't fail. And maybe watch out for the kid's family. Who knows what they're like, or what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:52:08-07:00","id":1379615,"title":"","content":"387) The new Prince has decided to &quot;return&quot; the All-Night Society to being ruled (completely dominated) by the alliance of the church (Lancea Sanctum) &amp; the state (Invictus). Anyone who doesn't fall in line will get crushed underfoot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:53:01-07:00","id":1379616,"title":"","content":"388) You're a nomadic kindred or a group of nomadic kindred. You make a point to personally say hello to the local Prince every time you enter a domain.<br /> This time you stand before the local Prince &amp; are shocked to see that they are not kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:54:05-07:00","id":1379617,"title":"","content":"389) Well, they did it. The Commonwealth of Carthage (a faction of the Carthian Movement) have blown the Masquerade wide open.<br /> Because of past actions, the local kindred have elected you to be one of the &quot;human liaisons&quot; that will be needed now. But first, let's get rid of the bloody Commonwealth of Carthage!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:54:52-07:00","id":1379619,"title":"","content":"390) You're being haunted, by yourself! You are dead after all. It's kinda disturbing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:55:22-07:00","id":1379620,"title":"","content":"391) A really old kindred has gone nutzoid. They've become possessed by the belief that they are Santa Claus. Never mind that it's the wrong season, &quot;Santa&quot; means to deliver &quot;presents&quot; &amp; &quot;lumps of coal&quot; to every child in the city. This needs to be stopped yesterday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:56:14-07:00","id":1379621,"title":"","content":"392) You &amp; four others all wake up in a windowless room. You quickly discover that you are now vampires.<br /> In the middle of the room is a stack of papers. On the top of the stack is a letter that says: <br /> &quot;Good morning, or evening, or whatever. Welcome to the start of your lives as kindred. In your clothes are secreted papers information about your new Clan. Hint: You're all of different Clans.<br /> In this stack of paperwork you will find basic information about all the Covenants in the city (there is a fair greater number than the norm.). Allies of mine will ensure your joining whichever Covenant you want will be relatively easy. Though I insist that one of you joins Invictus, for prosperity's sake. You can use the above building as a Haven. Oh, &amp; basic terminology &amp; rules of kindred society are also detailed in this stack of papers somewhere. I look forward to seeing what you will do.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:57:41-07:00","id":1379622,"title":"","content":"393) An Uratha has successfully &amp; unwillingly been Embraced. And they've still got everything that makes them Uratha. What to do about this? What do the wolves think about the situation? And who performed the Embrace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:58:17-07:00","id":1379623,"title":"","content":"394) A legendary kindred called the Morrigan approaches you &amp; claims to be your sire. Despite the fact that you're of different Clans.<br /> Oh, &amp; the Morrigan has multiple personality disorder, three very different ones to be exact, &amp; you have no idea which one is speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:58:56-07:00","id":1379624,"title":"","content":"395) Someone has noticed the/an urbiphage in the sky of the city.<br /> The city's population needs to drop yesterday, or at least before its too late.<br /> And just if there are souls (that is any kindred) that don't understand what this means, the Circle of the Crone has claimed that the city's destruction is coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T21:59:35-07:00","id":1379625,"title":"","content":"396) A powerful land developer has managed to buy a chunk of rundown land &amp; has plans to renovate it, turning it into a lovely little gentrified neighborhood.<br /> Why should you care? Well, that chunk of land? That's where the local Nosferatu have their Necropolis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:00:11-07:00","id":1379626,"title":"","content":"397) Your rival ghouled a beloved relative of yours. They didn't do this on purpose, but once they find out the connection you can be sure they will take advantage of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:00:51-07:00","id":1379627,"title":"","content":"398) A neonate woke up last night, completely immune to fire. And no fire frenzy either. Of course, they're taking advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:01:50-07:00","id":1379628,"title":"","content":"399) A Circle of the Crone ritual resulted in a human victim. Afterwards the human corpse got up. Turns out they've become a kindred. That wasn't in the plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:02:25-07:00","id":1379629,"title":"","content":"400) A mundane friend has picked up one of the Sutina, the grave goods. You're horrified by this. You manage to discretely get rid of the grave good without your friend knowing.<br /> And then they pick up another grave good, which you get rid off as well. And again. And again. And again.<br /> You can't keep doing this. You need to find a permanent solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:04:25-07:00","id":1379630,"title":"","content":"401) A kindred entered Elysium tonight claiming to been a draugr just a handful of nights ago.<br /> There's no proof that they're lying. There's no proof that they're telling the truth. And everyone has a different opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:05:05-07:00","id":1379631,"title":"","content":"402) Lancea Sanctum has started singing a new song. Although they identify with the Christian faith, they don't really care too much what the humans believe, or at least they don't enforce it.<br /> Now nearly every member of Lancea Sanctum in the country has declared that the humans will convert to the true faith &amp; be good, honest Christians, or else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:05:40-07:00","id":1379632,"title":"","content":"403) There's this one domain where, several years ago, it became illegal on pain of final death to be a member of a certain Covenant (Carthian Movement, Circle of the Crone, Invictus, Lancea Sanctum, Ordo Dracul, some other Covenant).<br /> Despite the Prince changing multiple times since this law was made, the law yet stands.<br /> You are a member of the banned Covenant &amp; have been chosen to enter this domain, get the law overturned, &amp; reintegrate the Covenant into local night-to-night society.<br /> Shouldn't be too hard, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:06:35-07:00","id":1379633,"title":"","content":"404) Circle of the Crone blood magic is Corrupting, Wild, Pagan.<br /> Lancea Sanctum blood magic is Judgemental, Holy, Deliberate.<br /> There is a new Covenant wielding blood magic. The thirteen initial members of the Lords of Night preach to become more than humans, more than vampires, more than the divine powers that made them.<br /> The blood magic of the Lords of Night is Profane, Territorial, Industrious.<br /> Will you join &amp; learn this new blood magic, or will you fight against the new Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:07:15-07:00","id":1379634,"title":"","content":"405) A Gangrel managed to &quot;inflict&quot; some kind of warped Protean effect on a Daeva, which isn't wearing off.<br /> The Daeva is currently figuring out how to make this semi-serpentine look work, while you are commanded to hunt the Gangrel down &amp; get this reversed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:08:43-07:00","id":1379635,"title":"","content":"406) Roughly twelve different kindred have appeared in the city at the same time, all claiming to be the one &amp; only Dracula.<br /> They all feel sufficiently old enough &amp; each has an appropriate level of knowledge of the Coils (though one is more supportive of that biker gang the Brides of Dracula than the Ordo Dracul).<br /> They all claiming they are the real one &amp; that the others are fakes.<br /> Congratulations, you've been &quot;volunteered&quot; to navigate this mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:09:34-07:00","id":1379636,"title":"","content":"407) You've been Embraced. Welcome to the rest of the your life.<br /> Oh, &amp; you've got a weird condition that means that you can only get sustenance from others of the same blood type. And of course your blood type is that one that's like only 8% of the population. At least you're not also a germaphobe like a vampire in London you've started hearing about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:45:10-07:00","id":1380447,"title":"","content":"408) Time travel, turns out it\u2019s possible and recently happened in your city since a down on his luck nonate you encountered has just gained about one hundred years of blood potency, mastery of many disciplines and the sort of money that comes from knowing to invest in Apple, Microsoft and Amazon early. Remind me, how did you treat him when you met?<br /> <br /> 409) the Mekhet you just helped out of a messy situation believed herself to be a genuine seer, ask one yes/no question about the city and she will look for potents and tell you what she learns.<br /> <br /> 410) Someone\u2019s done something nice for their ghoul, after teaching her the basics of the Gangrel disciplines (plus maybe a bloodline discipline of the Storytellers choice) he got her embraced into the Khaibit. Her new territory is almost right next to yours. Oh yeah I forget to say, she was a monster hunting bad ass before they met and he\u2019s connected, hope you get on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":".  Spelling 04-11-2020, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T17:53:25-07:00","id":1380525,"title":"","content":"411)A Nosferatu Dragon has stumbled across an alchemical method for severing the Beast from a vampire, embodying it in some small, horrid form, and set it loose to do one's bidding.<br /> <br /> The problem is, upon remerging, the vampire undergo strange mutations, as the Beast, unfiltered by the vampiric need for vitae, slakes its hunger in some other way. The vampire in question might become insectile or grow a face on the back of their head or even develop silver claws.<br /> <br /> But the Beast, having tasted freedom, wants out again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T16:16:05-07:00","id":1380785,"title":"","content":"412) The regent of one of the cities ethnic neighbourhoods has pissed off the prince and a contest has begun. You are one of the lucky groups who get to try to take her territory from her, succeed and it\u2019s yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T20:05:06-07:00","id":1380836,"title":"","content":"413) Flood.<br /> It was raining last night and obviously it rained most of the day because the water level is about a foot above the pavement and rising. The subways are closed and any havens below the water level have probably begun to flood, forecast is for at least 3 more days of rain. Also there is a tidal wave heading your way, the foods leaving tomorrow, good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:22:59-07:00","id":1381179,"title":"","content":"414)Against all the odds and helped along by strange Lupine shamans, a vampire has been gestating a &quot;baby&quot; of Athena's Blessing for over a hundred-some years. His body is swollen and grotesque, his &quot;baby&quot; having subsumed over 70% of his body, the Ordo Dracul went out of tneir way to study him and protect him.,,and, out of the blue, he just DISAPPEARS,<br /> <br /> The Dragons move heaven and earth and eventually track him down...or what's LEFT of him, he met Final Death by having EXPLODED, as if he'd swallowed a grenade! His insides were completely hollowed out, with signs of them having been CONSUMED FROM WITHIN.<br /> <br /> The first of Athena's monstrous progeny have been born, and now the hunt is on to track it down and control it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T03:53:35-07:00","id":1381884,"title":"","content":"415) Ordo Dracul experiments have resulted in a vampire that won't do what vampires do upon Final Death, disintegrate.<br /> Now mundane authorities have gotten a hold of the corpse in question &amp; are asking themselves &quot;what's up with this corpse?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T08:43:40-07:00","id":1381928,"title":"","content":"416)One day, [Fill-In-The-Blank] was a stereotypical city, run by an Invictus prince and supported by the Lancea et Sanctum, with Carthians as loyal opposition.<br /> <br /> Then..,silence. In fact, no one remembers the city even existing---save for the players' characters, who have their sires dwelling in the now vanished metropolis. It is clear only those sired by vampires of the missing city even remember such s place existed at ALL. Mortals no longer recall it, it's influences on history have been shifted to other locales, even Wikipedia is blank on the topic.<br /> <br /> What the hell is going on, here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T11:51:34-07:00","id":1381954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1381928#post1381928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">416)One day, [Fill-In-The-Blank] was a stereotypical city, run by an Invictus prince and supported by the Lancea et Sanctum, with Carthians as loyal opposition.<br /> <br /> Then..,silence. In fact, no one remembers the city even existing---save for the players' characters, who have their sires dwelling in the now vanished metropolis. It is clear only those sired by vampires of the missing city even remember such s place existed at ALL. Mortals no longer recall it, it's influences on history have been shifted to other locales, even Wikipedia is blank on the topic.<br /> <br /> What the hell is going on, here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Germelshausen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T17:57:53-07:00","id":1382022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1381954#post1381954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Germelshausen</div> </div> </div> </div>...I actually had to look this up. I like what Wilipedia told me. Maybe I can work elements of that story in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T00:50:00-07:00","id":1382084,"title":"","content":"417) You're a revenant who's down on their luck and nowhere near gutsy enough to try and wrestle a fully Kindred vampire for their soul to improve your lot. A shady vagrant led you to a dead-eyed herd of mortals and made an offer: consume one of the bottled vampire souls she's brought, and she'll have you sitting pretty before the year is done. All she wants in return is to observe \u2014 she mentioned something about a fallen tower, but honestly, you were too hungry to give that your full attention.<br /> <br /> What can it hurt? Your Beast needs better teeth, and anything's better than being stuck at the bottom of the barrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T20:08:04-07:00","id":1382884,"title":"","content":"418. You're a group of Dammitics(Jewish Sanctified) who's looking for an amulet that perished in the ashes of your community. Being &quot;home&quot; is strange as you get acclimated to how the kine may have moved past the injustices committed against your people, the dead have not forgotten. Strange occurrences happen as you attempt to find this lost heirloom and eventually a dybbuk makes itself known to you, asking for assistance undoing the injustices done to the community.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24708-spectre9924","name":"Spectre9924","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T19:04:52-07:00","id":1383267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1379600#post1379600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">375) A spot of the Land of the Worms has suddenly appeared in the middle of the city. And it is growing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wasn't there a reference to the Land of Worms in Banishers or some other MtAw book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T19:52:45-07:00","id":1383276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1383267#post1383267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wasn't there a reference to the Land of Worms in Banishers or some other MtAw book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the information on the Land of the Worms can be found in either Ancient Bloodlines or Ancient Mysteries. That's where my memory says I found it. Pretty sure it isn't mentioned in any MtAw book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T20:12:57-07:00","id":1383279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1383267#post1383267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a reference to the Land of Worms in Banishers or some other MtAw book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Summoners's section on Numbers Stations discusses the Helminth, massive all-consuming worms served by cryptic ghosts from an Underworld beneath all else, which Ancient Mysteries's section on the Land of Worms mentions in its Theories in the context of the cipher-riddled journal of the Nosferatu Victor Blackcloud, who disappeared within the Land and seems to have come to believe that the Land is a sort of staging ground for the apocalyptic emergence of the Helminth and that he himself was infested with worms through his tie to the land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T21:11:02-07:00","id":1383284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1383276#post1383276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the information on the Land of the Worms can be found in either Ancient Bloodlines or Ancient Mysteries. That's where my memory says I found it. Pretty sure it isn't mentioned in any MtAw book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My point was that the Land of Worms was <b>also </b>referenced by a Mtaw book. That wasn't not quite right, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks/page29\">Satchel </a>correctly remembered the crossover links that i forgot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T17:30:30-07:00","id":1383476,"title":"","content":"419. The Sangovani are coming, their mortal family have already acquired a large residential building and a club and a request has been sent to the Prince to allow their members to enter the city. This is going to shift a lot of kindred territory and your feeding grounds are likely to be contested in the shake up and the backlash won\u2019t stop there.<br /> 420. Power cut. The city\u2019s lost power possibly due to the Nosferatu possibly not but attention is on the problem and related issues. Mortals are more careful but the environment favours kindred and ruthless feeders are at a short term advantage but it can\u2019t last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:35:20-07:00","id":1383576,"title":"","content":"421) You know that vampire hunting group that started out as a sorority? Well, some idiot decided that it would make for a great joke to drag one of them into vampiredom (I'm serious, it was done as a joke).<br /> Now they've got detailed information about half the kindred in the city &amp; are planning an attack upon one of the Elysiums. Which one, you ask, I'm afraid we don't know that part.<br /> \u25cf Uses Maiden's Blood Sisterhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:36:08-07:00","id":1383577,"title":"","content":"422) You've decided to go into the illegal drug trade. It looks like an easy way to amass power.<br /> You start up your new &quot;business&quot; &amp; go to sleep for the day.<br /> When you wake up the next night, you are shocked to discover that your new &quot;business&quot; has been routed before it even really begun. Apparently the local drug dealers don't like to share with &quot;leeches&quot;.<br /> How exactly did they know it was vampire run?<br /> \u25cf Uses Night Watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:36:49-07:00","id":1383578,"title":"","content":"423) You come from politics, so when your really scary sire ordered you to establish a base of power for yourself, it made sense to return to those halls.<br /> Imagine your surprise when you met people that know of vamps &amp; don't like them in the halls of politics. <br /> You can't back out now, your life or unlife may potential be in imminent danger. Maybe you can forge an alliance &amp; share power &amp; resources. Yes, that might work.<br /> \u25cf Uses the Barrett Commission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:41:20-07:00","id":1383581,"title":"","content":"424) A high-ranked kindred got attacked by a cell of hunters that used, what are suspected of being Disciplines.<br /> Most of the All-Night Society find this very unsettling, but the Ordo Dracul are pointing at this as being proof of their practices.<br /> \u25cf Uses the Followers of the Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:42:04-07:00","id":1383582,"title":"","content":"425) You were hungry &amp; snacked on a nearby, available blood doll. Now you've become Emboldened, disturbing your allies.<br /> Intellectually, you know that the blood doll is to blame for this sudden, unusual attitude, but they've disappeared &amp; so cannot be questioned.<br /> And then you learn that you are not the only one who has had this sort of problem, &amp; it's getting more common.<br /> Maybe we should retire the blood dolls, cause that looks like the only way we're going to get out of this mess.<br /> (If the Emboldened Condition doesn't fit for some reason, switch it out for any other Condition that does.)<br /> \u25cf Uses Schrlach Spinnwebe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T01:05:18-07:00","id":1384123,"title":"","content":"426) You discover that a vampire you know unwittingly tried to feed on a werewolf and managed to drain nearly all of that creatures blood before it killed him and ate his heart. This somehow, against all reason, seems to have resulted in a Vampiric Werewolf that is hell bent on revenge against all Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:45:07-07:00","id":1386194,"title":"","content":"427) Wake up. Go to school. Hang with friends. Come home &amp; make a sacrifice to the Crone. You &amp; your friends are dhampirs raised in the shadow of the Circle of the Crone, despite what some people may think it's all very mundane &amp; ordinary most of the time.<br /> Then one evening the local Hierophant declares that there is a terrible threat coming to wipe out the city's kindred, &amp; that only dhampirs can stand against it.<br /> \u25cf Change the Covenant if needed for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:45:46-07:00","id":1386195,"title":"","content":"428) The first law that the Prince decreed in their reign was &quot;no dhampirs&quot;. If you are a dhampir, you will be put to the death. If you make a dhampir you will be punished, then put to the death.<br /> One night you see the Prince meeting with a living human. The human is heavily pregnant. It looks like the Prince has broken their first law, now how can you take advantage of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:48:04-07:00","id":1387230,"title":"","content":"429) The ultraconservative Archbishop declares his/her/their intent to make humans obey the rules of the Church as he/she/they sees them (no premarital sex, no gay sex, no &quot;devil worship&quot;, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T20:32:12-07:00","id":1387882,"title":"","content":"430) A Gangrel hungers for more challenging prey.<br /> A new arts company flourishing in town started by a young, brilliant actor who catches the eye of a Daeva.<br /> A Mekhet overhears an assassination plot &amp; is presented with the conundrum if they should act.<br /> A Nosferatu driven of their court desires vicious revenge on each Kindred who abandoned them.<br /> A young Ventrue determined to rise up &amp; take control of their whole court within a year.<br /> These five Kindred find in each other allies in solving their individual problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T20:37:39-07:00","id":1387884,"title":"","content":"431) When you arrive at Elysium there is a creature waiting for... you? The Prince? Some other Kindred?<br /> In any case, it's presence sets your Beast on edge like you have never felt before, despite the creature clearly not being Kindred itself.<br /> A nearby member of the Circle of the Crone names it as being an Igigi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T11:53:52-07:00","id":1388378,"title":"","content":"432. A coterie of young kindred have taken to soliciting online solutions to the mysteries of their requiem posting short stories or questioning RPG communities. The problem is these people are willing to go deep and now have deduced the real city inspiring these scenarios, it\u2019s only a matter of time before this moderately well connected group of difficult to identify individuals makes one connection too many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T03:12:55-07:00","id":1389608,"title":"","content":"433. Your mentor/sire/anyone else you\u2019re inclined to help or suck up to wants something, let\u2019s say a sword that will be arriving at a local museum in 2 days and staying there for a week. You\u2019ve seen a heist movie right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T19:26:44-07:00","id":1399467,"title":"","content":"434.<b>Parasite</b><br /> The city of [Fill-In-The-Blank] has a picture-perfect Domain: an elder prince, relatively non-contentious primogen and Elysians that are truly respected.<br /> <br /> What no one knows, of course, is that the prince was killed by hunters, and something...else...wears his skin. Something old and hungry and clever dragged itself out of the wet earth, and it has a dire agenda.<br /> <br /> It is not a vampire. It is not some other form of supernatural from any of the other splats. It is something unique, a one-of-a-kind abomination that feeds on vampires. It can wear the skins of its victims, and the longer it is awake, the greater its hunger grows.<br /> <br /> It has made contact with Belial's Brood. It's plans for the city's Kindred is a blood-soaked, cannibal apocalypse..,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 06-27-2020, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T18:14:03-07:00","id":1400223,"title":"","content":"435.<b>The Great Bear</b><br /> A Native American Nosferatu elder, warped and twisted to appear as s gargantuan tardigrade, has emerged from a torpor of over a thousand years. Rendered weak by his long torpor, this Great Bear is lost in a world that makes no sense, where everything he knew as sacrosanct is upended into ruination.<br /> <br /> Unable to find a Touchstone, confused and terrified, the Great Bear's Humanity slowly slips away to nothingness.<br /> <br /> But this is not the end of him. His sentience does not fade. Belial's Brood finds him, and now he hunts the despoilers of everything he has ever known!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T07:07:35-08:00","id":1423262,"title":"","content":"436. A prestigious local fashion show, hosted by the fashion design department of a prestigious local art college, is actually the cover story for a ghoul auction, kindred from around the region are arriving in the city to bid on ghouls from the most prestigious ghoul families. Your coterie has been assigned various jobs relating to the auction and fashion show. The assignments are easy jobs, bartending, hairdressing , Security that sort of thing, but there is the small matter of the assassin sent to eliminate some of the more controversial kindred guests, though the prince is certain you can handle that, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T06:38:26-07:00","id":1440940,"title":"","content":"437. One of the domain's most powerful elders has a tweenage dhampir child that the elder dotes on excessively. Said child has recently gotten into slot car racing, the latest trading card game, war gaming minis or some other such Hobby that is competitive and requires spending a lot of money. Since every lick in the domain wants to impress the elder they get into this hobby too. Cue a Kindred black market in the collectable in question, as well as a lot of cheating at the local tournaments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 03-22-2021, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:35:12-07:00","id":1466066,"title":"","content":"438: A golden apple appears in the middle of Elysium. &quot;To The Strongest&quot; can be found written on its side. A number of powerful kindred make moves to claim it (&amp; the associated status) as theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T11:14:21-07:00","id":1466497,"title":"","content":"439: A couple centuries ago one of the local elders wrote a series of letters to another elder and never sent them. Those letters are soon to be on display in a local museum, along with several other artifacts of the period and the elder who wrote them needs them recovered before their would-be recipient can see them. Which would potentially have unwanted effects on the current political situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","e